{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20","id":1511445,"title":"Sphere Oddities in M20","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-12T06:14:42-07:00","id":1511445,"title":"Sphere Oddities in M20","content":"I'm going through the M20 example charts and Sphere writeups to see where they call for Conjunctional Effects and I keep finding oddities that sound good but don't actually make sense when you dig into them. A lot of them actually. I give HDYDT a lot of crap for being all over the place rules-wise, but M20 itself is a mess of contradictions, arbitrary extra spheres, rules that were assumed but never actually stated, and examples that make less than no sense.<br /> <br /> Here's some of what I've found:<br /> <br /> <b>Correspondence</b><br /> <br /> There's no real examples of Conjunctional Effects for Correspondence 1, but for Rank 2 we start off with Clairvoyance. This is listed in the Common Magical Effects chart. It's a simple Correspondence 2 spell... except for Psychics for whom it is Corr 2/Mind 3. Mind is not doing anything in this spell except raising difficulty (because the highest sphere is now rank 3 instead of 2) and providing an extra method of countermagic. Not only that, but it means psychics have to have Correspondence 3 to cast the spell because a Mage's rank in Correspondence caps the max level of another sphere that he can bring to bear in a Correspondence spell. The spell remains Correspondence 2, but he can't cast it unless he has Correspondence 3.<br /> <br /> Next up, the Common Magical Effects Chart lists Corr 2/Prime 2/Other Sphere 2+ for Warding or Banning. Meanwhile the Correspondence writeup calls for Corr 4/Other Sphere 2+. Correspondence 4 is clearly the level for Wards and Bans, so I think that's the correct one. I have no idea what Prime would even do in this context.<br /> <br /> Then there's the Summon Small Objects or Creatures at Corr 2/Matter 2 and Corr 2/Life 2. This appears to be an example of Spheres being wrongly added for targeting purposes when <i>that's not a rule</i>. Correspondence alone is explicitly enough to teleport small objects.<br /> <br /> Next up we have levitation/flight. Despite the sheer nonsense that is HDYDT's levitation section the Common Effects Chart is quite simple. Correspondence 3 (or Forces 2) to levitate things, Life or Matter as locking spheres. The only real problem here is that nowhere in the Correspondence writeup does it say that the Sphere is capable of this. The idea of Correspondence based flight has been in Mage for a decades, though, so I'm guessing this was an oversight.<br /> <br /> However, then the Sphere writeup says: &quot;Also, by combining Correspondence 3 with Forces, Life, or Matter, the mage can move things around from a distance, levitating, manipulating or teleporting them without physical contact.&quot; That's cool, but levitation at a distance, manipulation at a distance, and teleportation at a distance are several very different effects. The recommendation works for remote levitation and remote manipulation since the first is the same spell as above (with a range augment that's already covered) and the second is a Forces, Life, and/or Matter spell with a range augment. On the other hand remote teleportation and just physically picking up and moving objects from a distance are merely Correspondence 2 on its own, no other spheres required.<br /> <br /> Create Multiple Images is listed as a mere Correspondence 3 effect, which makes sense, but Create Multiple Objects is listed as Corr 5/Matter 3/Prime 2. I can only think this was supposed to be Correspondence 5 OR Matter 3/Prime 2.<br /> <br /> Conjure Earthly Being is stated to be Corr 4/Life 2. The only possible reason for Life 2 is for targeting, which is unnecessary.<br /> <br /> Colocation is an interesting one. Correspondence 4 is enough to accomplish it, but you need Mind 1 to function effectively and Life 2 to be able to act independently at each location. This is an odd one because Life is either completely unnecessary or it is too low. Either we automatically treat every body like it is different and Mind is enough, or we need some special augmentation to make every body functionally different and Life 2 is too low for that.<br /> <br /> Just to muddy the waters a little more, Colocate Senses is described as Correspondence 5 / Life 3. But Colocate senses is already available at Correspondence 3 and doesn't need Life 3.<br /> <br /> I'll end on a piece of sanity. The Correspondence 5 writeup says that Corr 5 can be combined with the appropriate sphere at 2+ to stretch or compress objects, bodies, or forces. If we are charitable and assume it is a spacial distortion locked to a pattern, that would mostly track.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's 3 examples of arbitrary sphere additions (one practice based), 2-3 examples of unnecessary targeting spheres, and 3 spheres included at the wrong rank. Only 6 of the 15 examples I looked at made sense completely.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 05-15-2023, 09:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T08:20:19-07:00","id":1511451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20#post1511445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This appears to be an example of Spheres being wrongly added for targeting purposes when <i>that's not a rule</i>. Correspondence alone is explicitly enough to teleport small objects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've checked, because I was sure that I read similar requirements in older editions. In several books, in fact. Like <i>Blood Treachery</i> that requires Corr2/Forces 2 to get a ray of sunligth, or Cruzade that also used Corr 4/ Life 2 to &quot;Conjure Earthly Being&quot;<br /> <br /> So, I went to Revised Core, and <b>it seems this is a rule in Revised</b> (not sure about previous editions). It's very clearly stated on the Sphere of Correspondence (and on the examples too) that you need an appropiate Pattern Sphere to affect distant objects (including conjuring them). It doesn't seem required to teleport<i> the mage</i> with Corr 3, nor to &quot;touch&quot; things at distance with Corr 2, nor to open portals, but to conjure specific distant thing with magick, then yeah, a Pattern sphere at the &quot;appropiate level&quot; (whatever that means) it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-12-2023, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T09:16:58-07:00","id":1511455,"title":"","content":"Well in M20 the beginning of the Correspondence section says that you need pattern spheres if you are taking only part of a pattern. Teleporting someone's head off would require Life but teleporting the gun out of someone's hand would not require Matter. The section on Correspondence 2 contradicts this so one of the two sections must be wrong. Since the main section has specifics and reasons I err on the side of that being correct.<br /> <br /> In revised is it a stated rule that Life is harder to affect than Matter? That's another thing that is inconsistently tacked onto sphere costs without any real explanation. It's not in M20 except in the implicit assumptions of the author, as far as I can tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T11:17:41-07:00","id":1511463,"title":"","content":"Well...<br /> <br /> In the Corr 2 example Rote to teleport small stuff it's stated that you need Life to teleport living beings, just like in the Sphere, also that you need to have Correspondence at the same <i>level of complexity</i> of the thing you want to teleport<br /> <br /> Then Life 3 <i>suggests,</i> among it's conjunctional uses, to move arround simple lifeforms combined with Correspondence - so, it's comparing teleportation with a <i>transmutation of simple lifeforms</i> rather than an <i>alteration of simple lifeforms</i>.<br /> <br /> That would imply that Corr 2, practically speaking, it's not enough to teleport small living beings. Altrough the effect<i> it's</i> of Corr 2, the odd take Life has about it forces you to have 3.<br /> <br /> So...It's not really &quot;stated&quot; to be the case, as much as the consequence of a, perhaps questionable, stance the Life Sphere takes about this. But, <i>it</i> <i>is</i> <i>there</i>, if one looks very carefully. I wouldn't have noticed if wasn't looking for it.<br /> <br /> That's Revised's take ... does this sound like how M20's odd examples are handled?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-12-2023, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T11:50:46-07:00","id":1511465,"title":"","content":"This is more direct and goes beyond Correspondence. In quite a few places spells require Life when cast on living creatures, I've found a few examples in M20 so far. The Awakening Substances sidebar, for instance, shows that awakening a drug is just Spirit, but awakening a disease inside someone is Spirit and Life. Prime implies that consecrating inanimate things is just Prime while consecrating living things is Prime and Life.<br /> <br /> Here's the next round of issues I found:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Entropy</b><br /> <br /> Entropy, oddly enough, is fairly light. All three examples are in the Common Effects Chart.<br /> <br /> Bless/Curse can be done with Entropy 3/Life 3 (among other things). If this is a locked effect it should be Life 2, but its not even clear this needs a locking sphere.<br /> <br /> The Entropic version of Harm Ghost is an odd duck at Entropy 3/Prime 2. While Entropy is the sphere for tapping into the low umbra no rank is ever given for when it can do this. Normally, though, Entropy can't be used to attack until Rank 4. Meanwhile, Prime 2 can use Quintessence to hurt Spirits already and it doesn't need Spirit to do so, so there's no particular reason it would need Entropy to harm ghosts. Especially as there's a Spirit 3 version of Harm Ghost.<br /> <br /> Finally, I initially thought Disintigrate Object should be either Entropy 3 or Time 3, but this is a case where the combo makes sense. Entropy 3 only speeds the decay, Time 3 only ages the target. The two together should allow disintigration with fewer successes than Time 3 alone.<br /> <br /> Final tally: 3 effects, 1 arbitrary extra sphere, 1 unneeded targeting sphere.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Forces</b><br /> <br /> There aren't many I find objectionable here. Invisibility and Levitation are simple Forces Manipulation Effects locked to a target (Forces 2/Locking Sphere 2) and making things attract or repel can be accomplished the same way (though if you actually wanted to graft the forces to a target that would be Forces 3/Life 3).<br /> <br /> The classic Transforming another pattern into Forces is here, as is using Forces 3+/Prime 2 to manifest energy out of the ether. Transforming Thoughts or Spirit to Energy is are here as Forces 3 and either Mind or Spirit 3. This too works well as Mind and Spirit are actually doing something.<br /> <br /> It can't last forever, though.<br /> <br /> Conjure Physical Illusion suggests Forces 2+/Prime 2 and its not really clear what is happening here. Is this a Body of Light backed up by Forces? There's not a lot of information on Body of Light, so maybe? On the other hand Forces 2 is enough to manipulate Light, Sound, and Momentum on its own. It's not that this is wrong, its just that it isn't helpful to understanding spheres.<br /> <br /> Then there is Erode or Enhance Energies at Forces 3 and some level of Entropy. Forces 2 would probably be enough to reduce or enhance energies on their own. The Forces 3 in a Forces 3/Prime 2 fireball spell weaves the raw quintessence into a Fire pattern, so Forces 3 alone would be enough to convert a Forces pattern back into raw quintessence. You wouldn't need another sphere to just let it disperse though its probably really vulgar if you do. Perhaps Entropy is helping dissipate those raw forces seamlessly, but if so it is only needed for erosion.<br /> <br /> Finally there's the very strange Set Triggers for Energy Fluctuations. The problem here is that it is not at all clear what Energy Fluctuations are in this context. We can guess, but as an example it is not good at showing us what Forces 3 can do. Triggers at Time 4, at least, makes sense.<br /> <br /> Final Tally: 12 effects. 0-1 arbitrary sphere additions. 4 confusing effects.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 05-15-2023, 09:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T04:49:16-07:00","id":1511710,"title":"","content":"This time up, here's what I see in Life and Matter<br /> <br /> <b>Life... uh... finds a way... to be completely baffling</b><br /> <br /> First there's the near nonsensical Sense combinations. Sense Distant Organisms (Life 1/Corr 2) is the only one that makes sense as it is a sense spell at augmented range. Perceive a Creature Forward or Backwards in time is listed as Life 1/Time 2, but that's supposed to be a locked effect (the terminology in Time 2 is very similar to the terminology in the Locking section) so it should be Time 2/Life 2 (I reversed the order because it is easier to put locking spheres at the end). The suggestions of Life 1/Entropy 1 to see potential sickness/misfortune or Life 1/Prime 1 to see binding quintessence streams is completely off. Entropy and Prime can accomplish those tasks on their own.<br /> <br /> Create Simple Body is listed as Life 2/Prime 2 in the chart while the Life writeup makes it clear that should be Life 3/Prime 2.<br /> <br /> The Chart also gives a trifecta of spells to harm supernatural creatures. Heal/Harm Fae at Life 3/Mind 3. Heal/Harm Vampires at Life 3/Matter 2. Heal/Harm Werecreature at Life 3/Spirit 2. M20 makes it clear it takes more than Life to harm the major splats so the extra spheres are fine, but I don't understand the logic of the Ranks required. Either Mind is too high or Matter and Spirit are too low.<br /> <br /> At the very least the spells to create bodies listed in the Life writeup are consistent with the rules. Life 3 or 5/Prime 2 and transform bodies Life 3 or 5/Appropriate Sphere.<br /> <br /> De-ageing, though, is another case of surplus requirements. The two options are Life 5/Entropy 4 and Life 5/Time 3. Life 5 should be more than enough to de-age anything living. Entropy 4 should be enough as well. Time 3 could, though the target just be rewound so I could see using Life 3 for memory retention.<br /> <br /> Finally we come to the quagmire that is Reviving the Dead (Life 4/Spirit 4/Prime 3), Giving a Body Consciousness (Life 5/Mind 5), and Binding a Spirit into a body (Life 5/Spirit 5). It's not really clear what each sphere is doing here. Unlike many other cases where I say that, it is clear they are doing [/i]something[/i] it's just not clear what.<br /> <br /> Suppose we say that this is grafting effect. That involves transmuting two pattern types, so grafting a mind to a body would be Life 5/Mind 5. Except moving a Mind to another body (from the Mind writeup) is Mind 5/Life 4. That's either wrong or this isn't a graft. Meanwhile, Spirit 5 is explicitly enough to instill a soul within an empty shell, no Life needed at all. And don't even get me started on the Prime requirement for Reviving the Dead. Some of these are wrong, but its difficult to figure out which ones.<br /> <br /> Final Tally: 17 effects examined. 2 arbitrary extra spheres, 3-4 spheres at the wrong level. 2 accidentally merged spells. Three... somethings.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>After the mess that is Life, Matter has much better structure.</b><br /> <br /> Of the 13 effects I looked at, 8 were transforming matter into something or something into matter, and only 4 of those have any issues at all:<br /> <br /> Converting quintessence to matter at Matter 2/Prime 2 works, but the reverse should either be Matter 2 if you don\u2019t care where the released quintessence goes, or Matter 2/Prime 3 if the Mage is pulling it into his own pool. Matter 2/Prime 2 could effectively channel the released quintessence back into the ether, so this one isn't wrong, it just isn't explaining things well.<br /> <br /> Converting Matter to Living Tissue is stated as Matter 2+/Life 4+. That should be Matter 2+/Life 3+.<br /> <br /> Converting a car to a robot is listed as a Matter 4/Forces ?/Prime ?. Forces is a judgement call and depends a great deal on what\u2019s going on inside the car and the robot. Prime is completely unnecessary.<br /> <br /> If I\u2019m being pedantic, Transforming Matter is listed as Matter 3/Other Sphere 3+ but should actually start at Matter 2 for simple matter. Matter 3+/Other Sphere 3+ is the right spell for anything more complex than a brick.<br /> <br /> As for the other effects, Matter 2 says you can \u201cmove an object through space\u201d with Matter 2/Corr 2+, and \u201cmove an object through time\u201d with Matter. We already know from the Correspondence writeup that Matter is completely unnecessary to teleporting or moving an object around in space, there\u2019s no indication it is any more necessary for doing the same in Time. These are purely Correspondence and Time effects.<br /> <br /> Awakening the Spirit in an Object is listed in the Matter writeup as Matter 2/Spirit 3. Spirit alone should be enough to target a spirit so Matter is unnecessary even as a locking sphere. Most likely this is another example of unnecessary targeting. Indeed we can see in other locations in M20 that awakening the spirit in an object is just Spirit 3.<br /> <br /> Finally there is the delightful ability to melt steel with a thought as a Matter 5/Mind 3 spell. Matter 3 is enough to alter states of matter and Mind is doing nothing at all.<br /> <br /> Final tally: 13 effects examined. 1-2 arbitrary Sphere addition. 3 unnecessary targeting spheres. 3 effects with the wrong sphere rank listed. 5 of the 13 effects have no problems<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 05-15-2023, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T11:21:12-07:00","id":1511730,"title":"","content":"Big fan of this stepwise approach to dissecting the spheres!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T12:37:33-07:00","id":1511733,"title":"","content":"<b>Mind the Gap</b><br /> <br /> There\u2019s not actually a problem I can find until we get to Mind 3, but then they start coming fast and furiously. The Mind 3 writeup says: \u201ccombined with Correspondence, Forces, Matter, or Life, he is able to employ telekinesis, pyrokinetics, and psychophysical assault, influencing objects, elements, or people with the power of his mind. That\u2019s a staggering array of effects and a few might meaningfully use Mind, but most of them can be accomplished with just Correspondence, Forces, Matter, and/or Life:<br /> <br /> Moving objects around is Correspondence or Forces <i>alone.</i><br /> Controlling fire is Forces <i>alone</i>.<br /> If by Psychophysical assault we mean biokinetically attacking someone\u2019s body, that\u2019s Life <i>alone</i> (more on this later).<br /> Influencing objects or elements is vague but outside telekinesis most effects would be Matter or Forces<i> alone.</i><br /> Influencing people by psychically controlling their limbs (as opposed to their mind) would be Life <i>alone,</i><br /> Influencing people by psychically controlling their minds would be Mind <i>alone.</i><br /> <br /> None of the above (except the last one) actually use Mind as a Sphere. Of all of the suggested effects, only two reasonably use a combo with Mind:<br /> <br /> A Psychophysical Assault where the mage is specifically going for a psychic attack or illusion that has real world effects (Matrix style \u201cthe mind makes it real\u201d type effects or similar) would be a combined Mind/Life effect.<br /> <br /> Pyrokinetic effects where you create fire could use Forces/Mind to generate the fire out of thoughts rather than Forces/Prime to create the fire out of quintessence.<br /> <br /> <br /> Deep breath\u2026<br /> <br /> See Avatar is listed as Mind 3/Prime 2/Spirit 1. I don\u2019t know how to complain about this one because Avatars are somewhat vaguely defined anyways. That said, while I can accept that Spirit, Prime, or Mind might have a role in seeing one, there\u2019s no particular reason you\u2019d need all three. My best guess is that this was supposed to be Mind or Spirit, but not both. It\u2019s hard to say because this one comes from the Common Magical Effects chart and has no explanation.<br /> <br /> Compel Sleep is listed as Mind 4/Life 3. That should really be Mind 4 OR Life 3. There\u2019s nothing wrong with using both spheres, but either alone can do the job.<br /> <br /> Astral body of light is not well defined and whether the sphere combo of Mind 4+/Spirit 3/Prime 2 works depends on what it is. If it means creating a spiritual body from the ether and then projecting your mind into it, that would be the right sphere combo. That\u2019s not specified to be something projection can do, but it\u2019s also not specified as something projection can\u2019t do. The problem here is vagueness.<br /> <br /> Finally Move Mind to Another Body continues the confusion about how Minds are linked to bodies, though I already covered it in the Life section.<br /> <br /> Final tally: 15 effects examined. 7 arbitrary Sphere additions. No extra targeting spheres. 1-2 overengineered spell. 1 inconsistent unstated rule. 6 of the 15 have no problems.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Well that\u2019s just Prime\u2026</b><br /> <br /> Starting off with the animation rules. Animating a corpse is listed as Life 2/Prime 2. Animating a skeleton is listed as Matter 2/Prime 2. We could interpret that as Prime 2 providing some kind of animating force, while Matter and Life are locking spheres. The only problem is that Prime 2 doesn't list any such ability, none of the ranks of Prime do. Also Life could repair and animate flesh on its own without anything else, though I would not say the same for Matter.<br /> <br /> Physical illusions are listed as a combination of Prime and Forces. Manipulating light, sound, and momentum are all within the realm of Forces 2 alone, with no need for Prime. Prime could be generating a Body of Light and Forces giving it the feel of substance, I suppose, so its not that the combo of Prime 2+/Forces 2+ is wrong, just overly specific.<br /> <br /> Consecration of an object is listed as Prime 2, while consecration of a living being is Prime 2/Life 2+. I\u2019m surprised it took this long to get to an example, but Mage sometimes assumes that casting on living things is more difficult than casting on inanimate ones and so throws in extraneous Life requirements. If its ever spelled out as a rule I haven\u2019t found it, and it is applied with reckless disregard for consistency and common sense.<br /> <br /> A similar thing happens in Prime 3 with Enchant Lifeform requiring Life 3, when no such addition is required for enchanting an object. Notably the Common Magical Effects Chart does not require Life for enchanting lifeforms.<br /> <br /> Creating Soulgems and Creating Soulflowers requires Matter 4 and Life 5 respectively and there\u2019s not a good reason why or why not. We could argue that making this change involves a change to the actual matter or life pattern. We could also argue the other way. This effect implies that there\u2019s deeper elements to the metaphysics of Mage but never actually explains what those are.<br /> <br /> 10 total effects examined. 4 arbitrary sphere additions and 2 more that may or may not be arbitrary depending on metaphysics. Overall Prime is plagued by vagueness<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 05-15-2023, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T05:41:58-07:00","id":1511793,"title":"","content":"<b>Spirit</b><br /> <br /> Spirit is perhaps the lightest section with only three significant problems:<br /> <br /> Spirit 1 says that combined with other spheres a mage may spot forces, places, or items with unusual ties to the spirit world, such as Awakened objects, elemental spirits, possessed organisms, shallowings, Nodes, etc. Spirit can accomplish most of that without help. There\u2019s nothing wrong with using more spheres and there are benefits, but the book makes it seem mandatory and it isn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> Spirit 3/Mind 2 is suggested to read the resonance, synergy, and hierarchy of spirits and I don\u2019t see what Mind is bringing to the table in this arrangement. It would certainly be Mind 2 to determine a person's likes/dislikes, what they do, and who they work for, but for spirits that kind of thing is metaphysically deeper and speaks to their very nature as spirits. When you pull this information from a spirit, you aren't reading their mind you are reading them. That said, you could read their mind for the information as well, but in that case I don't know why you would need Spirit.<br /> <br /> Then commanding spirits is stated in the chart to require Spirit 4/Mind 4. This should probably be Spirit 4 or Mind 4, as Spirit 4 is explicitly enough to bind and command spirits.<br /> <br /> Final results: 8 effects examined. 1-2 arbitrary additions. 1-2 merged spell.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Time Enough at Last</b><br /> <br /> Like Spirit, Time attempts to expand the utility of Time 1 by tacking on other spheres to allow a mage to \u201cdetect the influence of the Time Sphere on other spells or Patterns. It should be able to accomplish that on its own.<br /> <br /> Then we have Prophecy, which is purely a Time 2 spell unless the mage is psychic, if he is he must add Mind 2 because the universe hates psychics. I wouldn't complain if Mind was an optional sphere that allowed better understanding of the Prophecy in some way but the Common Effects Chart lists these as the same spell.<br /> <br /> Reverse ageing. We covered this from the point of view of Life, but there are two Time based versions Time 3+/Life 4 and Time 3+/Matter 2. In either case Time is rewinding the clock on them on its own. The best I can come up with for Life and Matter is that the writeup is assuming that the spells are locked and that the spell is keeping memories intact. If so, the default spell is Time 3, it needs Matter 2 or Life 2 if the target is moving, and it needs higher levels of Matter or Life if you want to rewind some elements of the target while keeping others (memory, current levels of radioactivity, etc) intact. That's reasonable but not clear.<br /> <br /> Then there\u2019s the extremely vague \u201cCombining this Rank with other Spheres, the mage can affect other Patterns (Forces, Life, or Matter 2),\u201d which is completely unhelpful. I think perhaps this was meant to be part of the previous paragraph (in the book) on rewinding time and was incorporating a locking effect (technically still optional, but without it the rewind only takes things back to the point they entered the target area). In its current location it means nothing.<br /> <br /> Speaking of meaning nothing, with Time 3/Entropy 3 the mage can invoke multiple probabilities. What the mage can invoke multiple probabilities to do is left to the imagination of the reader.<br /> <br /> Apparently it takes Time 3/Life 3/Mind 1 to move back in time while remembering events from the future. Firstly, I think Life or Mind alone could accomplish that. Secondly, its completely unnecessary as the Mage doesn\u2019t have to rewind time for the target while moving it about. I suppose he could, but that\u2019s not what\u2019s being described.<br /> <br /> Time 4 says that by adding in Correspondence, Forces, Life, Matter, and/or Spirit a mage can trap a phenomenon in a time bubble. Charitably interpreted (and ignoring the suggested Correspondence) that\u2019s the addition of locking spheres. You could probably get away without them, though if so you'd be trapping an entire area in timeless space and that would be difficult to describe. More problematically, the example is a Time/Forces/Entropy effect to trap a tornado. While I do think there\u2019s an association between Entropy and weather, that has no bearing in this case and this should just be a Time/Forces effect.<br /> <br /> Final Tally: 12 effects examined. 3 arbitrary sphere additions (I'm only counting the extra sensory spheres as one, else I'd have to say 11 arbitrary sphere additions).<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T06:48:01-07:00","id":1511795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Astral body of light is not well defined and whether the sphere combo of Mind 4+/Spirit 3/Prime 2 works depends on what it is. If it means creating a spiritual body from the ether and then projecting your mind into it, that would be the right sphere combo. That\u2019s not specified to be something projection can do, but it\u2019s also not specified as something projection can\u2019t do. The problem here is vagueness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your supposition it's on point. This one comes straigth from <i>Infinite Tapestry</i>. It's the <i>Astral Sojourn</i> Rote. It was hard but efficient way to travel the Umbra bypassing the Avatar Storm.<br /> <br /> Mind 4/5 allows one to make an astral projection, and astral projections don't suffer from the Avatar Storm for some reason, but that takes you to the Astral Umbra and you can't travel freely elsewhere.<br /> The Prime 2/Spirit 3 component creates a spiritual body to be able to exist in the other layers of the Umbra, bypassing that limitation (with the added effect of you having your physical stats because apparently those are the stats of the &quot;body of ligth&quot;, for good or ill, but you're still leaving your body away connected with a silver cord )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T05:17:11-07:00","id":1511858,"title":"","content":"I took a look at the rotes. I wrote down analyses of the first few then just jotted down thoughts on the rest.<br /> <br /> <b>Black Card/Black Box</b> \u2013 Hack a system even from unconnected ports. Corr 2/Forces 2/Mind 2.<br /> I\u2019d say this should be Correspondence 2 alone. That said, if we are charitable to the book and uncharitable to the players we could say that the overall data stream is the pattern and we are teleporting it piecemeal. In that case we would need Forces for the connection. I don't see why Mind is here. Were this effect replacing the actual hacking I might see the need for Mind, but this effect specifically says the mage needs to do the hacking himself. <i>Unnecessary sphere or spheres added.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Hot Shotting</b> \u2013 Amplify the sound of a gun for increased damage and intimidation factor. Forces 2. Optional add of Mind 2<br /> The Forces side of this is odd because it gives reduced difficulty and an extra success that can either be used for accuracy or intimidation. Adding the extra Forces success to intimidation is sketchy but cinematic. There\u2019s nothing wrong with using Forces for either effect alone so they can certainly be used together, its just a unique way of approaching the system. I like the addition of the Mind sphere variant because it adds a unique extra intimidation effect against Willpower and there\u2019s a good reason to cast what would otherwise be two separate effects together. <br /> <br /> <b>Hands of Death</b> \u2013 Enhance hand to hand damage. Life 3 or Forces 2 or both. Optional adds of Entropy 2 or Prime 2.<br /> A basic Life attack on an unarmed strike or a Forces augmentation to that unarmed strike. The Life attack is not aggravated damage unless the strike is truly theatrical, so in most cases the Forces version is undeniably superior (lower difficulty and more damage). Entropy addition reduces armor, durability, or soak. Prime 2 allows the Forces version to get aggravated damage (still vulgar so Life 3 doesn\u2019t need the help), though the Common Effects chart indicates that cost a point of quintessence and the spell doesn\u2019t call for that. <i>That quintessence cost is the only issue I see.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Right Click</b> \u2013 Instant Data with a Mind Computer Interface. Mind 3/Data 3, with Forces, Life, Matter, Prime, DimSci options.<br /> The description is a little vague but the spell allows the mage to pull up a lot of information about what he sees through a combination of mental scans and internet access. Mind is specifically used to read surface thoughts while Data grants remote access. The problem here is that surface thoughts only require Mind 2 and a worldwide connection only requires Data 2. The optional spheres add other senses to the data as appropriate and DimSci 2 allows the rote to work from the umbra. <i>The Sphere requirements are too high.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Hypernarrative Influence</b> \u2013 Mental Influence via Tropes. Mind 4 with an Entropy 2 option.<br /> Influences people to behave in accordance with common tropes and, with the Entropy addon, influences reality to do the same. The basic rote lets the mage trigger the desired behavior with a successful Manipulation + Appropriate Skill roll. There's no real system for the Entropy effect, that's in the hands of the ST. I see no issues here.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T07:38:38-07:00","id":1511868,"title":"","content":"<b>Sanitize Evidence</b> \u2013 Clear up the scene by evaporating what we don\u2019t like. Matter 2/Forces 2 and/or Prime 4<br /> Correctly gets that Prime 4 is enough to dissolve patterns. It also gets that using pattern spheres to evaporate matter and energy doesn\u2019t require Prime or Entropy. On the other hand, I doubt all of the matter being removed is simple and converting it to Forces (or converting extraneous Forces) should be Forces 3. So the pattern sphere variant should be Matter 2+/Forces 3. It is also quite slow. One hour converts 10 pounds of matter into pure energy. That seems like a made up restriction. <i>Spheres have the wrong rank. Invented restrictions.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Secure the Scene</b> \u2013 Keep people away from the scene while examining it. Mind 2/3 /Forces 1/Matter 1 with a Forces 3<br /> This is way too many things getting put into the same effect. The Mind effect suggests people ignore the scene or pushes them to. Presumably there would be a Mind 4 version that would command them to. The Forces 1 and Matter 1 are for perception boosts, which have nothing to do with the other parts of the spell and really should be their own thing (much like Sanitize Evidence is its own thing). In normal circumstances these would be different actions taken by different people or the same person at different times. The Forces 3 variant allows a very vulgar blackout sphere. That effect does make sense in the context of this spell. <i>Each sphere makes sense but they make more sense as separate rotes. </i><br /> <br /> <b>Dimension Bomb</b> \u2013 Use Spirit or Dimensional Science to toss a bomb across the gauntlet \u2013 DimSci 3, optional Forces 3/Prime 2<br /> Toss a bomb across the gauntlet. The variant option replaces the bomb with a forces attack. This is a very basic idea and I see no problems.<br /> <br /> <b>Golden Gunman</b> \u2013 Multiple actions combined with acrobatics. Time 3/Forces 2<br /> Basic multiple actions from Time and increased mobility from Forces. There\u2019s not really a system for how to handle the acrobatics. Also, given the description it seems like the effect functionally needs to travel with the target, so I\u2019d require a locking sphere. This should have Life 2 (or I suppose Matter 2 if the effect pairs with the weapons). <i>Missing benefits and requirements</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Bullet Catch</b> \u2013 Deflect or catch bullets. Forces 2/Life 2/Time 2<br /> I don\u2019t see the need for all three spheres here. I see what each one is doing, and there\u2019s nothing wrong with using all three, but I think the effect can be done with less. If all three are required, I\u2019d like to see how the combination is superior to partial versions.<br /> <br /> <b>Chain of Whispers</b> \u2013 Contagious gossip spreading. Mind 3/Correspondence 2<br /> A very strange application of Correspondence. The description says that Correspondence pulls the information from person to person. That doesn\u2019t sound right. Instead, I\u2019d say that Mind attaches the infectious desire to spread the information to the idea and Correspondence is used to propagate the spell between people via that connection formed when they tell each other. I\u2019m really not sure Correspondence is needed here. <i>Odd use of Correspondence.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Penny Dreadful\u2019s Bright New Penny</b> \u2013 Restore old objects \u2013 Matter 3 or 4/Time 2/Prime 2<br /> This is interesting because there\u2019s no reason you couldn\u2019t do it this way. Peek into the past, see the form it is supposed to be and then restore it or create it from scratch. Prime only makes sense in the recreating from scratch version of the spell, Matter 3 alone could probably change the item back to what it was unless you only have a few fragments of it. The purpose of Prime is badly explained but otherwise this one works well.<br /> <br /> <b>Psychic Interface</b> \u2013 Psychically commune with a computer. Mind 3 or 4/Data 2/Forces 2. Spirit is a potential alternate to Data.<br /> Mind 3 to project the mage\u2019s consciousness into the computer mind, Mind 4 to project himself to the digital web. Forces 2 to manipulate the electrical systems. Data is the sticking point here. I think its being used for translation, which is why it can be replaced by Spirit but not Correspondence. Spirit can also replace Mind, so it would probably be good to list a Spirit/Forces variant.<br /> <br /> <b>Talons</b> \u2013 Grow talons. Life 3 or 4. Optional Matter 2 and Prime 2 addons.<br /> A very basic body alteration spell with a Matter 2 variant to allow inorganic claws and a Prime 2 variant to allow enchanted Agg damage. The only issue is that enchanting living matter is Prime 3, so that would be the requirement without using Matter for inorganic claws. <i>Wrong sphere ranks in one specific case.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Witch\u2019s Vengeance</b> \u2013 Really open ended rote for cursing. Entropy 4 or Life 3 or Time 3 or some combination. Correspondence/Data range boosting.<br /> Really bad punctuation is making it look like it is Entropy 4 or Life 3/Time 3, but it is any combination of the three. Honestly this is a pretty ridiculous entry as it is really saying <i>Witch\u2019s Vengeance: Do some form of cursing</i>. Also, normal range is clear sensory range, not touch. There\u2019s no reason this should be touch. <i>Invented restrictions.</i><br /> <br /> <b>The Notorious V.L.C.</b> \u2013 Turn a vampire into a lawn chair. Life 5/Matter 5<br /> I don\u2019t like the tone. There\u2019s nothing wrong with the sphere requirements (edit: actually, Matter might be high), but the description goes out of its way to say this is really stupid. Yes, this is a silly and petty spell, but it is also a grand Mage tradition. It\u2019s fine to say this is probably a bad idea, but padding out the list or drawbacks to almost a page is excessive, and making up mechanics just to reduce the effectiveness of the spell is spiteful. <i>Invented restrictions.</i><br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 05-17-2023, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T10:34:50-07:00","id":1512366,"title":"","content":"I started digging more into the Vampire Lawn Chair rote, but my breakdown was becoming more of a rant so I'll shelve that for now and just give my final thoughts:<br /> <br /> I suspect that the rules changed a few times during production and not every instance was caught in editing. Sometimes reading M20 feels like an archaeological dig where you can see the newer layers of rules built on the ruins of the old ones. There are a lot of accidental additions of spheres, \u2018ands\u2019 instead of \u2018ors\u2019, statements that are contradicted a paragraph later, and descriptions that don\u2019t actually describe anything.<br /> <br /> Beyond that there is also missing information in the rules that really needs to be present. The Locking Spheres section, for instance, does not say what rank you need to use to lock. Certain spheres seem to omit capabilities that other parts of M20 assume they have. Others seem to be hurting for not enough to do. So when there's a discrepancy it is often hard to tell if the book is appealing to rules it never stated or ignoring the rules. <br /> <br /> Four spheres in particular really suffer:<br /> <br /> Correspondence and Time are a mess of contradictory statements and vague descriptions that don\u2019t give enough information. There are clauses and sentences that are either out of place or need to be cut entirely, and descriptions of spells that indicate one thing is happening paired with sphere requirements that indicate another thing.<br /> <br /> Forces suffers from not having enough meat, and I think it always has (I need to check my library). The other pattern spheres can divide up into simple and complex versions, but all the forces a mage typically wants to play with (motion, light, sound, heat, electricity, etc.) would be simple forces. Things like gravity and storms are interesting but situational. So Forces takes things like magnitude, which would ordinarily be a function of successes, and pushes them to higher ranks. It\u2019s not terribly elegant, and it makes the higher levels of Forces seem like Inspector Leopard of the Yard: \u201cThe same, only more violent!\u201d<br /> <br /> Prime is small, vague, and uncertain. It is a short section with only a few concrete abilities per rank, and half of them claim to need other spheres to even make work (even when that isn\u2019t clear) On the other hand there are not one but two abilities attributed to it that are never stated anywhere in its writeup (animating things and illusion). Additionally, it seems to be the catchall requirement: any time it seems like something isn\u2019t difficult enough there\u2019s a good chance Prime will be tacked on as a requirement.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T02:11:19-07:00","id":1512550,"title":"","content":"Prime has a short list of applications, but is the dustbin catchall for &quot;magic stuff that isn't covered by the 8 spheres based on 'real' things&quot;. Making Charms and Wonders is pretty key, and you need Prime for it. Inflicting Aggravated damage, and making things resist it, seems to be an application... though resisting it is only told to us in the Armor instrument. In the instruments section.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> have you considered doing more posts regarding weird additions like that? For instance the only reason we know (know?) that Prime 2 can let you soak Agg is an entry relating to an instrument, and it seems to be instrument-specific, which is a HUGE can of worms. It's like if the Inventions instrument writeup casually mentioned that Time 3 lets you travel in time if you build a time machine.<br /> <br /> Prime is, as you say, also a go-to requirement for when an effect needs to be more magical-er and contributes to sphere bloat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T07:37:00-07:00","id":1512572,"title":"","content":"Well I did a quick search of every time a sphere combination is given for a specific effect in M20, I then checked them against the Prime writeup. Entries that match the writeup are in green, those that are wrong are red, those that give a new ability to Prime are in purple.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">332 \u2013 Countering Paradox </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">332 \u2013 Fueling Countermagic </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">332 \u2013 Absorbing Quintessence Through Avatar, From a Node with Prime 1, From Tass with Prime 3, From anywhere with Prime 5. No mention of absorbing by degrading a pattern </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">332 \u2013 Prime 1 - See Quintessence </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">407 \u2013 Armor hardened with Prime can resist Aggravated Damage. Repeated on 588 \u2013 Not sure this is in the writeup. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">418 \u2013 Weapons enchanted with Prime can hit non-materialized spirits </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#8e44ad\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">418 \u2013 Spirit 2/Prime 2 acts like Life magic to spirits, but not ghosts. For ghosts its Entropy 3/Prime 2. This is an alternate combination to the more standard Spirit 3. Repeated on 508. I'm on the fence about this one.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#27ae60\">422 \u2013 Using Prime 2 a mage can make an attack directly attack a pattern.</span><span style=\"color:#c0392b\">Or Prime 3.</span><span style=\"color:#538135\"> The Sidebar says both, but 2 is consistent with the writeup</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">434 \u2013 In Old Style Certamen, Prime is used to soak. Not in the writeup, but then, why would it be?</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">436 \u2013 Fire naturally turns patterns into \u201cquintessential chaos\u201d and Prime 3 can channel that quintessence.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">438 \u2013 Prime is one of the spheres suggested for putting up a Vulgar magic shield against a blast.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">440 \u2013 Prime can undermine the durability trait via disintegration. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#538135\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">464 \u2013 Prime 2 can enhance a power supply. I initially thought this was new, but enhancing objects is Prime 2.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">477 \u2013 Objects can be bound to people so they follow them spiritually or astrally. </span><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Apparently this requires Entropy for the Underworld, which is nonsense.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">477 \u2013 Astral Sojourn\u2019s Body of Light \u2013 Actual explanation. Prime here is creating an Astral Body of Light as a base. Repeated on 509</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">477 \u2013 Astral beacon to help adrift astral travellers find their way back. Not clear what Prime is doing here but it doesn\u2019t map to anything in the writeup.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">479 \u2013 Prime 3/Spirit 2 to use a familiar or Totem to shield from the Avatar Storm. Spirit 4/Prime 3 to force one. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">485 \u2013 Not an ability, but Prime is always vulgar in the underworld.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">494 \u2013 Spirit 4/Life 3/Prime 2 is an Exorcism. Prime doesn\u2019t seem to do anything here.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">505 \u2013 Forces 2+/Prime 2+ for Physical Illusions. Forces 4+/Prime 4+ for Holodeck levels. What is Prime doing? Repeated on 508</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">505 \u2013 Prime 2 and a point of quintessence to turn another magical attack aggravated. Repeated multiple times on 543. This is repeated so often it is clearly intended, it just isn\u2019t in the Prime writeup. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">507 \u2013 The table for how much Quintessence can be extracted from a living creature.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">508 \u2013 Crafting Wonders requirements (Trinket 2 (consecration), Periapt 3, Talisman, Fetish, or Device 4)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">508 \u2013 Prime 2 is a component of animating undead. This is giving Prime an animating force.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">508 \u2013 Standard creation from nothing rules. This is repeated often so I\u2019m not going to call it out every time.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">508 \u2013 Life 4/Spirit 4/Prime 3 to revive the recently dead. What is Prime doing?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#538135\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">508 \u2013 Prime 5 can bless or curse, apparently. I initially thought this was new, but there is a line about it in the writeup.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">508 \u2013 Prime 4/Spirit 4 to drain a spirit\u2019s essence. These numbers are off. Prime should be able to do this on its own at 5, but it should only be 3 if using Spirit to convert the spirit to quintessence.</span> <span style=\"color:#538135\">Indeed on pg 521 this is Spirit 2/Prime 3.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">509 \u2013 Prime 2 can conceal an aura</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">509 \u2013 Probably a hasty generalization. Prime 2 can Consecrate/Harden/Perfect an Object. This would also indicate Matter 3+ could consecrate, so I think this one merged a few different things for convenience.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">509 \u2013 Prime 2 - Object inflicts or resists aggravated damage.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">509 \u2013 With Mind and Spirit, Prime 2 can see an Avatar. Avatars are strange.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">509 \u2013 Prime 2+ is allegedly necessary for Ward/Ban. Nonsense. There are uses for Prime in this, but only in specific cases.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">510 - Prime 2 to employ a periapt, </span><span style=\"color:#538135\">fuel a pattern, or weave a body of light</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">510 </span><span style=\"color:#538135\">\u2013 Prime 3 to Absorb or Channel Quintessence, Create a Quintessence Weapon, Drain Quintessence, Energize a Periapt, or Exchange Quintessence</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">510 \u2013 Prime 4 to Destroy an object by draining quintessence, </span><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">Drain a node, or Refine Tass.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">510 \u2013 Prime 5 to Create a node, destroy a creature by draining, or Nullify Paradox.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">513 \u2013 Prime 4 necessary for setting up a Ward or Ban based on Resonance. Much more reasonble. Prime 4 may be high, but it is the rank at which mages can move about resonance.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">516 \u2013 Counter pattern bleeding. Details needed, but presumably this is an application of summoning and channeling quintessence, which is in the writeup.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">516 \u2013 Prime 1/Life 1 to see the flows of energy that bind creatures to the universe. Should be Prime alone.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">517 \u2013 Life 5/Prime 5 \u2013 Transmute living creatures to raw energy. <span style=\"color:#c00000\">If this is destructive it is Prime 5 alone.</span><span style=\"color:#7030a0\"> If it is meant to turn the person into a being or raw energy, that\u2019s new.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">518 \u2013 Matter 2/Prime 2 \u2013 Dissolve a simple substance into quintessence. Wrong Prime value. Either 0 or 3.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">519 \u2013 Transforming cars into robots requires an arbitrary addition of Forces and Prime. Possibly another application of animating force.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">520 \u2013 Unnecessary addition in a spell to create physical objects from ephemera. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">537 \u2013 It takes Prime 3 to spend more than a point of Quintessence per dot in Avatar.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">545 \u2013 Using countermagic to reflect a spell or protect someone else, or unweave a spell requires Prime 1 in addition to any other requirements.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">545 \u2013 Prime 3 can harden reality (anitmagic). Uses the Prime rank as a dice pool.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">546 \u2013 Prime and Mind necessary to counter Fae powers.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">549 \u2013 Nullify Paradox</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">557 \u2013 Prime 4/Mind 4 to drive out the Paradox from the mind of a Mage suffering from Quiet. Isn\u2019t paradox Prime 5?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">597 \u2013 Harvest quintessence from a sacrifice.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">602 \u2013 Right Click \u2013 Optional sensory addition to see quintessence.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">603 \u2013 Sanitize evidence \u2013 Convert matter to raw quintessence at Prime 4.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">606 \u2013 Social conditioning is a Mind 3/Prime 2 effect. What is Prime 2 doing?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">633 \u2013 Summon storms with Forces 4/Prime 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">658 \u2013 Life 3/Forces 2/Prime 2 to disrupt cybernetics? Prime isn\u2019t doing anything that I can see.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">663 \u2013 Life 5/Mind 5/Prime 5/Spirit 5/Time 4 effect to reconstitute someone from a save point. What is Prime 5 doing?</span></span><br /> \u200b</span><br /> <br /> Entirely new powers: Animating Force, Hardening reality, Countermagic, Blast Protection, and possibly Illusions and things to do with Avatars.<br /> Niche powers: Affecting Fae, Certamen.<br /> Powers that were certainly intended but accidentally left out: Using a periapt, Refine Tass, and Drain a Node.<br /> <br /> As it turns out, enhancing objects to resist agg damage is in the writeup. When you first mentioned it I thought it wasn't, but I checked and its there.<br /> <br /> Edit: And looking carefully at Prime 2 it says it can infuse weapons or attacks to do aggravated damage. It doesn't specifically say spells, but any spell you infuse this way would be an attack spell, so while it could be clearer I think it is reasonable to say the effect is in the writeup after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 05-25-2023, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T08:10:54-07:00","id":1512575,"title":"","content":"What's funny is that the armor section says you can enchant an object to resist agg... and then one of the examples is painting yourself with woad. I know it's niche, but that just means you can get the effect onto your body without wearing any armour!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T12:22:26-07:00","id":1512615,"title":"","content":"Woad would count as an object, technically. Also, it should be possible to do this to a person as well. This is one area where the writeup of Prime gets very iffy.<br /> <br /> Prime 2 describes infusing weapons and attacks with quintessence in order to hurt spirits and inflict or protect against aggravated damage. The very next line it says: &quot;On a related note, she may also \u2013 with Life 2 for simple organisms, or Life 3 for complex ones \u2013 consecrate a living thing at this Rank, as if that life-form were an object described above.&quot; <br /> <br /> If you read that paragraph in isolation, as you are likely to do if you are quickly referencing the section, it is very clearly saying you can enchant living creatures to take and resist aggravated damage. The sentence immediately follows the description of enchanting weapons. It is in the same paragraph with the description of enchanting weapons. Enchanting objects is the only other thing in that paragraph, and the sentence itself starts with &quot;On a related note,&quot; It's not just a reasonable interpretation of what is written, it is the most reasonable interpretation of those words in that order. Prime 2 even lists Enchant Patterns in its header, so it tracks with what the book says that Rank can do. If it wanted to limit the effect to objects, the header should say Enchant Objects.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Prime 3's header lists Enchant Life and its writeup specifically mentions (with the same nonsensical Life 3 requirement) enchanting living things to inflict or endure aggravated damage. The wording here is more direct. Also, Prime 1 has a definition for consecration<br /> <br /> So we have two alternatives. Either the same effect has duplicate writeups in both Prime 2 and Prime 3, which is quite possible given some of the other editing issues in the spheres writeups, or we completely ignore the words &quot;On a related note&quot; and the proximity, and we interpret the sentence as applying to the consecration effect described in Prime 1. Given the context of Prime 1 and Prime 3 I think the latter was the intention, but you'd never even consider that if you were just grabbing a quick reference.<br /> <br /> And don't get me started on the ridiculous way extra Life requirements are thrown into both sections with no regards for the capabilities of Life or Prime.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T15:42:12-07:00","id":1512782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1512615#post1512615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you read that paragraph in isolation, as you are likely to do if you are quickly referencing the section, it is very clearly saying you can enchant living creatures to take and resist aggravated damage. </div> </div> </div> </div>This Effect, Spell, Casting, or Capability most likely does also include regenerating and healing from aggravated damage of various types.<br /> Depending on the particular Mage ( whether an Ecstatic, a Verbenae, or a Syndicate Technocrat ) Prime magic ( or Prime lore ) should be enough for this purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T17:41:26-07:00","id":1513586,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve been going through some of Ramnesis\u2019s stuff to see what I can resolve of the various discrepancies, before I encounter a need to supply an answer in my upcoming game (which is probably still months away). It really is quite a useful list.<br /> <br /> I have worked out resolutions I am happy with for some items. However, then I hit this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1512572#post1512572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">418 \u2013 Weapons enchanted with Prime can hit non-materialized spirits </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#8e44ad\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">418 \u2013 Spirit 2/Prime 2 acts like Life magic to spirits, but not ghosts. For ghosts its Entropy 3/Prime 2. This is an alternate combination to the more standard Spirit 3. Repeated on 508. I'm on the fence about this one.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Reading the actual text, I note that it says that Spirit 3 acts as Life 3 on a spirit. (Technically it says \u201cUmbrood entity\u201d, and then abbreviates this to \u201centity\u201d; while I\u2019ve considered whether the writer is trying to distinguish between \u201cUmbrood entity\u201d, \u201cUmbral entity\u201d and \u201cspirit\u201d, I think these are being used as synonyms in the relevant passage.) Is it possible that the intent is to allow Spirit 3 to act as Life 3 against spirits, but that Spirit 2 combined with Prime 2 can act as Life 2 on spirits?<br /> <br /> There\u2019s not a lot of applicable Life 2 effects. (Life needs 3 to do damage, and healing is limited to self or simple life-forms at Life 2, for example.) But Life 2 can be used to alter simple life-forms, including heal them, harm them, or cause or cure a disease. So maybe Spirit 2/Prime 2 can do these things to the simple spirits that make up much of the spirit world (for example, if walking through an Umbral forest, the trees could be simple spirits), but Spirit 3 is needed to directly damage or alter the kind of spirits that could generally be considered a threat to a PC (including any tree-spirit that is aware enough to carry on a conversation with a PC)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T06:16:16-07:00","id":1513640,"title":"","content":"That would work, though the Spirit sphere doesn't make a distinction between simple and complex spirits in its writeup. Also, if Spirit 3 doesn't need help affecting spirits, why would Spirit 2? <br /> <br /> Honestly, the more I think about it, the more I think the combination is nonsense. The only consistent way that Prime 2 makes spells like Life is in causing Aggravated damage. Spirit 2 can't attack anyways only to allow another attack to hit spirits. Even then, most spirits treat aggravated damage like lethal so adding it is meaningless. Ghosts do mark Aggravated damage (if you are using Wraith rules) but they use a different sphere combo anyways. <br /> <br /> I really can't think of a single thing Prime could be doing that would matter in this context. Even if we use its unstated and hypothetical ability to affect/create animating forces, I don't see why that alters how Spirit works.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> On an unrelated note, there's a method I've been using to figure out sphere requirements: I break down the spell into Main Effect (X) on Subjects (Y) with conditions (Z). <br /> <br /> X is just the primary effect stated as simply as possible, with no consideration for complications. <br /> <br /> Y is what it takes to get and keep the spell working on what you want it working on. By default a spell can be cast on any complete pattern in normal sensory range, but it won't move with the target. This step covers what you need to extend beyond that default, so elements like Range Extension (Correspondence and Time), Locking Effects (Pattern Spheres), affecting parts of patterns, etc. <br /> <br /> Z covers any other modifications you need to make to the spell to get it to behave in specific ways, most commonly triggers and exceptions. <br /> <br /> So for instance, a spell to teleport any contestant who crosses out of bounds back to the starting line might break down like:<br /> <br /> Main effect: A gateway spell where the opening is the out of bounds line and the exit is the starting line. We don't tend to think of gateways having different sized entrances and exits but there's not really a reason they have to. Correspondence 4.<br /> <br /> Subject: The subject is the locations themselves. If it is a long course the mage might need range extenders to cast it over the area, however the spell is already at Corr 4 so that doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> Conditions: When I picture this spell I picture everything looking normal until the line is crossed, so light and other forces need to pass through the region normally. M20 doesn't give much explanation of how to make exceptions, but the few examples we have (Wards and Bans) points to needing the same rank you would need to affect a pattern directly. Forces 2 would be the easiest way, though you could also handle this by making the gate only work for Life and Matter.<br /> <br /> Overall: Correspondence 4/Forces 2 for this method. <br /> <br /> By breaking things down this way I get an idea of what each sphere is doing and how the requirements might change if we consider a different primary effect (e.g. if instead of a gateway, the primary effect is a direct teleportation of the contestant (Corr 3)).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T06:24:18-07:00","id":1513763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1513640#post1513640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if Spirit 3 doesn't need help affecting spirits, why would Spirit 2?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that\u2019s my big concern with that interpretation. When I consider what would lead the writer to that design decision\u2026 well, I just can\u2019t think of anything.<br /> <br /> I did some rules archaeology to try to work out what effect the writer might have been trying to bring in from a previous edition, given that M20 is mostly a compilation of rules from previous editions. The best I\u2019ve spotted so far is the combination of The Spirit\u2019s Caress and Bond of Blood noted in Revised (core rulebook page 187), which would allow a mage to transfer Quintessence/Essence/Power (a spirit has Power in Revised, which is renamed Essence in M20, and is exchanged for Quintessence by the effect) to or from a spirit, and since losing Essence is basically taking damage, and gaining Essence is basically healing, for spirits, this looks a lot like a Life effect when you generalise and simplify it a bit for inclusion in M20. But if this is the inspiration for it, it should require Spirit 2 and Prime 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T07:29:45-07:00","id":1513768,"title":"","content":"This is all rather on par for Mage.<br /> <br /> Its got 2 decades of history that to pull from for 20th Anniversary and much of that history was full of conflicting authors or attempts of fix the mother of all settings for creating &quot;<b>When engineers play RPGs</b>&quot; type problems(for an example from D&amp;D: look up bag of holding + Portable Hole arrows).<br /> <br /> Mage in particular is a setting that can easily fall apart if you look at it too hard with the above engineering mindset, something the Technocracy is supposed to be doing 24/7/365 and has been doing canonically for hundred-to-thousands of years before we get into time sphere shenanagans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T08:26:01-07:00","id":1513877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1512572#post1512572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">518 \u2013 Matter 2/Prime 2 \u2013 Dissolve a simple substance into quintessence. Wrong Prime value. Either 0 or 3.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting one. From what I can see, it\u2019s actually pretty consistent, with one important caveat\u2026<br /> <br /> Prime 2 allows the mage to \u201cdivert Quintessence into new [\u2026] forms. Combined with other spheres, this allows that mage to create new [\u2026] matter patterns\u201d. (Prime 2 on page 520.) Matter 2 includes corresponding information about creation of raw matter, but also adds this ability to dissolve raw matter into Quintessence.<br /> <br /> Prime 3 is required to \u201cpull small amounts of life force from a living sacrifice or (with Matter 2) from inert objects\u201d, and I think the intent here is to sacrifice these things in exchange for quitessence, which the mage then absorbs and uses.<br /> <br /> But the Matter 2 entry doesn\u2019t say anything about gaining Quintessence from dissolving matter.<br /> <br /> I conclude that the combination of Matter 2 and Prime 2 can reasonably be used to dissolve simple, homogenous, non-living substances into Quintessence - basically nothing, or thin air - as long as the mage doesn\u2019t care about harvesting that Quintessence. If the mage wants to absorb that Quintessence - even if the matter was conjured from Quintessence in the first place - Prime 3 would be required. (Quite possibly another mage with Prime 3 could channel that Quintessence as it is released, probably without even needing Matter.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11151,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","user":"travisjhall","date":". 06-04-2023, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T16:53:35-07:00","id":1513901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1512572#post1512572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">520 \u2013 Unnecessary addition in a spell to create physical objects from ephemera. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not finding any mention at all of this spell on page 520. What is this referring to?<br /> <br /> Edit: Ah, it\u2019s probably a wrong page number. Page 522 has something relevant, under Spirit 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11151,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","user":"travisjhall","date":". 06-04-2023, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T05:54:17-07:00","id":1513944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1513877#post1513877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I conclude that the combination of Matter 2 and Prime 2 can reasonably be used to dissolve simple, homogenous, non-living substances into Quintessence - basically nothing, or thin air - as long as the mage doesn\u2019t care about harvesting that Quintessence. If the mage wants to absorb that Quintessence - even if the matter was conjured from Quintessence in the first place - Prime 3 would be required. (Quite possibly another mage with Prime 3 could channel that Quintessence as it is released, probably without even needing Matter.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with most of your analysis. You\u2019ve nailed my reasons for when we should require a higher Prime rank. Here\u2019s my justification for the lower Prime rank:<br /> <br /> Prime\u2019s contribution to creation effects is making quintessence available for the Pattern Sphere to work on, it is not part of the conversion process. The pattern sphere is what converts that quintessence into a full pattern. For that reason the pattern sphere alone should be capable of converting the pattern back into quintessence. If the Mage doesn\u2019t care about what happens to the quintessence at that point, he doesn't need Prime at all. Prime 2 would only be useful if he wants to cleanly push that quint back into whatever place he diverts it from.<br /> <br /> Or basically, there are three interpretations of dissolving matter into quintessence:<br /> <br /> Matter 2 to dissolve a rock and let the quintessence do whatever it does.<br /> <br /> Matter 2/Prime 2 to dissolve a rock and clean up the quintessence.<br /> <br /> Matter 3/Prime 3 to dissolve a rock and absorb the quintessence.<br /> <br /> And while all three are reasonable interpretations, the Prime 2 variety fits the description least because there isn\u2019t any quintessence when you are done.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1513901#post1513901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not finding any mention at all of this spell on page 520. What is this referring to?<br /> <br /> Edit: Ah, it\u2019s probably a wrong page number. Page 522 has something relevant, under Spirit 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I have to add 1 to my PDFs page number to get the correct M20 number. I must have subtracted by mistake.<br /> <br /> You did find the one I was referring to. Spirit 3/Matter 3/Prime 2 to create objects from ephemera. If Prime is there, you don\u2019t need Spirit. If Spirit is there, you don\u2019t need Prime. Also the Matter requirement is the wrong rank.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T02:31:55-07:00","id":1513996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1513944#post1513944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prime\u2019s contribution to creation effects is making quintessence available for the Pattern Sphere to work on, it is not part of the conversion process. The pattern sphere is what converts that quintessence into a full pattern.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see why you could want this to be so, and having it be so in your games is a reasonable call. However, I haven't spotted anything in the rules that requires this to be so.<br /> <br /> What I'm seeing in the rulebook seems consistent with the idea that Prime is required not just to supply Quintessence but also to allow Quintessence to be transformed into Matter (or, alternatively, a living creature, or possibly things governed by other spheres).<br /> <br /> And at the moment, I'm happy with that as far as the game I intend to run in the future.<br /> <br /> And that means Matter 2/Prime 2 to utterly destroy simple matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1513944#post1513944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bYou did find the one I was referring to. Spirit 3/Matter 3/Prime 2 to create objects from ephemera. If Prime is there, you don\u2019t need Spirit. If Spirit is there, you don\u2019t need Prime. Also the Matter requirement is the wrong rank.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It says &quot;objects&quot; rather than &quot;matter&quot;, and that's consistent with Matter 3. (Raw simple substance at 2, an object at 3, a complicated device at 4.)<br /> <br /> The one thing I can think of that would make this make sense would be to require Prime 2 to allow this type of conjuration would be if Matter 3/Prime 2+Quintessence (actually spending one or more points of Quintessence) allows creation of a permanent object, but Matter 3/Prime 2/Spirit 3 (and no expenditure of Quintessence) allows conjuration of a temporary object. I'm not yet conviced that this is a good approach, though, or supported by other text.<br /> <br /> Especially since conjuration using Spirit would seem to require having an ephemeral object to begin with (so you need to find the spiritual counterpart of the object you want) rather than trying to conjure from nothing. If you had to create the ephemera from nothing at all, you'd be back to needing Prime (if you're interpreting the rules as needing Prime for conjuration from nothing even if Quitessence is not expended).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T04:23:47-07:00","id":1514001,"title":"","content":"I can see the argument far saying that you'd need Prime 2 to utterly destroy an object: basically, you're treating Prime as if it was another Pattern Sphere, governing Quintessence; and creation and destruction are then treated as \u201ctransforming ambient Quintessence into a physical form\u201d and \u201ctransforming a physical form into ambient Quintessence\u201d, respectively.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I buy the argument, though. What Sphere governs air? I think it's Forces (\u201cair\u201d being treated as \u201cwind\u201d); but it might be Matter. If I turn a rock into air, that would be either Matter 2/Forces 2 or just Matter 2; and while that's not technically the same thing as utter annihilation of the rock, in all practical ways it might as well be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-06-2023, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T06:02:56-07:00","id":1514003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1514001#post1514001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see the argument far saying that you'd need Prime 2 to utterly destroy an object: basically, you're treating Prime as if it was another Pattern Sphere, governing Quintessence; and creation and destruction are then treated as \u201ctransforming ambient Quintessence into a physical form\u201d and \u201ctransforming a physical form into ambient Quintessence\u201d, respectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that\u2019s exactly it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1514001#post1514001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I buy the argument, though. What Sphere governs air? I think it's Forces (\u201cair\u201d being treated as \u201cwind\u201d); but it might be Matter. If I turn a rock into air, that would be either Matter 2/Forces 2 or just Matter 2; and while that's not technically the same thing as it annihilation of the rock, in all practical ways it might as well be.</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn\u2019t a problem unique to this interpretation of the Spheres.<br /> <br /> The Common Magickal Effects section includes \u201cDisintegrate an Object\u201d (under Objects &amp; Elements, page 509), requiring either Matter 3 or Entropy 3/Time 3. The latter is presumably applying the effects of time to wear the object away. The former confirms that Matter 3 alone can simply change an object such that it is no longer there\u2026 but there\u2019s nothing to say that the object is simply removed from existence. This transformation could be transforming it into dust, or even into air, and letting it just dissipate.<br /> <br /> These things also raise questions of how many successes are required for this, and difficulty. I\u2019m not sure that the rules give strong guidance. And technically a transformation is supposed to end, unless at least 6 successes are rolled, so does the air coalesce back into the object at the end of the duration?<br /> <br /> If a rock is transformed into air, how much air results? Does this involve an explosion due to the pressure? (If mass is preserved, that\u2019s a heavily pressurised volume of air immediately after transformation.) Maybe Prime is desirable to avoid this.<br /> <br /> (I would say that wind would fall under Forces, as the movement of air, but air itself would be Matter. That would make it even easier to effectively annihilate a rock. But if any transmutation is possible, you have that problem anyway.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T06:43:47-07:00","id":1514008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1513996#post1513996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see why you could want this to be so, and having it be so in your games is a reasonable call. However, I haven't spotted anything in the rules that requires this to be so.<br /> <br /> What I'm seeing in the rulebook seems consistent with the idea that Prime is required not just to supply Quintessence but also to allow Quintessence to be transformed into Matter (or, alternatively, a living creature, or possibly things governed by other spheres).<br /> <br /> And at the moment, I'm happy with that as far as the game I intend to run in the future.<br /> <br /> And that means Matter 2/Prime 2 to utterly destroy simple matter.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1513996#post1513996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"></div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct that it works as an interpretation of prime so if it works for your game that\u2019s all that matters.<br /> <br /> That said, when I look at the wordings in M20, what I see is that quintessence isn\u2019t being transformed into patterns, it is the substance that the patterns are woven with. The opening description of Prime casts quintessence as the baseline energy that fuels the patterns of other forms. Prime 2 describes diverting quintessence into patterns, not transforming it. Indeed, most of Prime describes handling quintessence in terms of moving it around \u2013 drawing, draining, infusing, etc. Nor is this language new to M20. The implication is that Prime isn\u2019t transforming quintessence, it is channeling it.<br /> <br /> To use an art analogy, if the pattern is the image you draw on the page, the quintessence is the lead you draw it with. The lead isn\u2019t transformed in the process, just arranged in specific ways to make the drawing. Erasing the drawing doesn\u2019t change the drawing back into lead, it just destroys the arrangement thereof. The quintessence never stops being quintessence, it just gets bound into other things.<br /> <br /> So I maintain that Prime 2 is used to pull or induce quintessence into a pattern, which is necessary for creation effects, but not for disintegration ones. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It says &quot;objects&quot; rather than &quot;matter&quot;, and that's consistent with Matter 3. (Raw simple substance at 2, an object at 3, a complicated device at 4.) </div> </div> </div>This is more an editing complaint on my part than anything. When it comes to describing conjuration and transformation effects, sometimes Mage uses the lowest level of pattern sphere capable of this (Matter 2), sometimes it uses the lowest with a quick caveat that higher levels are needed (Matter 2+), sometimes it lists all possible ranks (Matter 2/3/4). And sometimes it picks a rank somewhere in the middle (Matter 3), and if you aren\u2019t already familiar with the rules you wouldn\u2019t realize that there are lower rank options for simpler patterns.<br /> <br /> I also think the author sometimes forgot that Matter can transmute at a lower rank than the other Pattern spheres. I have no way of proving that, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The one thing I can think of that would make this make sense would be to require Prime 2 to allow this type of conjuration would be if Matter 3/Prime 2+Quintessence (actually spending one or more points of Quintessence) allows creation of a permanent object, but Matter 3/Prime 2/Spirit 3 (and no expenditure of Quintessence) allows conjuration of a temporary object. I'm not yet conviced that this is a good approach, though, or supported by other text.<br /> <br /> Especially since conjuration using Spirit would seem to require having an ephemeral object to begin with (so you need to find the spiritual counterpart of the object you want) rather than trying to conjure from nothing. If you had to create the ephemera from nothing at all, you'd be back to needing Prime (if you're interpreting the rules as needing Prime for conjuration from nothing even if Quitessence is not expended). </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I like the permanence option, but that\u2019s not usually how permanence is achieved.<br /> <br /> One thought, though. While spirit transmutation is described entirely in terms of converting a material thing into its spiritual counterpart, and vice versa, it should also be capable of converting one ephemeral object into another. If a player asked me at what rank they could turn a spiritual stone into a spiritual sword, I\u2019d say Spirit 3. So I think Spirit 3/Matter 2+ allows a mage to turn any ephemeral object into any physical object.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T07:49:38-07:00","id":1514012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1514008#post1514008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, when I look at the wordings in M20, what I see is that quintessence isn\u2019t being transformed into patterns, it is the substance that the patterns are woven with. The opening description of Prime casts quintessence as the baseline energy that fuels the patterns of other forms. Prime 2 describes diverting quintessence into patterns, not transforming it. Indeed, most of Prime describes handling quintessence in terms of moving it around \u2013 drawing, draining, infusing, etc. Nor is this language new to M20. The implication is that Prime isn\u2019t transforming quintessence, it is channeling it.<br /> <br /> To use an art analogy, if the pattern is the image you draw on the page, the quintessence is the lead you draw it with. The lead isn\u2019t transformed in the process, just arranged in specific ways to make the drawing. Erasing the drawing doesn\u2019t change the drawing back into lead, it just destroys the arrangement thereof. The quintessence never stops being quintessence, it just gets bound into other things.<br /> <br /> So I maintain that Prime 2 is used to pull or induce quintessence into a pattern, which is necessary for creation effects, but not for disintegration ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if this description of how it works is true, it still doesn\u2019t mean that wiping that pattern away can be achieved without Prime. You can reasonably say that erasing the pattern is easier, and doesn\u2019t require Prime, but I can say that it isn\u2019t easier and does require Prime if I prefer.<br /> <br /> An interesting thing about this, for Mage, is that both interpretations - transforming Quintessence into matter, or arranging Quintessence into a pattern, or indeed transforming Quintessence into a pattern - can each be equally true, and highly enlightened mages can debate over which is the truth of the universe. We only need to settle on the mechanic that we\u2019re going to use right now to run our games (separately - we don\u2019t need to agree and do the same thing).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1514008#post1514008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. I like the permanence option, but that\u2019s not usually how permanence is achieved.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1514008#post1514008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thought, though. While spirit transmutation is described entirely in terms of converting a material thing into its spiritual counterpart, and vice versa, it should also be capable of converting one ephemeral object into another. If a player asked me at what rank they could turn a spiritual stone into a spiritual sword, I\u2019d say Spirit 3. So I think Spirit 3/Matter 2+ allows a mage to turn any ephemeral object into any physical object.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly Spirit Sphere doesn\u2019t mention transmuting one spiritual object into another because spiritual objects cannot routinely be transmuted that way. Perhaps the spirit world resists such changes. Perhaps that as spirits are concepts perceived, it isn\u2019t meaningful to transform a spirit that way.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, perhaps not. But if a Spirit-using mage wants to transform an ephemeral stone into a material sword, I\u2019d probably require more successes. It\u2019s a more drastic transformation, after all.<br /> <br /> Spirit 5 does say: \u201cThe Spirit Master is now able to command ephemera itself, creating, challenging, and destroying spirit matter as he Wills.\u201d Yes, challenging. I submit that that is an autocarrot error. It undoubtedly should be \u201cchanging\u201d. But you could justify reserving transmutation of spirit matter to Spirit 5 if you want.<br /> <br /> And then there is Dimensional Science, that describes somewhat different abilities\u2026<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure that I would necessarily want a mage with Matter and Spirit to necessarily lose their ability to manipulate Matter when visiting another world via the use of Spirit, though. Although I could see myself desiring that in some realms.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T11:30:58-07:00","id":1514028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1514012#post1514012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if this description of how it works is true, it still doesn\u2019t mean that wiping that pattern away can be achieved without Prime. You can reasonably say that erasing the pattern is easier, and doesn\u2019t require Prime, but I can say that it isn\u2019t easier and does require Prime if I prefer.</div> </div> </div> </div>You certainly can, though the most important question shouldn\u2019t be how hard we think it should be, it should be what is each sphere doing. That\u2019s one the core ways I\u2019ve evaluated everything in this thread including this effect. I think it\u2019s a good practice at the table too, though obviously that is up to you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Possibly Spirit Sphere doesn\u2019t mention transmuting one spiritual object into another because spiritual objects cannot routinely be transmuted that way. Perhaps the spirit world resists such changes. Perhaps that as spirits are concepts perceived, it isn\u2019t meaningful to transform a spirit that way. </div> </div> </div>I had that thought, too. There\u2019s not much game benefit to treating ephemera that way, though, and all it really does is add the extra step of transmuting the ephemera to physical matter, changing that matter, and transmuting it back. Basically its a Spirit 3 surcharge with a complicated explanation. That's a lot of extra explanation.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Spirits themselves probably should be harder to affect than base ephemera. It\u2019s not really clear what rank you\u2019d need to change a Wolf Spirit into a Glass Spirit but it should be more difficult than just binding them. More on that in a moment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Spirit 5 does say: \u201cThe Spirit Master is now able to command ephemera itself, creating, challenging, and destroying spirit matter as he Wills.\u201d Yes, challenging. I submit that that is an autocarrot error. It undoubtedly should be \u201cchanging\u201d. But you could justify reserving transmutation of spirit matter to Spirit 5 if you want. </div> </div> </div>That is a very fair interpretation. I agree with you that its likely a typo. I\u2019ll submit one more possibility. Spirit 3 allows the transmutation of ephemeral things, Spirit 5 is necessary for changes to Spirits themselves. Thus changing a spiritual rock into a spiritual sword is Rank 3, but changing a Rock spirit into a Sword Spirit is rank 5. <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T21:10:22-07:00","id":1514076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1514028#post1514028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You certainly can, though the most important question shouldn\u2019t be how hard we think it should be, it should be what is each sphere doing. That\u2019s one the core ways I\u2019ve evaluated everything in this thread including this effect. I think it\u2019s a good practice at the table too, though obviously that is up to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's multiple ways of interpreting &quot;hard&quot;. I wasn't talking about difficulty number for the roll, or number of successes required (although you could go do things in that area too). It's reasonable to say that removing something from existence is harder by requiring certain knowledge, and a rating in a Sphere represents having gained that knowledge.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1514028#post1514028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI had that thought, too. There\u2019s not much game benefit to treating ephemera that way, though, and all it really does is add the extra step of transmuting the ephemera to physical matter, changing that matter, and transmuting it back. Basically its a Spirit 3 surcharge with a complicated explanation. That's a lot of extra explanation.</div> </div> </div> </div>It adds a requirement to have the Matter sphere (at a rating depending on the exact change required) in order to transmute ephemeral (non-living) matter.<br /> <br /> And to be frank, I don't want my PCs to visit an Otherworld, and in so doing have the Etherite's major abilities stop working and hand those abilities to the Dreamspeaker instead, just because Spirit was required to get there. Not every time, at any rate, though I can certainly see myself wanting to have spiritual realms where changing matter is meaningless because there isn't actually any matter there at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1514028#post1514028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit 3 allows the transmutation of ephemeral things, Spirit 5 is necessary for changes to Spirits themselves. Thus changing a spiritual rock into a spiritual sword is Rank 3, but changing a Rock spirit into a Sword Spirit is rank 5.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That is rather at odds with the statements about Spirit affecting spirits the way Life affects (non-spirit) living creatures. Although that does depend a bit on what it means to be a Rock Spirit or a Sword Spirit. (Is being a Sword Spirit different from being a spirit that has the form of a sword? If I transmute the ephemeral form of a Rock Spirit into the form of a Sword Spirit, does that just give me a Rock Spirit that looks like a Sword Spirit, rather than actually producing a Sword Spirit?)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T07:28:09-07:00","id":1514112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1514076#post1514076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's multiple ways of interpreting &quot;hard&quot;. I wasn't talking about difficulty number for the roll, or number of successes required (although you could go do things in that area too). It's reasonable to say that removing something from existence is harder by requiring certain knowledge, and a rating in a Sphere represents having gained that knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s your call, of course. M20 doesn\u2019t say that, though. It doesn\u2019t give any reason for the Prime 2 requirement, and it doesn\u2019t match Prime as written, so I\u2019m leaving it on the list as an improper combo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And to be frank, I don't want my PCs to visit an Otherworld, and in so doing have the Etherite's major abilities stop working and hand those abilities to the Dreamspeaker instead, just because Spirit was required to get there. Not every time, at any rate, though I can certainly see myself wanting to have spiritual realms where changing matter is meaningless because there isn't actually any matter there at all. </div> </div> </div>Officially (M20 pg 484-485) in most of the Umbra Matter and Life only work on objects and creatures that originated in the material world. For creatures and objects of the umbra, you need Spirit. You will probably need to house rule things here to get the game you want.<br /> <br /> For what it is worth, there are parts of that writeup I would house rule too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is rather at odds with the statements about Spirit affecting spirits the way Life affects (non-spirit) living creatures. Although that does depend a bit on what it means to be a Rock Spirit or a Sword Spirit. (Is being a Sword Spirit different from being a spirit that has the form of a sword? If I transmute the ephemeral form of a Rock Spirit into the form of a Sword Spirit, does that just give me a Rock Spirit that looks like a Sword Spirit, rather than actually producing a Sword Spirit?) </div> </div> </div>Yes. A spirit\u2019s shape is not the same thing as its domain/nature so changing the former doesn\u2019t change the latter. HDYDT even has a section on changing a spirit\u2019s form. I\u2019m not going to cite its suggested rules because, well, that book is a hot mess. However, we can tell from the example (making a demon look like a tormented soul and dropping it into hell to be hunted) that it is possible to change a spirit\u2019s form without changing its essence.<br /> <br /> Note, I\u2019m not trying to justify the possibility I gave as the official ruling. \u201cActs like Life or Matter on spirits\u201d is a very open ended statement.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 06-07-2023, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T11:14:38-07:00","id":1514121,"title":"","content":"That said I think we do have to use that statement (\u201cActs like Life or Matter on spirits\u201d) as an actual description of Spirit's capabilities. If we do, it closes up most of the holes in the Sphere by copying whatever pattern sphere best fits. Matter for ephemeral objects, Forces for ephemeral forces, and Life for spirits. It is consistent with what Matter and Forces say about transmuting between ephemera and the material<br /> <br /> It's not a problem free solution. We have to decide for ourselves which spirits count as simple life and which ones complex and we have to ignore what Spirit 5 says about forging ephemera. It largely works, though.<br /> <br /> The alternative is we ignore the line and try to extrapolate from what is written in the Spheres. Things get very odd that way. You can clearly change spirit into matter at rank 3, but you can't change spirit into spirit until rank 5... except as a part of the process of converting it to the material (at least by the wording in Forces). This method is counterintuitive, it directly contradicts the numerous times M20 says Spirit acts like Life and Matter, and I do not think this is how Spirit is meant to function.<br /> <br /> But...<br /> <br /> I suspect it may have been the intention at one point.<br /> <br /> Going back to the &quot;create short-lived objects from ephemera&quot; in Spirit 3, I think I misinterpreted the intended effect. I don't think this means create a physical object from ephemera, I think this is supposed to forge an ephemeral object. This tracks better with the wording which says the object is constructed \u201cas if\u201d it were material and that it fades away at the end of the duration. Now Spirit 3/Matter 3/Prime 2 is still a bad combination for creating an ephemeral object, but it is a reasonable combination for making a physical object and turning it into an ephemeral one. In a system where you can't create ephemeral objects until Spirit 5, this is a good workaround.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T01:57:05-07:00","id":1514560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1514112#post1514112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s your call, of course. M20 doesn\u2019t say that, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I keep saying that various things are \u201creasonable\u201d, rather than correct. There\u2019s a lot of possible interpretations that fit well with the written rules, but aren\u2019t actually mandated.<br /> <br /> And while annihilation doesn\u2019t get the same specific reasoning as creation-from-nothing on page 511, the rule book is pretty consistent about pegging annihilation to the same level of Prime as creation. I wouldn\u2019t say that it is entirely without support in the rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1514112#post1514112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Officially (M20 pg 484-485) in most of the Umbra Matter and Life only work on objects and creatures that originated in the material world. For creatures and objects of the umbra, you need Spirit. You will probably need to house rule things here to get the game you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, maybe not so much. I\u2019m good with Spirit being the go-to in the Umbra itself. It\u2019s when you get to Doissetep (and the world beyond it, not just the castle itself - and yes, I know the official metaplot destroyed it before Revised) or Narnia or whatever that I\u2019d prefer to give Matter and Forces mages a fair shake. Especially so if I wind up dealing with an alternate Earth accessed via Dimensional Science rather than Spirit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1514112#post1514112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. A spirit\u2019s shape is not the same thing as its domain/nature so changing the former doesn\u2019t change the latter. HDYDT even has a section on changing a spirit\u2019s form. I\u2019m not going to cite its suggested rules because, well, that book is a hot mess. However, we can tell from the example (making a demon look like a tormented soul and dropping it into hell to be hunted) that it is possible to change a spirit\u2019s form without changing its essence.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Ephemeral mutation? Yeah, but it isn\u2019t really clear about whether the spirit undergoes a change to its nature when its form is changed.<br /> <br /> But Ephemeral Mutation does mention Spirit 4 and Spirit 5 in that effect. Maybe the difference is that the Spirit 4 version just changes the appearance, but the Spirit 5 version changes the nature of a spirit.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, transforming a complex creature (other than themself) into an entirely different species requires Life 5, so that\u2019s a pretty convincing reason to require Spirit 5 to do similar to a spirit. Even if you\u2019re relying on the \u201cacts as Life\u201d bit, it\u2019s still a 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T05:05:05-07:00","id":1514680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1514560#post1514560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, maybe not so much. I\u2019m good with Spirit being the go-to in the Umbra itself. It\u2019s when you get to Doissetep (and the world beyond it, not just the castle itself - and yes, I know the official metaplot destroyed it before Revised) or Narnia or whatever that I\u2019d prefer to give Matter and Forces mages a fair shake. Especially so if I wind up dealing with an alternate Earth accessed via Dimensional Science rather than Spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you are good. Realms can and do have their own rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ephemeral mutation? Yeah, but it isn\u2019t really clear about whether the spirit undergoes a change to its nature when its form is changed.<br /> <br /> But Ephemeral Mutation does mention Spirit 4 and Spirit 5 in that effect. Maybe the difference is that the Spirit 4 version just changes the appearance, but the Spirit 5 version changes the nature of a spirit.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, transforming a complex creature (other than themself) into an entirely different species requires Life 5, so that\u2019s a pretty convincing reason to require Spirit 5 to do similar to a spirit. Even if you\u2019re relying on the \u201cacts as Life\u201d bit, it\u2019s still a 5. </div> </div> </div>Since the book doesn't really tell us, this is how I would adjudicate it:<br /> <br /> Spirits can have such a wide array of appearances, even among those of the same type, so I would say that most reasonable changes would be Spirit 2 or 4. By reasonable changes I mean changes that fit the spirit's nature/domain. Changing a pain spirit from a rabbit made from red electricity to a humanoid made of broken glass sounds massive, but both fit with the idea of pain so its an alteration. Changing a spirit to a form antithetical to its nature (changing that pain spirit into a fluffy bunny) would be Spirit 3 or 5 because even though it sounds like a smaller change it is transmuting the spirit out of type.<br /> <br /> And as you say, changing a spirit's essence is definitely akin to changing a creature's species, which is Life 3 or 5 so it becomes Spirit 3 or 5.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 06-13-2023, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T10:28:43-07:00","id":1514716,"title":"","content":"Two more oddities I've come across.<br /> <br /> Seeing Weak Spots<br /> <br /> Entropy has the ability to see weak points. This seems to come in three flavors:<br /> <br /> Entropy 2+ to reduce the Durability of objects, armor ratings, etc. by 2 per success in addition to any damage. Pg 440 and (with diminished effect) pg 601<br /> <br /> Entropy 1 to reduce difficulty of a future attack roll. Pg 416<br /> <br /> Entropy 1 to do absolutely nothing. Entropy is still used to see weak points, but there are no mechanical effects and the rest of the spheres alone could accomplish the effect. Pg 415, pg 563. <br /> <br /> <br /> Durability and Transmutation<br /> <br /> It's not stated in the Casting Spells Step by Step section or in the quick charts, but apparently to transmute objects you need to overcome durability at a cost of 1 success per 1-2 durability (the section says 1, but then says Matter lets it be 2 and all object transmutations involve Matter. I haven't been able to find an equivalent requirement for overcoming soak in order to transmute living creatures, though transmuting vampires apparently requires overcoming health levels for... reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T09:10:17-07:00","id":1514966,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I scanned through M20 for Spirit examples like I did for Prime:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#538135\">Green is for effects that fit the writeup.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#c00000\">Red is for effects that have something wrong. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">Purple is for abilities that are apparently intended but not clearly written in the Spirit writeup</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">417 \u2013 The Spirit sphere can be used to soak a spirit\u2019s Rage based damage.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">418 \u2013 See invisible spirits</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">418 \u2013 Spirit 2 is required to touch most spirits, even in the Umbra. Restated in multiple places. The way Spirit 2 is written it is easy to miss that this is an all the time thing.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">418 - Spirit 3 allows for a Life 3 type attack but on spirits</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">418 \u2013 Spirit 2/Prime 2 acts like Life magic on umbral entities. Doesn\u2019t really make sense. The way everything else is written, Spirit 2 alone should be like Life 2 for umbral entities.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">443 \u2013 Spirit 3 to rouse the spirit of a drug.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">443 \u2013 Spirit 3/Life 3 to rouse the spirit of a disease in someone else\u2019s body. The Life requirement is sketchy. The only way this makes sense is if we consider the disease to be part of the pattern of the person, in which case it requires Life 4+.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">475 \u2013 Spirit 3 to step sideways, Spirit 4 to open a gateway. Both effects convert the travelers to ephemera and back.</span> <span style=\"color:#c00000\">However, apparently if someone opens a portal for a Mage, they still need Spirit 4 to use it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">477 \u2013 Mind 4 or 5/Spirit 3/Prime 2 for an Astral Soujourn. As I covered in the prime sphere, this essentially forges an ephemeral body and projects a mind into it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">478 \u2013 Spirit 2 to see across the gauntlet.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">478 \u2013 Entropy 4/Spirit 3(4)/Life 2(3) for travel to the underworld by dying but staying tethered to your body. How well this works depends a great deal on what\u2019s happening. The target is taken killed so that their spirit goes to the Underworld, while magic keeps their body alive so they can return. The Spirit requirements make sense because this is crossing into one of the Umbra\u2019s. Theoretically it isn\u2019t involved in getting the spirit to the Underworld, as that can happen without magic, but it is necessary to come back. Life is keeping the body alive while dead, essentially killing and healing at the same time. Life 2(3) is the right combo for both.</span> <span style=\"color:#c00000\">Entropy is the odd one, but either it is contributing to keeping the body alive, which Life is already doing, or it is a necessary part of opening a path out of the Underworld. </span><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">The second one actually works but there's no explanation of why it is the rank it is.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">479 \u2013 Spirit 4 cannot ward against the Avatar Storm</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">479 \u2013 Prime 3/Spirit 2 to use a familiar or Totem to shield from the Avatar Storm. Spirit 4/Prime 3 to force one. Spirit 2 was probably chosen because that\u2019s the level to manipulate the Gauntlet. Spirit 4 is necessary to command a spirit.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">480 \u2013 Entropy 5/Spirit (or Mind) 5 to move outside the Underworld during the Agama Soujourn. That appears to be an arbitrary rank increase. It gives credence to the idea that the Agama Sougourn uses Entropy to open the way to the Underworld, but if so, Spirit 5 and Entropy 5 are too high here.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">485 \u2013 Spirit 3 to step through Pericarps (Realm Gauntlets). Individual realms might use different spheres. Realms do sometimes have their own rules so that works.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">485 \u2013 Spirit works like Life against umbral creatures and Matter on umbral objects.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">486 \u2013 Not an ability. Spirits often appear as what the viewer effects and may look different to different people. Masters of Spirit apparently understand that a Spirit\u2019s identity comes from what it does, what mask it wears, and what deals it makes.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">489 \u2013 Make a fetish.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">489 \u2013 Spirit 2 is required to communicate with most spirits.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">490 \u2013 Spirit can countermagic certain spirit attacks.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">494 \u2013 High powered Spirit or Entropy magic is necessary to break down a pattern web.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">494 \u2013 Spirit 4/Life 3/Prime 2 is an Exorcism. Spirit 4 is the correct rank and the spirit is part of the pattern at this point so Life also makes sense.</span> <span style=\"color:#c00000\">Prime is superfluous. My guess is it was added for a flair of \u2018holiness.\u2019</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">508 \u2013 Life 3/Spirit 2 to heal a werecreature. Why this is only Spirit 2, I don\u2019t know. It\u2019s Spirit 3 to heal a spirit.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">508 \u2013 Life 4/Spirit 4/Prime 3 to revive the recently dead. What is Prime doing? Life is too high a rank, it is presumably healing the body and that can happen at Life 3</span><span style=\"color:#538135\">. I was going to complain about Spirit 4, but that is the same rank it takes to bring a ghost out of the underworld according to the Agama Sojourn. Spirit is the only thing right in this effect.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">508 \u2013 Awaken object\u2019s spirit.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">508 \u2013 Spirit 3 to conjure a spirit. Does this mean pull a spirit into the physical world or summon it to a location? Either way, this is a Spirit 4 spell.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">508 \u2013 Prime 4/Spirit 4 to drain a spirit\u2019s essence. These numbers are off. Prime should be able to do this on its own at 5, but it should only be 3 if using Spirit to convert the spirit to quintessence. Indeed on page 521 this is Spirit 2/Prime 3, which is correct for Prime but not Spirit. As best I can tell this should be Spirit 3/Prime 3.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">509 \u2013 Spirit 2/Mind 1 to conceal an Avatar. Odd combo. Presumably Spirit 2 is a Lull Spirit effect, so the rank is correct.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">509 \u2013 Spirit 1 to see Auras.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">509 \u2013 Mind 3/Prime 2/Spirit 1 to see an Avatar. What even is happening here? Spirit 1 is at least the right rank for sensory magic, so that is something.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">516 \u2013 Spirit 3/Forces 3 to convert spirit stuff into physical energy. This reinforces the statement on 485.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">517 \u2013 Life 5/Spirit 3 or 5 to create a body and instill it with spirits. This should be Spirit 4 or 5, not 3 or 5.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">517 \u2013 Matter and Spirit converts Matter to Ephemera or vice versa. No ranks given. This reinforces the statement on 485.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">518 \u2013 Matter 2/Spirit 3 to convert ephemera into matter or matter to ephemera. This reinforces the statement on 485.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">518 \u2013 Matter 2/Spirit 3 to awaken the spirit of an object. Nonsense, this is Spirit 3 alone.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">523 \u2013 Time 4 and Spirit to trap a spiritual thing in a bubble of time. Presumably this is a locking effect, though I\u2019m not sure locking is necessary.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">545 \u2013 When casting on something on the other side of the gauntlet, the difficulty is the gauntlet rating.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">547 \u2013 Spirit is optionally necessary to counter werecreature gifts and Wraith arcanoi.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">608 \u2013 An alternate to Data and Mind for psychically interfacing with computers.</span></span><br /> \u200b</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T23:03:48-07:00","id":1515625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph;n1511he 795</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind 4/5 allows one to make an astral projection, and astral projections</div> </div> </div> </div>The different and various types of Wizardy / Magick could definitely and clearly be used for researching, creating, practicing, and casting a Casting / Change / Result/ Effect that could be identified and defined as belonging and contributing to classifications and categories related to / about :<br /> <br /> Spiritual travel soul wandering, psyche sending, or astral projedction.<br /> For example Prime, Spirit, Time, Correspondence, or Life could be considered, used, and developed in regard to this type and category of special ability Certainly Magick types, kinds, and categories are clearly defined and described and they are most often also drawn painted or sketched throught World of Darkness and Vampire : the Masquerade role playing games.<br /> <br /> There is the notable and unique quality or trait that the Spellcasters \\ Mages in the World of Darkness are also very often sketched and pictured as having outright striking or perfect physical appearance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 06-20-2023, 02:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T02:52:05-07:00","id":1515839,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone, nice to meet you all and a pleasure being here.<br /> <br /> So, Im so glad Ramnesis brought this up. I always felt that the writers dont understand their own material. <br /> <br /> I always felt that, writers of games like Gurps or D&amp;D and others, they are too &quot;detail driven&quot;, creating tons of rules for every tiny little thing and what not.<br /> <br /> However, the writers of WoD were just an explosion of Glamour - an endless burst of creativity power in raw form.<br /> <br /> But all of this creativity has never came with much structure... Too much creativity chaos, too little order.<br /> <br /> The games of WoD are amazing, the themes, the motifis, the ideas, simply incredible but... They absolutely lack structure and internal consistency. Which is why they are a total mess.<br /> <br /> The vast majority of effects for Spheres are absolutely random. It feels that, the writers created the Spheres because some changelling muse infused them with letal doses of glamour, but after that they werent able to understand what they had created.<br /> <br /> I will take a look in all that list because I too dont agree with some 95% of the stupid effects ever published. The books just make me so mad that I just decided to ignore them all completely. <br /> <br /> The writers just go for the &quot;feeling&quot; of the effects, rather than the logic of them. For example is every single effect ever published that uses &quot;psychic powers&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, to the writers, because it is &quot;psychic&quot;, then it must use Mind sphere because... err... I dont know... because psychic powers come from the mind?<br /> <br /> What level of mind do you say? Err.... I dont know... 2? Maybe 3? Perhaps 4? I dont know.... If it &quot;feels&quot; too powerful, make it 3 or 4, if not maybe 2 or 3...<br /> <br /> Likewise it is the same for &quot;Chi magic&quot;. Oh, so you're a monk that channels Chi for magic? That's Prime.<br /> <br /> Do you wanna heal using Chi? Prime + Life<br /> Do you need to channel Chi to read minds? Prime + Mind<br /> Do you need to channel Chi to open portals? Prime + Correspondence <br /> <br /> AND THIS IS SOOOOOOOO DUMB.<br /> <br /> The writers of WoD are perhaps one of the best examples of utterly dumb genius people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T03:52:14-07:00","id":1515845,"title":"","content":"And even on the very description of the Spheres there's idiotic dumb stuff. For instance, why the &quot;lock on&quot; effect (for example, Correspondence + Life to &quot;teleport&quot; pieces of the target) requires the lvl 2 of the Sphere? What does lvl 2 do in such a case?<br /> <br /> Let's see generally:<br /> Level 1 overall is Sense and Measure <br /> Level 2 overall is &quot;Control and Diversion. &quot;<br /> Level 3 is &quot;Command and Simple Creation&quot;<br /> Level 4 is &quot;Authority&quot;<br /> And Level 5 is &quot;Complete Power&quot;<br /> (I can explain better those if anyone wishes).<br /> <br /> Now, to me a &quot;lock on&quot; effect seems more like a Level 1 kind of stuff, does it not? As in &quot;Sense and Measure&quot; a Pattern?<br /> <br /> Correspondence: I hate how this Sphere is written. It's total nonsensical. Why do you need &quot;same level of other sphere&quot; to aport things?<br /> <br /> Also, what sense does it make to have you using Corr 2 to for example teleport plants by adding Life 2, if Teleport is only Corr 3? <br /> <br /> Seriously, Aport effects should be Corr 3 (which is Teleport) and a lvl 1 Sphere (or &quot;Detect [X]&quot;).<br /> <br /> But even that I dont fully agree; teleporting is just a Space manipulation; if you were shrinking the body of a person for example, then I would agree &quot;ok, you need Life 1&quot;. But no, Teleport is JUST Space manipulation. You are &quot;pulling&quot; someone over a &quot;wormhole&quot;. That's it. You're not affecting the Life Pattern AT ALL. That effect is no different than pushing somebody through a door.<br /> <br /> Which leads us to Corr 4, further proving my point. With Corr 4, you create a &quot;portal&quot;, creating a &quot;sustainable wormhole&quot; between 2 points. No other spheres needed to push stuff through that.<br /> <br /> And no, &quot;Aport&quot; should never be Corr 2. That's just Teleport. Once again, it feels the writers went with their feelings rather than logical thinking (too much Glamour with not enough Banality to ground all that creativity in reality). Corr 2 should be the typical trope of &quot;crystal balls&quot; only (see stuff far away).<br /> <br /> Following the general guideline for what each lvl should do, lvl 1 Corr is perfect - Detect and Measure. Thus, &quot;feeling spaces&quot;. Althought I think that stretching your senses to cover large areas may be a bit much, but ok.<br /> <br /> For all of those that watched Batman: The Dark Knight (99% of the population over 30 years old at least), remember that &quot;Sonar Vision&quot; that Batman developed? Ok, so that's what Corr 1 is. It's basically &quot;sonar vision&quot; with 360 degrees (only that by itself is already insanely powerful). That was the system developed by Fox. Then, Corr 2 would be the upgraded version of that system, the machine that Bruce Wayne built, capable of applying that sonar concept to EVERY single cellphone of Gotham, to find the Joker. That's Corr 2 (with Entropy 1 to be able to detect the Joker specifically from all the millions of phones).<br /> <br /> And there's several other cases more, where the description of the spheres themselves dont make sense, let alone the effects. Forces may be the most egregious example. So, the rules say that, the strenght of an effect is a matter of &quot;number of successes&quot; right?<br /> <br /> Well, what's the difference between the highly subjective &quot;minor&quot; and &quot;major&quot; forces? What's the difference between a gentle breeze and a hurricane if not for the intensity - which should be translated into 1 success versus 10+ successes for the same effect?<br /> <br /> Which is why I divided Forces between electromagnetic, kinetic, light and thermal energies as &quot;minor forces&quot; and gravity and radiation as &quot;major&quot; forces to make sense of it.<br /> <br /> And dont even let me start with Prime, that's an utter mess.<br /> <br /> Im not with much time right now, but I always wanted to revise all these inconsistencies, I'll return to this later on","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T06:27:45-07:00","id":1515943,"title":"","content":"The problem I\u2019ve had with this entire thread is figuring out what is the correct interpretation. It\u2019s not as simple as saying the Sphere writeups are king and everything else is only as valid as it accords with them. The Sphere writeups themselves are wrong and often contradictory. You're hitting on several of the major issues here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1515845#post1515845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now, to me a &quot;lock on&quot; effect seems more like a Level 1 kind of stuff, does it not? As in &quot;Sense and Measure&quot; a Pattern?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of M20s big problems. The Locking section never says what rank locking is. All of M20s examples seem to use Sphere 2, so I\u2019ve been using that on the assumption that it is an intended but unstated rule.<br /> <br /> For the purposes of keeping the spell locked on, you are right that it makes sense you should only need to be able to sense the anchor. The only counter I have to that is that locking has two effects: keeping the spell locked on a target, and freeing it up so the mage doesn\u2019t have to concentrate on it. Sensory magic really shouldn\u2019t do the latter, though outside of an arbitrary ruling I can\u2019t say why Rank 2 of a pattern sphere would either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Correspondence: I hate how this Sphere is written. It's total nonsensical. Why do you need &quot;same level of other sphere&quot; to aport things?<br /> <br /> Also, what sense does it make to have you using Corr 2 to for example teleport plants by adding Life 2, if Teleport is only Corr 3?<br /> <br /> Seriously, Aport effects should be Corr 3 (which is Teleport) and a lvl 1 Sphere (or &quot;Detect [X]&quot;). </div> </div> </div>I think the basic idea is that bringing stuff to yourself (Rank 2) is easier that bringing yourself to something else (Rank 3), which is easier than moving anything to any other thing (Rank 4). The size limits on Rank 2 don\u2019t make sense except for game balance reasons.<br /> <br /> Not that the Correspondence section actually makes this clear. Instead it is a hash of contradictions, at one point saying you only have to add pattern spheres if you are teleporting part of a pattern, then later saying you have to add them if you want to teleport any other pattern). I go with the clearly stated rule in the base Correspondence section that you only ever need to add pattern spheres if you are teleporting part of a pattern.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But even that I dont fully agree; teleporting is just a Space manipulation; if you were shrinking the body of a person for example, then I would agree &quot;ok, you need Life 1&quot;. But no, Teleport is JUST Space manipulation. You are &quot;pulling&quot; someone over a &quot;wormhole&quot;. That's it. You're not affecting the Life Pattern AT ALL. That effect is no different than pushing somebody through a door. </div> </div> </div>I wouldn\u2019t even agree with the shrinking example. If all you are doing is manipulating the space they take up (such that it feels the same to them but for everyone else it is smaller, Tardis style), you shouldn\u2019t even need Life. Only if you are somehow messing with the pattern itself would Life be necessary.<br /> <br /> This, by the way, is the main argument why Correspondence can't make direct attacks. Direct correspondence attacks would mean actual pattern alterations and Correspondence needs Pattern spheres to make pattern alterations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And there's several other cases more, where the description of the spheres themselves dont make sense, let alone the effects. Forces may be the most egregious example. So, the rules say that, the strenght of an effect is a matter of &quot;number of successes&quot; right?<br /> <br /> Well, what's the difference between the highly subjective &quot;minor&quot; and &quot;major&quot; forces? What's the difference between a gentle breeze and a hurricane if not for the intensity - which should be translated into 1 success versus 10+ successes for the same effect?<br /> <br /> Which is why I divided Forces between electromagnetic, kinetic, light and thermal energies as &quot;minor forces&quot; and gravity and radiation as &quot;major&quot; forces to make sense of it. </div> </div> </div>I agree with you completely on this one. Most of Forces' limitations on size and successes appear to be hacks to get around problems with the system. It often seems to be more hacks than actual substance.<br /> <br /> I think that division of minor vs major forces is actually supposed to be in the game too. I\u2019d have to check but I think it is in Revised but somehow was left out of M20.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T10:34:48-07:00","id":1515954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1515943#post1515943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem I\u2019ve had with this entire thread is figuring out what is the correct interpretation. It\u2019s not as simple as saying the Sphere writeups are king and everything else is only as valid as it accords with them. The Sphere writeups themselves are wrong and often contradictory. You're hitting on several of the major issues here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I havent even got to Prime yet...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is one of M20s big problems. The Locking section never says what rank locking is. All of M20s examples seem to use Sphere 2, so I\u2019ve been using that on the assumption that it is an intended but unstated rule.<br /> <br /> For the purposes of keeping the spell locked on, you are right that it makes sense you should only need to be able to sense the anchor. The only counter I have to that is that locking has two effects: keeping the spell locked on a target, and freeing it up so the mage doesn\u2019t have to concentrate on it. Sensory magic really shouldn\u2019t do the latter, though outside of an arbitrary ruling I can\u2019t say why Rank 2 of a pattern sphere would either. </div> </div> </div>I didnt understand what you mean by &quot;feeing it up&quot; (on the &quot;lock on&quot; effect), could you please clarify?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the basic idea is that bringing stuff to yourself (Rank 2) is easier that bringing yourself to something else (Rank 3), which is easier than moving anything to any other thing (Rank 4). The size limits on Rank 2 don\u2019t make sense except for game balance reasons. </div> </div> </div>And that's my problem with it all. Like I say, the writers of WoD had bursts of creativity, but no organizational structure. They needed somebody to turn all that raw creativity into an organized thought.<br /> <br /> Higher sphere levels are NOT (or rather, should not be) about it being &quot;harder&quot;, but rather MORE COMPLEX.<br /> <br /> Creating a grass the size of a building that is hard as steel is much harder than engaging in astral projection, but astral projection is more complex.<br /> <br /> And, there's already rules adressing difficulty. It's the rules for numbers of targets, size of feat and correspondence reach.<br /> <br /> That goes into another problem I have in Life and Prime. Healing (Self) is Life 2, while Healing (Other) is Life 3. Again, that's also entirely wrong, because the reasoning given is that &quot;it's easier&quot; to heal yourself - again, the same problem. Correlating difficulty of a feat with complexity, when they absolutely are NOT the same.<br /> <br /> And the rules already adress that. You dont need any additional successes for affecting yourself. For each additional target, you need 1 success. Bam! Healing yourself is easier already, problem solved. It makes no sense for the same effect to be a lvl bellow just because the target is &quot;self&quot;.<br /> <br /> Likewise, &quot;pushing&quot; things to you or &quot;pulling yourself&quot; into another place is ALL Teleportation. You may argue that there's a difference in difficulty - but that's NOT a difference in complexity. It's all teleport still.<br /> <br /> And difference in difficulty is already adressed in the rules: you just require more successes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not that the Correspondence section actually makes this clear. Instead it is a hash of contradictions, at one point saying you only have to add pattern spheres if you are teleporting part of a pattern, then later saying you have to add them if you want to teleport any other pattern). I go with the clearly stated rule in the base Correspondence section that you only ever need to add pattern spheres if you are teleporting part of a pattern. </div> </div> </div>Nothing about it is clear - or make any sense<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that division of minor vs major forces is actually supposed to be in the game too. I\u2019d have to check but I think it is in Revised but somehow was left out of M20.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>Yes, Minor/Major forces were in both 2e and rev\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T11:03:19-07:00","id":1515955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1515954#post1515954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didnt understand what you mean by &quot;feeing it up&quot; (on the &quot;lock on&quot; effect), could you please clarify?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are difficulty penalties for having too many spells active, but they don't apply to spells that are on a trigger or are locked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Higher sphere levels are NOT (or rather, should not be) about it being &quot;harder&quot;, but rather MORE COMPLEX.<br /> <br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>I actually did mean more complex not more difficult. Each of those steps is arguably more complex than the last. It doesn't have to be, but I could imagine up an explanation for why it is. Also I can come up for a reason for why teleporting a beer bottle to yourself is less complicated than teleporting a person:<br /> <br /> At Correspondence 2 mages get the ability to manipulate things at a distance. That is, they can move them about with their bare hands, but at a distance. That's essentially what the Affect Distant Object is on page 509. It doesn't use Forces or any other sphere because the Mage is essentially doing it manually. I think teleporting small objects is taking that one step further and holding on to the object when they pull their hand back. The size limit then is the size limit for what the mage can easily manipulate with one hand. <br /> <br /> Is that the actual explanation? No idea. It tracks with the complexity step ups, though. Teleporting small objects falls under Reach Through Space, teleporting yourself falls under Open and Close Gates, and teleporting others is Rending Space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T15:24:46-07:00","id":1515969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1515955#post1515955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are difficulty penalties for having too many spells active, but they don't apply to spells that are on a trigger or are locked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Errr.... That's NOT multiple spells however... That's just a single one.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter how many Sphere's I throw into an effect, if it's condensed into a single effect, it's a single spell.<br /> <br /> For example, if I throw Time 4 Entropy 2 to set a huge series of triggers into a Ward, for example, I add Matter 2/Life 5/Mind 2 to &quot;turn anyone depressed entering the are into a statue of gold&quot;, but with another trigger I throw in Forces 3/Prime 4/Mind 2 to &quot;electrocute anyone that is happy&quot; and I throw in Life 5/Mind 2 to &quot;turn anyone angry into a butterfly&quot; and I call this effect the &quot;Ward of multiple madness containing and weird punishments&quot;, all of that is a SINGLE effect. All of that is a SINGLE spell.<br /> <br /> Having multiple spells means keeping your mental shield against mental attacks up, while you keep your &quot;increased lucky zone&quot; and your ethereal lightsaber is ignited, all at once. Those are different &quot;spells&quot;.<br /> <br /> In the case of the Apport, the &quot;teleport&quot; part and the &quot;lock on&quot; part are NOT two different spells, but just parts of the same effect, the same spell. You are not &quot;locking&quot; a target and then teleporting it, you're doing it all at once.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I actually did mean more complex not more difficult. Each of those steps is arguably more complex than the last. It doesn't have to be, but I could imagine up an explanation for why it is. Also I can come up for a reason for why teleporting a beer bottle to yourself is less complicated than teleporting a person:<br /> <br /> At Correspondence 2 mages get the ability to manipulate things at a distance. That is, they can move them about with their bare hands, but at a distance. That's essentially what the Affect Distant Object is on page 509. It doesn't use Forces or any other sphere because the Mage is essentially doing it manually. I think teleporting small objects is taking that one step further and holding on to the object when they pull their hand back. The size limit then is the size limit for what the mage can easily manipulate with one hand.<br /> <br /> Is that the actual explanation? No idea. It tracks with the complexity step ups, though. Teleporting small objects falls under Reach Through Space, teleporting yourself falls under Open and Close Gates, and teleporting others is Rending Space. </div> </div> </div>It's still Teleporting thou. That's the thing, you're not actually doing anything more complex. You're moving object X from point A to point B in an instant. That's teleporting.<br /> <br /> Here you're making the same mistake as the writers: you are confusing scale with complexity. So, what's the limit here? A staff? Just some small items that fit inside the wizard's hand? So, could he now theoretically increase the size of his hands with Life to grab bigger items? Is the size of your hands some sort of arcane, universal measure to which Consensus itself bends to?<br /> <br /> Or is it a matter of his Strenght, in which case he could again increase it with Life?<br /> <br /> No, that's not complexity. That's difficulty.<br /> <br /> Manipulating things at a distance is not the same as breaching the distance. &quot;Affect Distant Objects&quot; is different from &quot;Teleportation&quot;. Now, if you're strong enough, you could lift a car over your head. Could you then &quot;Apport&quot; a car? Because, if you have the Strenght to lift it, you can certainly do it at a distance using Corr 2.<br /> <br /> No. The difference between teleporting a coin and a skyscraper is the difference between 1 single success and 20+ successes.<br /> <br /> The difference between teleporting something from Scandinavian to you or to Japan is 0 extra successes since target (self) is 0 successes, and instead to Japan is extra successes needed based on the Correspondence table (on top of what was already needed to reach Scandinavian in the first place).<br /> <br /> But it's all still teleport.<br /> <br /> Corr 4 is different, is not changing the places of stuff, but rather opening wholes in space, creating &quot;wormholes&quot; or &quot;gates&quot;.<br /> <br /> Why not just using teleport? Because a teleport is an &quot;instant spell&quot;. As soon as you used it, it's done. If you forgot something, you need a new teleport.<br /> <br /> The Gate on the other hand can be used any time while it lasts, with a single spell. No need to keep recasting it. That's added complexity.<br /> <br /> Manipulate at distance <br /> Teleport<br /> Wormholes<br /> == Complexity<br /> <br /> &quot;Teleport small stuff&quot;<br /> &quot;Teleport big stuff&quot;<br /> == Dificulty","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T19:39:43-07:00","id":1515980,"title":"","content":"And all of this is why, when M5 eventually comes out, I will be able to forgive a <i>lot </i>of faults if they rework the Spheres and take cues from <b>Mage: the Awakening</b> when doing so.<br /> <br /> I <i>like</i> the way that <b>Awakening</b>'s Space Arcanum (its counterpart to Correspondence) pays so much attention to Sympathetic Links, and not just in terms of how they overcome distance. The Fate and Death Arcana have a lot more logic to their progressions than the Entropy Sphere does. <i>All</i> of the Arcana are more useful than their Sphere counterparts because you can actually <i>do </i>something with one dot in them. And all of them are more self-sufficient, with Conjunctional Effects being rare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-24-2023, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T19:55:52-07:00","id":1518475,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> any plan to do the Technocracy Spheres?<br /> <br /> <br /> (love the thread by the way)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T08:25:27-07:00","id":1518530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1515980#post1515980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And all of this is why, when M5 eventually comes out, I will be able to forgive a <i>lot </i>of faults if they rework the Spheres and take cues from <b>Mage: the Awakening</b> when doing so.<br /> <br /> I <i>like</i> the way that <b>Awakening</b>'s Space Arcanum (its counterpart to Correspondence) pays so much attention to Sympathetic Links, and not just in terms of how they overcome distance. The Fate and Death Arcana have a lot more logic to their progressions than the Entropy Sphere does. <i>All</i> of the Arcana are more useful than their Sphere counterparts because you can actually <i>do </i>something with one dot in them. And all of them are more self-sufficient, with Conjunctional Effects being rare.</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as I like MTAs background I\u2019m increasingly leaning towards just using Awakenings Arcana as well as it\u2019s spell casting system, already switched to its Rotes, Paradox and Quintessence use as it\u2019s far better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","user":"Arcanus","date":". 07-22-2023, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T13:22:30-07:00","id":1518563,"title":"","content":"Sometimes I think they add extra sphears just to make casting spells harder. for a game about being a mage they really discourage useing magic. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3647-eric-ericson","name":"Eric Ericson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T23:32:23-07:00","id":1518874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1515980#post1515980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And all of this is why, when M5 eventually comes out, I will be able to forgive a <i>lot </i>of faults if they rework the Spheres and take cues from <b>Mage: the Awakening</b> when doing so.<br /> <br /> I <i>like</i> the way that <b>Awakening</b>'s Space Arcanum (its counterpart to Correspondence) pays so much attention to Sympathetic Links, and not just in terms of how they overcome distance. The Fate and Death Arcana have a lot more logic to their progressions than the Entropy Sphere does. <i>All</i> of the Arcana are more useful than their Sphere counterparts because you can actually <i>do </i>something with one dot in them. And all of them are more self-sufficient, with Conjunctional Effects being rare.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had very much the opposite reaction. I find Entropy\u2019s progression to make far more sense. Entropy is the sphere of controlling end points. That is generally what Fate really means, and death is the ultimate end point of one\u2019s life. And the progression fits with this quite we<br /> <br /> 1: sense fate, lets you see omens, get a sense of endpoints, how significant things or events or people are to one\u2019s fate, as well as when one deviates from one\u2019s fate. Sensing disorder or weakpoints feeds in to this, as they are an omen towards the endpoint of the items destruction. You may also sense when something someone says does not align with fate, as per the zone of truth rote.<br /> <br /> 2: manipulate purely random events: This is because randomness has no \u201cfate\u201d associated with it. So your magic may be used to force an endpoint without clashing with the established fate there.<br /> <br /> 3: manipulate predictable events: at this level you can begin to manipulate events with simple fates, anything predictable such as the workings of a machine, when trains happen to leave, sudden meetings with friends, objects going missing, the likelihood of being caught while hiding. Anything which fate guides towards a specific and determined endpoint you can change or alter.<br /> <br /> 4: manipulate complex events: now your understanding of Entropy lets you manipulate more complex fates, things which are harder to predict but no less governed by that invisible hand, family curses, one\u2019s eventual profession, the fate of their children, the progression of disease, one\u2019s eventual death, the stock market exchange, one\u2019s personal narrative set against the grander scheme.<br /> <br /> 5: determine fate: at mastery level you can essentially manipulate the highest level of events, whereas before you could manipulate one\u2019s personal narrative, you may now dictate their narrative, determining their fate perhaps via a geas, also, you now can manipulate the grander scheme itself, you can affect the eventual outcome for whole cities or even nations, create narratives by ascending one person as the main character to a particular setting, or removing their importance in a role entirely, you can even shape how the population of a group reacts to particular events, and thereby shaping the end point of said event entirely.<br /> <br /> to me this makes a lot of sense in a way that Fate arcanum felt a bit\u2026lacking? <br /> <br /> also, I really found the Death arcanum to be rather laughable. It is often claimed to be a separation of Entropy\u2019s \u201cfate and death\u201d aspects, which as may be infered above I don\u2019t actually see as a dichotomy at all, but they realised Entropy itself doesn\u2019t actually have much Death specific stuff in there, so they had to scramble to incorporate Spirit and Forces effects to make the arcana even passable.<br /> <br /> personally I find it really silly that Awakening distinguishes between ghosts and spirits in such a mechanical way. Ascensions lets spirit interact with all of them without issue and that feels far more consistent. If it\u2019s ephemeral, it\u2019s spirit, done and dusted.<br /> <br /> and regarding conjunctional effects. I have tried to make them in awakening, and each time it has caused my ST to throw up a blue screen of death as they have no idea how to handle them. I wanted to use Space and Prime in order to determine the connections of a supernal object wonder equivalent (since they told me you need Prime to see supernal things so space isn\u2019t enough) and they didn\u2019t want to allow it because \u201cit would open the door to just using space with everything and then getting the mechanical advantage for using major arcanum on all effects\u201d<br /> <br /> another time I tried using Matter and Death to get a sense for which objects made of Jade were also anchors and was told \u201cno, those are two separate effects, you can use matter to check if something is jade, and you can use Death to feel anchors, and your gnosis is not high enough to combine spells, so you can\u2019t do both.\u201d<br /> <br /> Then there is the whole \u201cif the book doesn\u2019t say you can add Death to this Spirit rote to affect ghosts, then the spirit rote can not affect ghosts\u201d argument that makes me think some awakening players are almost incapable of off-book interpretations in a way that ascension not only allows but actively encourages.<br /> <br /> I admit this might because every awakening game I have ever played in was with a bad ST, but these are problems I have never experienced with Ascension","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T23:38:32-07:00","id":1518875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Ericson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1518563#post1518563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes I think they add extra sphears just to make casting spells harder. for a game about being a mage they really discourage useing magic.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hdydt is a bit of a departure from the usual philosophy of how the spheres combine to allow effects. Generally speaking, spheres are a means to include the manipulation of specific aspects of reality in to an effect. For each rote I like to ask \u201cwhat does each sphere contribute to the effect. How would the effect be possible if this sphere was reduced in rank, of missing that sphere entirely.\u201d<br /> <br /> for example, Clairvoyance with Corr 2 alone is essentially scrying, but if one wishes to read the minds of those they scry on, and thus reaching the \u201ctruer\u201d definition of clairvoyance, then adding Mind 1 would allow for sensing emotions, Mind 2 for sensing surface thoughts, and Mind 3 for sensing subconscious thoughts/memories. And it is the Mind 3 version of the rote which enables what is classically described as clairvoyance.<br /> <br /> While it does get a bit wibbly here, the wording on HDYDT\u2019s \u201cPerceiving from a distance\u201d here does imply that the limit of Corr effects on range, where you can only use spheres of the rank up to your corr rank to access the corr range table, is specific to effects which \u201ccommand\u201d from a distance, not sense.<br /> <br /> therefore, it is conceivable that Corr 2 Mind 3 would indeed be enough to read subconscious minds from a distance, but not manipulate their conscious thoughts (which would need you to have corr 3). Indeed, this would apply to any sensory effect done from a distance, they would only need the addition of corr 2 to pull off. However you would suffer the increase in difficulty for targeting things beyond sensory range without corr 3.<br /> <br /> If you have any other particular examples, I\u2019ll be haply to try and explain how I understand the sphere logic to play out. Though do allow that if they come from HDYDT, I might need to refer to previous editions to explain why I disagree with some of the decisions made for that book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 07-27-2023, 03:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T00:10:54-07:00","id":1518880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1518874#post1518874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had very much the opposite reaction. I find Entropy\u2019s progression to make far more sense. Entropy is the sphere of controlling end points. That is generally what Fate really means, and death is the ultimate end point of one\u2019s life. And the progression fits with this quite we<br /> <br /> <b>......</b><br /> <br /> to me this makes a lot of sense in a way that Fate arcanum felt a bit\u2026lacking?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not Dataweaver of course, but I think what they meant about logical progression has to do with internal consistency, not the external/philosophical one, where spell effects are organized into Practices, and you get access to the more complex Practices as you raise your Arcanum dots. (Made even clearer in 2e, where they snipped out things like &quot;Compelling spells are 1-dot, but radiation requires Forces 5&quot;, and hard-locked all Practices into dot levels)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> also, I really found the Death arcanum to be rather laughable. It is often claimed to be a separation of Entropy\u2019s \u201cfate and death\u201d aspects, which as may be infered above I don\u2019t actually see as a dichotomy at all, but they realised Entropy itself doesn\u2019t actually have much Death specific stuff in there, so they had to scramble to incorporate Spirit and Forces effects to make the arcana even passable.<br /> <br /> personally I find it really silly that Awakening distinguishes between ghosts and spirits in such a mechanical way. Ascensions lets spirit interact with all of them without issue and that feels far more consistent. If it\u2019s ephemeral, it\u2019s spirit, done and dusted. </div> </div> </div>This is more about what the setting establishes; calling it laughable or silly is highly subjective. Death is its own thing in that neighborhood, and so are ghosts. What's there is there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200b<br /> and regarding conjunctional effects. I have tried to make them in awakening, and each time it has caused my ST to throw up a blue screen of death as they have no idea how to handle them. I wanted to use Space and Prime in order to determine the connections of a supernal object wonder equivalent (since they told me you need Prime to see supernal things so space isn\u2019t enough) and they didn\u2019t want to allow it because \u201cit would open the door to just using space with everything and then getting the mechanical advantage for using major arcanum on all effects\u201d<br /> <br /> another time I tried using Matter and Death to get a sense for which objects made of Jade were also anchors and was told \u201cno, those are two separate effects, you can use matter to check if something is jade, and you can use Death to feel anchors, and your gnosis is not high enough to combine spells, so you can\u2019t do both.\u201d<br /> <br /> Then there is the whole \u201cif the book doesn\u2019t say you can add Death to this Spirit rote to affect ghosts, then the spirit rote can not affect ghosts\u201d argument that makes me think some awakening players are almost incapable of off-book interpretations in a way that ascension not only allows but actively encourages.<br /> <br /> I admit this might because every awakening game I have ever played in was with a bad ST, but these are problems I have never experienced with Ascension </div> </div> </div>Huh, your ST(s) must've been <i>really</i> confused.<br /> <br /> Seeing what connections (I presume sympathetic ones) a Supernal object has ought to be just Space 1, without Prime. Unless the 'connection' you're talking about is something like Resonance, which falls under Prime... and thus require just Prime 1, without Space. But... 1e was more restrictive on Arcana requirements, so I think that may have been the problem?<br /> <br /> Casting one Combined spell is doable at Gnosis 1 as of 2e, so I assume you were using 1e rules? Also, this isn't really about Conjunctional Arcana. It's about Combined spells. Different issue, as I see.<br /> <br /> Maybe I was dense, but I'm afraid I do not know of the last argument you mention in Awakening; I only know Ascension's rough equivalents of &quot;You're a shaman/psychic, so you must add Spirit/Mind&quot; comments that this thread seems to frown against. Generally, the book's creative/dynamic spell structure allows a mage to just... make up that exact spell, Rote or not, so I don't even understand why would someone argue that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T00:50:42-07:00","id":1518883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1518880#post1518880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe I was dense, but I'm afraid I do not know of the last argument you mention in Awakening; I only know Ascension's rough equivalents of &quot;You're a shaman/psychic, so you must add Spirit/Mind&quot; comments that this thread seems to frown against. Generally, the book's creative/dynamic spell structure allows a mage to just... make up that exact spell, Rote or not, so I don't even understand why would someone argue that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This point if rather overstated and in my opinion somewhat of a misinterpretation for how spheres relate to practice.<br /> <br /> any practice can be paired with any sphere combination, but certain sphere combinations allow one to perform the types of effects which are more in line with that practices\u2019s tropes.<br /> <br /> Without Spirit, a shaman may use Forces to encourage the spirits of fire to grow, move to avoid people, or strike specific targets. But with Spirit, they may also communicate with the spirits of fire, perhaps getting them to take the reigns of part of the effect and even act long after the shaman\u2019s magic has finished. In this case, Forces allows direct manipulation of fire, while Spirit allowed the spirit of fire to do the work as they may negotiate, the two together allows for both to be part of the same effect, control and communication. The shaman\u2019s practice allows this as they are in tune with the notion of spirits in all elements, and Forces is a way to manipulate the spirits of elements without directly breaching the gauntlet. Forces directs the mundane manifestation of the spirit, while Spirit allows interaction with the ephemeral aspect of the spirit<br /> <br /> Similarly, Mind allows one to do what is associated with psychics, such as pyrokenisis.<br /> <br /> With Forces alone, the mage may use their psionic abilities to focus on the flame and cast the effect to cause it to strike another, grow, avoid, or otherwise make a single movement. What adding Mind allows is for the mage to transform their thoughts into manifestations of Forces. Mind 3 Forces 3 is the transmutation of your conscious thoughts in to, for example, fire. This allows you to focus on a space and cause a fire to appear for as long as you focus on it, or for you to have the fire change shape and move around as you imagine with only the casting of a single ongoing effect. You can make the flame spell out your name, change in to the shape of your face, and then float towards someone before bursting into smaller flames, all in one effect, something that would be far more complex with Forces alone, requiring a new cast for each element of the change, racking up paradox with each cast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 07-27-2023, 05:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T01:58:34-07:00","id":1518889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Ericson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1518563#post1518563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes I think they add extra sphears just to make casting spells harder. for a game about being a mage they really discourage useing magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hdydt is a bit of a departure from the usual philosophy of how the spheres combine to allow effects. Generally speaking, spheres are a means to include the manipulation of specific aspects of reality in to an effect. For each rote I like to ask \u201cwhat does each sphere contribute to the effect. How would the effect be possible if this sphere was reduced in rank, of missing that sphere entirely.\u201d<br /> <br /> for example, Clairvoyance with Corr 2 alone is essentially scrying, but if one wishes to read the minds of those they scry on, and thus reaching the \u201ctruer\u201d definition of clairvoyance, then adding Mind 1 would allow for sensing emotions, Mind 2 for sensing surface thoughts, and Mind 3 for sensing subconscious thoughts/memories. And it is the Mind 3 version of the rote which enables what is classically described as clairvoyance.<br /> <br /> While it does get a bit wibbly here, the wording on HDYDT\u2019s \u201cPerceiving from a distance\u201d here does imply that the limit of Corr effects on range, where you can only use spheres of the rank up to your corr rank to access the corr range table, is specific to effects which \u201ccommand\u201d from a distance, not sense.<br /> <br /> therefore, it is conceivable that Corr 2 Mind 3 would indeed be enough to read subconscious minds from a distance, but not manipulate their conscious thoughts (which would need you to have corr 3). Indeed, this would apply to any sensory effect done from a distance, they would only need the addition of corr 2 to pull off. However you would suffer the increase in difficulty for targeting things beyond sensory range without corr 3.<br /> <br /> If you have any other particular examples, I\u2019ll be haply to try and explain how I understand the sphere logic to play out. Though do allow that if they come exclusively from HDYDT, I might need to refer to previous editions to explain why I disagree with some of the decisions made for that book.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T02:30:03-07:00","id":1518892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1518883#post1518883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This point if rather overstated and in my opinion somewhat of a misinterpretation for how spheres relate to practice.<br /> <br /> any practice can be paired with any sphere combination, but certain sphere combinations allow one to perform the types of effects which are more in line with that practices\u2019s tropes.<br /> <br /> Without Spirit, a shame may use Forces to encourage the spirits of fire to grow, move to avoid people, or strike specific targets. But with Spirit, they may also communicate with the spirits of fire, perhaps getting them to take the reigns of part of the effect and even act long after the shaman\u2019s magic has finished. In this case, Forces allows direct manipulation of fire, while Spirit allowed the spirit of fire to do the work as they may negotiate, the two together allows for both to be part of the same effect, control and communication. The shaman\u2019s practice allows this as they are in tune with the notion of spirits in all elements, and Forces is a way to manipulate the spirits of elements without directly breaching the gauntlet. Forces directs the mundane manifestation of the spirit, while Spirit allows interaction with the ephemeral aspect of the spirit<br /> <br /> Similarly, Mind allows one to do what is associated with psychics, such as pyrokenisis.<br /> <br /> With Forces alone, the mage may use their psionic abilities to focus on the flame and cast the effect to cause it to strike another, grow, avoid, or otherwise make a single movement. What adding Mind allows is for the mage to transform their thoughts into manifestations of Forces. Mind 3 Forces 3 is the transmutation of your conscious thoughts in to, for example, fire. This allows you to focus on a space and cause a fire to appear for as long as you focus on it, or for you to have the fire change shape and move around as you imagine with only the casting of a single ongoing effect. You can make the flame spell out your name, change in to the shape of your face, and then float towards someone before bursting into smaller flames, all in one effect, something that would be far more complex with Forces alone, requiring a new cast for each element of the change, racking up paradox with each cast.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the record, I agree with whatya saying here. I feel overly restrictive interpretations on Arcana/Spheres are frequently present in both Mage games <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T03:56:40-07:00","id":1518913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1518880#post1518880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not Dataweaver of course, but I think what they meant about logical progression has to do with internal consistency, not the external/philosophical one, where spell effects are organized into Practices, and you get access to the more complex Practices as you raise your Arcanum dots. (Made even clearer in 2e, where they snipped out things like &quot;Compelling spells are 1-dot, but radiation requires Forces 5&quot;, and hard-locked all Practices into dot levels)</div> </div> </div> </div>This. I wasn't advocating that Awakening's specific mechanics be ported into M5 (though there are quite a few of them that I would like to bring over); I was thinking more in terms of implementing something like Awakening's Practices in Ascension. The Entropy approach of \u201cthree dots let you affect Matter; four dots let you affect Life; five dots let you affect Mind\u201d feels weird to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T05:39:25-07:00","id":1518921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1518913#post1518913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This. I wasn't advocating that Awakening's specific mechanics be ported into M5 (though there are quite a few of them that I would like to bring over); I was thinking more in terms of implementing something like Awakening's Practices in Ascension. The Entropy approach of \u201cthree dots let you affect Matter; four dots let you affect Life; five dots let you affect Mind\u201d feels weird to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve seen that more as a shorthand to help describe what each level does. The ranks are more along the lines of 3: affect predictable, 4: affect chaotic, 5: control outcome<br /> <br /> it is just that matter patterns for the most part conform to predictable mechanisms, life patterns to more choatic mechanisms, and Mind pervading to human behaviour and interaction, which is so beyond the usual scope that to affect this is to essentially determine the outcome.<br /> <br /> while it could be better communicated, the progression is logical, with each step you are controlling aspects where fate would have a greater role in the eventual outcome<br /> 2: affect that which fate has little/no impact, it is pure chance<br /> 3: affect that which fate has a predictable impact<br /> 4: affect that which fate has a complex impact<br /> 5: affect that which fate directly determines","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T17:41:13-07:00","id":1519059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1518913#post1518913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Entropy approach of \u201cthree dots let you affect Matter; four dots let you affect Life; five dots let you affect Mind\u201d feels weird to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that definite, major, and clear limitations, distinctions and narrow progression like Entropy Magick has can be avoided or changed. This does of course rely on the Mage's Paradigm, honest, efforts, intelectual and scholarly resources, and distinct grasp of concepts, ideas, notions and as well sheer talent.<br /> <br /> Entropy ( or Fate, as it could be considered ) is not the only type of Magick that shows this tendency. Prime and Forces also show this trend in allocation of categories for Effects. <br /> <br /> Another curious and noteworthy trend is the definite and spectacular unlocking of situation changing capabilities and results as a Mage ( or a Technocrat ) advances in Correspondence Magick.<br /> <br /> It also can be observed that in Life Magick the Mage - be it a Chorister or a Verbenae - gains access to results and feats that clearly can lead to vastly different outcomes, victories, situations and gains, as the Mage's grasp on Life Effects increases, grops, and develops.<br /> This allows the Mage to be more or less certain - or at the very least to have strong tools and precuations at the ready. The Mage can easily deal and achieve gains and victories while participating in regard to situations, events, and challanges that involve the physical body, environment and nature, temporal achievements and efforts, and also wellbeing and health.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T13:34:26-08:00","id":1529337,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:black\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Correspondence</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">68 - At Corr 1, a mage can spot connections and measure distances.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">68 - At Corr 2, a mage can look across distances and pull small objects from nowhere.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">68 - At Corr 3, a mage can step through intervening space.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">68 - At Corr 4, a mage can appear in multiple places at once. No mention is made of processing senses or moving separately in each of these places.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">68 - At Corr 5, can stack multiple locations in the same location.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#9b00d3\">417 - Active Corr 1 sensory effects cancel the Multiple Opponents penalty.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">422 - Correspondence sensory effects allow the Read An Opponent maneuver to be used at at a distance.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#ff8000\">422 (In the Thunder Punch sidebar) - Correspondence 1 allows a mage to judge the perfect spot to hit. This sort of makes sense and sort of doesn't.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">439 (In the Dodging the Blast sidebar) - The book suggests Correspondence to teleport out of the area of a blast as a method of dodging blasts. No sphere level is given, so presumably Corr 3.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#9b00d3\">467 - Astral Immersion in the Digital Web requires at least 2 dots in Correspondence though this is not a magical effect and does not have an Arete roll. Holistic immersion, on the other hand, requires a Life 4/ Corr 2/ Forces 2 effect to convert and upload the mage to the web. </span><span style=\"color:green\">Corr 2 is fine</span><span style=\"color:black\">, </span><span style=\"color:red\">though I think this would need to be Forces 3.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">469 - Within the Digital web a mage can use a Corr 3 effect to backspace out of a hotlink. Essentially a specific application of personal teleportation.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">478 - Correspondence 2 allows an Astral traveler to continue to sense the body they left behind. </span><span style=\"color:red\">If this means they can perceive the senses of their body and their astral body at the same time, this should be Co-locality perceptions from Corr 3. </span><span style=\"color:green\">Of course, since Astral Projection is usually Mind 4, a mage needs to have Correspondence 4 to do this either way.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">482 - Verbena can use Correspondence 1 to find the Old Roads.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#9b00d3\">485 - Correspondence does not allow senses to extend between spirit realms and teleportation and colocation require extra successes. This definitely contradicts the previous rules on sensing your body during astral travel.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#9b00d3\">485 - Correspondence is unreliable in the Low Umbra.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#9b00d3\">504 - Correspondence is not capable of inflicting damage without other spheres.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#9b00d3\">509 - Correspondence 3/Matter or Life 2 as a levitation/flying spell. The Correspondence writeup does not mention this, but it is consistant with previous editions. As long as Matter and Life are locking spheres (and why should we think otherwise) this is reasonable.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">509 - Correspondence 2 for Clairvoyance. Perfectly reasonable.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\">509 - Mind 3/Correspondence 2 for Clairvoyance. Utter nonsense unless it has some application the previous effect does not. This being the quick reference chart, no such application is given. </span><span style=\"color:green\">If, somehow, this was supposed to add the ability to read the thoughts of the people you remotely view, that would reasonably be Mind 3/Corr 2. Note that it could not be cast unless the Mage had Corr 3, though.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#ff8000\">509 - Affect distant object or being is Correspondence 2+. A quite unhelpful entry for its vagueness. </span><span style=\"color:red\">If this means a mage can mundanely affect the thing as if it was right next to them, that is Corr 2.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#ff0000\">509 - Conjure Earthly Being is listed at Corr 4/Life 2. Corr 4 can do this alone.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#9b00d3\">509 - Create Multiple Images is Correspondence 3. I only just realized that colocating the image of something isn't really listed anywhere in Correspondence. Whether this is the right rank depends on what is happening. If we treat this as a variant of colocality perceptions or co-location it should be rank 4 at least. However, it a mage were to take the sense through space of Corr 2 and extend it to other people, then that would accomplish the same thing at Correspondence 3.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\">509 - Create Multiple Objects is Correspondence 5/Matter 3/Prime 2. That has to have been Correspondence 5 OR Matter 3/Prime 2.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">509 - Correspondence 4 to open gateways between locations. That is a straightforward application of Corr 4.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">509 - Teleportation is Corr 3 (4). Assuming thats for self teleportation and teleporting others respectively that is correct. Note that no locking spheres are given.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\">509 - Ward/Ban takes Correspondence 2+/Prime 2+/[Appropriate Sphere] 2+. Correspondence doesn't get wards/bans until level 4. Prime doesn't do anything. It is reasonable to need a sphere to set the nature of the ban, but I'm not sure we ever get rules as to what levels are required.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">510 - Prime 2 or Prime 2/Corr 2 to employ a periapt. Presumably the Corr version is to do so at a distance. None of the other Prime effects on this page include a Corr version.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:black\">513 - When using Correspondence with other spheres, the Mage's correspondence rank caps the rank of other spheres in the spell. That is, a mage with Matter 5 and Correspondence 2 is limited to Matter 2 when using Correspondence.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:black\">513 - Unless other spheres are included, Correspondence deals with whole patterns only. No partial teleportations.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\">513 - Corr 2/Life ? or Corr/Matter ? to teleport housecat sized objects to the mage. This is nonsense. The book just got done saying that Correspondence alone can teleport objects, so this should not need Matter or Life. </span><span style=\"color:#ff8000\">Even with that correction, there is still a problem in that this section doesn't specify the logic as it seems to do something that isn't available till Corr 4, just with an arbitrary size restriction. I think the idea is that this is is an extension of reaching across space, essentially adding picking things up to all the other ways a Correspondence mage can manipulate them at a distance. The size restriction isn't a size restriction at all, its the limit of what a mage could easily reach out and grab if it were right in front of him.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\">513 - Combined with Forces, Life, and Matter, Correspondence 3 can move things around from a distance, levitating, manipulating, or teleporting them without physical contact. Okay, this is a hot mess. Firstly, its Corr 2 to move things from a distance, not Corr 3. Using Forces rather than your hands doesn't change that. Secondly, Life and Matter, aren't necessary. </span><span style=\"color:green\">The statement that Corr 3 allows teleporting objects without physical contact does support the idea that Corr 2 'teleportation' is just picking things up from a distance. If so it is the only meaningful statement in the paragraph.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\">Edit: 513 - Permanent gateways are stated to take 10 successes, which contradicts the 6+ (storyteller discretion) of the reference charts. No reason is given for the special rule.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:green\">513 - Correspondence 4 plus appropriate spheress to ward or ban. </span><span style=\"color:#ff8000\">No indication of how you calculate the appropriate spheres is given.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">516 - Life 1/Corr 2 to extend life senses across space. I think this was included for padding.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\">518 - Matter 2/Corr 2 to move an object through space. If the item is small enough, this is Correspondence 2 alone. If it is larger, it can be Correspondence 3 alone. Matter is, at best, a locking sphere. More padding, it seems.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\">520 - Correspondence is mentioned as one of the spheres that can be paired with Mind to accomplish things it can already do without Mind.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">522 - Corr + Time 2 to see the past and future impressions of alternate locations. No rank for Corr is given, so I think it defaults to 2. That is, I'd flag it as wrong if it did.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\">523 - Time 3/Corr 3 to cast spells across space and time. Casting across space is Corr 2.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\">523 - Corr is one of the spheres listed to help Time capture things in bubbles of time. I'm not sure what Corr would add to this. Possibly it would be used to capture locations, but by default spells are cast on locations.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\">533 (Axis of Coincidence sidebar) - Corr does not summon taxis. This was probably meant to mean that a spell to take a mage from point A to point B does not accomplish the effect by summoning a taxi. Corr 4 can definitely teleport a taxi to you.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\">533 (Axis of Coincidence sidebar) - Corr 3 to find a taxi. Why is this not 2?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\">543 - Corr 3 to extend sensory range. That should be Corr 2.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">562 - Corr 4/Time 3/Forces 2/Matter 2 focused through a hypercharged sportscar to allow it to give it a high speed getaway mode. Correspondence is to allow it to &quot;skip from one place to another through intervening distances in order to avoid hitting other vehicles.&quot; Poor wording, but Corr 4 is the correct sphere for teleporting the car and its occupants. </span><span style=\"color:red\">The other spheres have much poorer justifications though.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">563 - A Corr 2/Mind 2/Matter 2 for a locked spell that wards against scrying, pushes a general keep out vibe, and warns the caster if someone trespasses.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:green\">563 - A Corr 2/Mind2/Entropy 1 spell to mentally impulse to get the targets to say embarrassing things in front of cameras. Entropy is a superfluous add on, but since this is an example of a player making a spell, that's fine.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#ff8000\">595 - Correspondence 3/Mind 3 to... well... its not quite clear. The beginning of the paragraph starts out with a transportation effect. It ends with an alteration of US law with belief in political power as a focus. If its supposed to be a transportation spell it is barely a spell as he mostly uses resources he has available. At best there's a small amount of mental influence, which would be Corr 2/Mind 2. If it is supposed to be an actual mental manipulation of judges, it is a Mind 3 spell. No correspondence is needed because the mage is in the room. There's not enough detail to see why this should be the combination it is.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\">601 - Corr 2/Forces 2/Mind 2 to hack a computer you can't connect to using a hollywood style device. I think this should be Corr 2 alone. Possibly Forces is involved in connecting the data stream itself. Mind is doing nothing</span><span style=\"color:#ff8000\">.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#ff8000\">608 - Chain of Whispers - Mind 3/Corr 2 to create an infectious rumor. Allegedly Correspondence pulls the information from person to person. This is a very odd use of Correspondence.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 01-29-2024, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T09:19:24-08:00","id":1529438,"title":"","content":"Special Mention - Consecration<br /> <br /> Prime 1 specifically mentions that a mage can consecrate an item to himself so that it will change metaphysically when he does. This includes when he shapeshifts and when he steps sideways. Indeed, having an item (or clothing) that travels with you is one of the primary purposes of this. Well don't tell that to the Otherworlds section. In that section, it is unnecessary for stepping sideways and not enough for astral or agama travel, which require Prime 2 + 5 successes on a willpower roll and Entropy 3/Prime 2 respectively.<br /> <br /> You can make the argument that the Agama Sojourn and the Astral Sojourn involve you leaving your body while just stepping sideways does not. That would certainly make sense. But then the two sojourn sections say to bring items they need to be metaphysically bound to the character and that's what consecration does.<br /> <br /> Given the explicit wording of Prime 1, I think it overrides the Otherworlds possessions sections and a lot of wordcount was wasted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 01-25-2024, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T13:52:10-08:00","id":1529462,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Entropy</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Entropy gets wrongly tacked onto spells a lot, because it seems like it is at least tangentially involved in many things even when the other Spheres involved are enough. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#548235\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">407 \u2013 Entropy 4 attacks inflict Agg damage.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#548235\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">413 \u2013 Entropy can be used to spot weak points. </span></span><span style=\"color:#C55A11\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is a consistent use and it makes sense, but often there is no functional benefit for using it to do so.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#C55A11\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">415 \u2013 An example of the above: A Life 3/Matter 3/Entropy 1 that explicitly uses Entropy to spot weak points. Great. Life and Matter make the spell damaging to vampires and Life makes it Agg damage. The Enlightenment (Arete) roll is 4 so 8 damage, same as it would be for a Life 3/Matter 3 spell. The attack is a Dex + Martial Arts, with no indication of reduced difficulty. Mechanically, what is Entropy doing? It's not a wrong use, and it is the right sphere for the claimed effect, its just that there is no functional difference between the spell with the effect and the spell without it. </span></span><span style=\"color:#C00000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Edit: Also, it only takes Matter 2 to make Life damage vampires.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#548235\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">416 \u2013 On the other hand, here\u2019s a good example of Entropy 1 to find weaknesses. A purely Entropy 1 spell. This spell lowers the difficulty of the next attack by -1 per success (presumably capping at -3 total)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#C00000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">419 \u2013 Entropy 3/Prime 2 attacks do Aggravated and metaphysical damage to ghosts. This is odd because normally Entropy can\u2019t even directly attack until level 4, though I suppose this is a special exception. Also the Aggravated damage is explicitly coming from the Entropy side, so Prime is unnecessary. This should have been a flat Entropy 3.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#548235\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">422 (Thunder Punch sidebar) \u2013 Thunder punch is another good example of Entropy 1 to find weak points. It\u2019s another -1 per success. Entropy 2 to adjust probabilities is also given as a potential way of invoking Thunder Punch, which is technically correct but functionally pointless. </span></span><span style=\"color:#C55A11\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Using Entropy 2 ups the difficulty without changing the benefit.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#7030A0\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">438 (Dodging the Blast sidebar) \u2013 Entropy is one of the spheres that allow mages to invoke the optional Dodging the Blast rule.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#7030A0\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">440 \u2013 If using the optional Durability and Structure rules, Entropy attacks reduce object durability by -2, and Entropy augmented transmutation spells reduce it by -2 per success for the purposes of overcoming Durability. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#7030A0\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">478 \u2013 Agama Sojourn \u2013 Entropy 4/Spirit3/Life 2 for self passage and Entropy 4/Spirit 4/Life 3 for others. As mentioned in the Spirit writeup, it isn\u2019t clear what Entropy is doing, but we can infer that it is a necessary part of leaving the Underworld when you are done. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">480 \u2013 Taking items on the Agama Sojourn requires infusing them with Entropy 3, then binding them to the traveler with Prime 2. Consecration is Prime 1, and needs no special spheres. I suppose this section could be saying that Consecration isn\u2019t enough for the Agama Sojourn or the Astral Sojourn, but it looks more like Consecration was forgotten when these sections were written. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#C00000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">480 \u2013 Moving from the Low Umbra to other layers requires Entropy 5/Spirit 5 to open a gateway, or Entropy 5/Mind 5 to astrally project from a ghostly body. Since we are never told what Entropy is doing in any of these Agama spell it is impossible to judge what the right sphere should be. However, without explanation, this should be Entropy 4 like the Agama Sojourn itself.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#7030A0\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">485 \u2013 Entropy is at -2 difficulty in the Underworld, but using it at all strengthens nearby Shadows and Spectres. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#7030A0\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">491 \u2013 Calcify does not work on Mages with an Entropy of 4 or higher. This seems to be a part of a recurring idea that the Entropy sphere is intrinsically linked with the forces of decay and entropy, which is only fitting for some games, not all.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#548235\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">508 \u2013 Entropy 4 to Rot Body. It\u2019s a basic Entropy attack.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#548235\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">508 \u2013 Alter probability at Entropy 2</span></span><span style=\"color:#C00000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+</span></span><span style=\"color:#548235\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">. </span></span><span style=\"color:#C00000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alter probability is the explicit domain of Entropy 2. I think the + is referring to giving people good or bad luck which happens at Entropy 3, but that\u2019s better described as another effect like Bless/Curse.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#C00000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">508 \u2013 Bless/Curse for Entropy 3/Life 3. What\u2019s Life doing here? This is possible with Entropy 3 alone.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#548235\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">508 \u2013 Entropy 3+ to Bless/Curse but this time its listed as a Spirit Power\u2026 </span></span><span style=\"color:#C55A11\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I don\u2019t see why this is a spirit power though, or why this is listed twice.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#548235\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">508 \u2013 Entropy 3+ to Cause Decay. I probably would have just said Entropy 3. Entropy 4 allows a mage to inflict decay on living things, but that is better described by Rot Body. Its not inaccurate to put it here, I suppose.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#548235\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">508 \u2013 Entropy 1 to spot weaknesses.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#C00000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">508 \u2013 A repeat of the Entropy 3/Prime 2 to harm a ghost. Same issue.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#C55A11\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">509 \u2013 Entropy 3/Time 3 to disintegrate an object. I\u2019ve said before that this works, but I\u2019d like to see a comparison with what Entropy 3 alone and Time 3 alone would do. It seems like the combined spell should be better, but I don\u2019t know how to adjudicate that. If its not better, this should be Entropy 3 OR Time 3, as there\u2019s no reason to put more complicated methods in the common magical effects chart.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#C00000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">516 \u2013 Forces 3/Entropy 3 to erode or enhance energies. Forces 3 can do this alone. Actually, Forces 2 can do this alone.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#C00000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">516 \u2013 Life 1/Entropy 1 to see the potential for sickness and misfortune. Entropy 1 can do this without help.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#C00000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">517 \u2013 Life 5/Entropy 4 to age or de-age a living thing. Life 5 can do this alone.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#C00000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">518 \u2013 Matter 1/Entropy 1 to see the weak points in an object. Entropy 1 can do this alone.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#7030A0\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">519 \u2013 When Time is used to prolong an effect, Entropy 3 can be added to set an end condition. I\u2019m not sure why Rank 3 is the right rank, though I don\u2019t know which rank would be better.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#C00000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">522 \u2013 Time 2/Entropy 2 to see multiple futures and pick out the one most likely to occur. I\u2019m not sure what this means, but if it is only sensing which one is most likely, shouldn\u2019t it be Entropy 1? And if the mage is choosing which one is most likely, what does that mean?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#C55A11\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">523 \u2013 Time 3/Entropy 3 to invoke multiple probabilities. To do what? This is so unclear it isn\u2019t even wrong. I simply do not know what this means in any practical way.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#C00000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">523 \u2013 Time/Forces/Entropy to capture a tornado in a bubble of time. I don\u2019t see what Entropy is doing here. Just because a storm is chaotic doesn\u2019t mean Forces needs help controlling it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#C00000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">524 \u2013 Data 2 and Entropy let a mage predict and alter probability patterns or spot the flaws in objects, and it doesn\u2019t take Data 2 to see that Entropy can do all that without help.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#548235\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">532 \u2013 Entropy 2 to increase the odds of finding a taxi. This is tricky. I\u2019d say increasing the odds of a taxi driving by would be Entropy 2 while increasing the odds of someone finding a taxi is Entropy 3. That said, if there is an Entropy 2 way of doing it, it is a correct statement.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#C00000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">546 \u2013 Entropy and Spirit to counter ghostly Arcanoi. I think this should be Entropy OR Spirit.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#C00000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">562 \u2013 Entropy 2/Life 2/Spirit 1 to manipulate the probability of someone giving the mage a free lunch. This is an example of player thinking so the redundancy is fine. Still, Entropy alone can do this, and if Life is involved it is just a sensory effect, so it is Life 1.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#C00000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">563 \u2013 Correspondence 2/Mind 2/Entropy 1 to curse people to accidentally reveal embarrassing info. This is another example of Entropy 1 searching for weak points but having no real effect on the spell.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#548235\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">601 \u2013 Hands of Death has an optional Entropy 2 version that \u201cspots weak points\u201d to reduce armor. Spotting weak points is technically Entropy 1, but Entropy 2 is the rank for repeatedly hitting weak points so this works. </span></span><span style=\"color:#C00000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That said, it reduces durability/armor/soak by -1 per success, in addition do damage, which makes this the third different system given for this effect. (-2 per attack and -2 per success being the other 2.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#548235\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">603 \u2013 Hypernarrative Influence has an optional Entropy 2 that causes pop culture appropriate events to pop up. Some of the examples are actually not probabilities, but otherwise this works.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#548235\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">610 \u2013 Witch\u2019s Vengeance uses Entropy 4 to age or decay someone.</span> </span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 02-05-2024, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-29T10:09:56-08:00","id":1529652,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Forces</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Forces has a magnitude problem. Most high powered phenomena should technically be possible at 2, so in addition to the normal progression, magnitude is often locked behind higher spheres, which is clumsy and arbitrary. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:green\">68 - At Forces 1, a mage can note elemental phenomena.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:green\">68 \u2013 At Forces 2 a mage can make burning candles flare or go out.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">68 - At Forces 3 can conjure winds or make fire leap. Both of these should be possible at Forces 2</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:green\">68 - At Forces 4 a mage can conjure storms. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:green\">68 - At Corr 5 a mage can command firestorms, blizzards, and nuclear blasts. </span><span style=\"color:#e67e22\">These are listed in the Forces 5 section but there's no real reason they can't be done with Forces 4. They're not beyond Forces 4 ranges.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:green\">421 \u2013 Forces 2 to add velocity and momentum to a thrown weapon gives a -1 difficulty per success.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:green\">422 (Thunder Punch Sidebar) \u2013 The same effect, but for any attack.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">429 (Catching Bullets Sidebar) \u2013 Time 3/Forces 2/Life 2 to add a bullet catch effect to the Arrow Cutting feat. This effect can be done with fewer spheres and Forces 2 on its own should be enough.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">438 (Dodging the Blast sidebar) \u2013 Forces is one of the spheres that allow mages to invoke the optional Dodging the Blast rule.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">440 \u2013 Forces 2/Matter 2 to make an attack on a pillar. Forces for the attack, Matter to reduce its durability (Optional Rule)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">457 \u2013 Forces 2 effect to disperse clouds of toxins.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c55a11\">465 \u2013 Suggested Forces effect to augment a taser. One possible result is an extra damage die per two successes. It\u2019s an unclear section.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">467 \u2013 Astral Immersion into the digital web is Life 4/Correspondence 2/Forces 2. Since the idea is that the character becomes pure information, this is a transmutation effect which requires Life 5 and Forces 3.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">470 \u2013 In the Digital Web, Forces effects that score more than 5 successes risk Whiteout. I would rule that this doesn\u2019t apply to Forces 1 sensory effects, but that's personal opinion.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">485 \u2013 In Otherworlds, by default, Forces spells are at a +1 difficulty. Forces spells do not work at all in the Low Umbra.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">505 \u2013 Forces adds an automatic success for Damage.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">506 \u2013 \u201cPhysical Illusions\u201d take Forces 2+/Prime2+ and Immersive Illusions (holodeck levels of apparent reality) take Forces 4+/Prime 4+. I covered this back on the first page, but its not clear what Prime is doing here, especially with the + sign. Possibly Prime 2 it is creating a Body of Light framework for Forces to map to, but I have no explanation for Prime 4. And even Body of Light is an unnecessary addition. Forces 2 can do all of this on its own; even Forces 4 is unnecessary unless the area of effect gets into a range of miles. Basically, both of these spells boil down to the same spell, which is Forces 2+.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">508 \u2013 Transforming an object into air is apparently a Forces 3/Matter 2 effect. Incorrect. Forces 3/Matter 2 is the combination to transmute a simple object into energy (such as making a brick disappear in a flash of light). Transforming an object into air is changing from one form of Matter into another and is the explicit domain of Matter 3. Forces would only be used if you were heating the object to the point it evaporated, in which case Matter would not be needed.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">508 \u2013 Immersive Illusions once again take Forces 4+/Prime 4+ but this time also take Mind 4. Prime 4 is just as nonsensical as before. Mind depends a great deal on what it is doing. No explanation is given. Since the idea of \u2018holodeck\u2019 level illusions includes autonomous reactive ones, maybe this is making the illusion adaptable? Whatever the case, Forces 4+ is still wrong.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">509 \u2013 Call Storm is Forces 4+/Prime 2. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">509 \u2013 Conjure element. Forces 3/Prime 2 to conjure fire is correct. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Forces 3/Prime 2 to conjure wind is not. If you can levitate a person with Forces 2 you can accelerate air with Forces 2. If you don\u2019t already have air then the spell becomes Forces 2+/Matter 2/Prime 2 to summon the air and accelerate it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">509 \u2013 Conjure Physical Illusion is now listed as Forces 2+/Prime 2. This works.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">509 \u2013 Direct existing elements is Forces 2+. Again, if you can accelerate a person you can accelerate air.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">509 \u2013 Invisibility is Forces 2</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">509 \u2013 Invisibility on a living being is Forces 2/Life 2. Since that\u2019s a locking effect this is also correct.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">509 \u2013 Levitation or flying. I really think this was supposed to mean Forces 2+/[Pattern Sphere] 2 or Correspondence 3/[Pattern Sphere] 2. The distinction will matter when I get to Matter, for now Forces 2+ is the correct level for unlocked levitation/flight.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">509 \u2013 Speed or slow velocity at Forces 2+</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">509 \u2013 Transform Forces at Forces 3+/[Appropriate Sphere] 2. Forces 3+ is correct. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">For once, though, the missing + is a problem. This should be Forces 3+/[Appropriate Sphere] 2+.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">509 \u2013 Create multiple images has a Forces 2+/Prime 2 variant. This is essentially another physical illusion (though purely light based). Prime 2 is unnecessary.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">509 \u2013 Telekinesis at Forces 2+. Correct. And for once, no superfluous Mind addition.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">509 \u2013 Mind 3/Forces 2 to translate language so that other people can understand it. This is an awkward description of a reasonable effect. Mind 3/Forces 2 is the method of translating the physical sensations of language: sound to sound, or text to text, etc. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">If the mage is just making the targets think they are hearing a different language, that\u2019s Mind alone.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">513 \u2013 Forces 3/ Prime 2/ Corr 2 to start fires at a distance.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">513 \u2013 Forces + Correspondence 3 to levitate things at a distance. This would be Correspondence 2. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">513 \u2013 Forces combined with Correspondence 4 can create a ward or ban against forces and energies. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c55a11\">No specific level is given though and advice to consult HDYDT which falsely implies that HDYDT is helpful. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c55a11\">513 \u2013 Forces + Corr 5 to stretch or compress energies. This is too vague to be useful. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\"> If it means a special distortion locked to a pattern it technically works. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">If it means stretching or compressing a space such that those inside don\u2019t notice, I don\u2019t think you need a pattern sphere at all. If you are stretching or compressing the patterns you don\u2019t need Correspondence at all. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">515 \u2013 The direct statement that large scale Forces effects require both higher ranks and more successes, which is a double whammy unique to Forces.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">516 \u2013 Forces 2 contains the stated area limits of \u201caround a single human-sized character\u201d or 20 square feet. It doesn\u2019t use the term square feet, but since a 20 ft by 20 ft area is way bigger than a human I think it was the intention. This is an arbitrary limit and I don\u2019t like it. Forces 3 is limited to several dozen yards (Again, square I think). Forces 4 to miles. Forces 5 has no limit.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">516 \u2013 Transforming people into electricity is Life 5/Forces 3</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">516 \u2013 Changing water into air is listed as Forces 3/Matter 3. This is incorrect. Evaporating water would be Forces 2 OR Matter 3. Turning water into air would be Matter 3. Edit: Both changing the state of matter (solid ice to liquid water) and transmuting matter in one state to a different type of matter in another (solid ice to liquid gold) are the explicit domain of Matter 3.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">516 \u2013 Attaching elemental forces to a person or object is described as Forces 3/[Appropriate Sphere] 3, but if we read the description its basically just a force anchored to a pattern, which is [Appropriate Sphere] 2</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">516 \u2013 Forces 3/Entropy 3 to erode or enhance energies. I can\u2019t think of a meaning to this that can\u2019t be done with Forces alone.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">516 \u2013 Forces 3/Mind 3 to manifest thoughts into energies. Really poor wording. This is the correct combination for transmuting a thought or idea into energy. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">It is not the correct combination for thinking up a Forces effect and then casting it. It is especially not the combination for casting a Forces effect if the Mage is a psychic.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">516 \u2013 Forces 3/Spirit 3 to transmute ephemera into energy.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c55a11\">516 \u2013 Forces 3/Time 4 is probably the correct combination for setting triggers for energy fluctuations. I just wish I knew what energy fluctuations were or why they needed to be triggered. </span><span style=\"color:#c00000\">If the energy fluctuations are the trigger, though, Forces 3 is too high. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">516 \u2013 Transforming people into other elements is Life 5/Forces 3 or Life 5/Matter 3.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">519 \u2013 Transforming cars into robots is Matter 4 plus Forces and Prime. I don\u2019t see what Forces or Prime are adding. Maybe if the robot in question has a specific feature this would be necessary. If the robot is somehow &quot;alive,&quot; Prime might be an animating force, but this is not a listed ability of Prime and robot does not imply the need for an animating force.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">520 \u2013 Forces can be combined with Mind to pull off telekinesis, pyrokinesis and a whole host of things that Forces can already do <i>without Mind</i>. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">521 \u2013 Spirit 2/Forces 2+ to stir up elemental disturbances within Otherworlds\u2026 essentially cast a Forces spell across the Gauntlet.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">522 \u2013 Forces + Time 3 to cast across time.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">522 \u2013 Forces + Entropy + Time 4 to trap a tornado in a no-time space. The more I read this the more I think it is wrong. I\u2019ve already covered how Entropy is wrong, but Time probably doesn\u2019t need help moving patterns any more than Correspondence does. That said, this effect might need Correspondence as you are not just freezing the storm in time but also moving it to an extradimensional space.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">530 \u2013 Forces 3/Prime 2 to conjure a fireball with a lighter and spray can. The lighter and spray can are creating a small fireball already, it only takes Forces 2+ to manipulate it into a bigger one. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">533 (Axis of Coincidence sidebar) \u2013 Life 5/Mind 5/Matter 4/Forces 3/Prime 3 to create a fully functional taxi and driver. Unless you want to summon it with the engine running, there\u2019s really no need for Forces.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">535 \u2013 Forces 2 to make a breeze or make a candle flame fly across the room.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">544 \u2013 Forces 5/Corr 2/Prime 2 to blow up the moon.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">562 - Corr 4/Time 3/Forces 2/Matter 2 focused through a hypercharged sportscar to give it a high speed getaway mode. The justification for Forces is not accelerating the car, Correspondence does that by skipping through intervening spaces. Forces is to counter the g forces. From the description it\u2019s not even clear that\u2019s necessary, the car is faster because it has a different relation to time and space, not because it is faster. As a player choice this is okay, but I wouldn\u2019t use it as an example.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">563 \u2013 Forces 2/Prime 2 to up the damage of a bullet and give it Agg.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">601 - Corr 2/Forces 2/Mind 2 to hack a computer you can't connect to using a hollywood style device. I think this should be Corr 2 alone. Possibly Forces is involved in connecting the data stream itself. Mind is doing nothing.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">601 \u2013 Hot-Shotting at Forces 2. Each success reduces the difficulty of the next attack and adds an automatic success. These can be added to intimidation rolls, damage, or to expand the number of targets. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">My only complaint is that this is a lot of utility for a single success and it seems like two different effects, one altering the sound of the gun and one altering the efficiency.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">601 \u2013 Hands of Death applies the rules from the Damage or Duration chart to hand to hand damage, with one automatic success for Forces.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">601 \u2013 Right Click. The Forces 1 add-on gives infrared or ultraviolet scanning capabilities.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">603 \u2013 Sanitize Evidence uses Matter 2/Forces 2 to evaporate evidence. This should be Matter 2+/Forces 3 as it is a transmutation effect.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">604 \u2013 The Forces 1 part of Secure the Scene is for scanning, and appears to help detect blood and evidence. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c55a11\">It can do this indirectly but is far from the best sphere. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">The Forces 3 add on adds a blackout effect that warps light and sound around the area</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">. This should be Forces 3+ based on area of effect.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">605 \u2013 Dimension Bomb uses DimSci 3/Forces 3/Prime 2 to create a forces based explosion on the other side of the gauntlet.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">605 \u2013 Golden gunman uses Forces 2 to let an operative do acrobatic flips unhindered by the recoil of any weapons. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">No system is given for these acrobatic flips so presumably they are mundane.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">608 \u2013 Bullet Catch. Forces 2/Life 2/Time 2. Same effect as earlier. Same complaint as earlier.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">608 \u2013 Psychic Interface. Mind 3(4)/Data 2/Forces 2 to psychically interface with computers. I could see arguments for dropping Forces, but it also makes sense.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">626 \u2013 Matter 3/Mind 3/Forces 2 to reprogram a HIT Mark X. I don\u2019t see what Matter and Forces are doing here. </span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 02-05-2024, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-30T05:03:22-08:00","id":1529698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1529652#post1529652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Forces</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Forces has a magnitude problem. Most high powered phenomena should technically be possible at 2, so in addition to the normal progression, magnitude is often locked behind higher spheres, which is clumsy and arbitrary. </span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that, because of the sheer variety and potential of possible Forces Effect, mentioning just magnitude is too simple. There is also the option of including qualities like intensity, complexity, reliability, variety, or stability. These qualities and details of particular elements and their possible manifestations and expressions can very well be the included and contained in a Forces Effect.<br /> Definitely Mages and Technocrats skilled in Forces can manipulate, control, and perceive more categories of details and qualities contained within elemental and natural phenomena than just linear magnitude or power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-30T07:04:47-08:00","id":1529711,"title":"","content":"That would be a good solution. Of the ones you listed, I think only complexity is ever used to divide Forces effects in M20, with storms getting pushed to Forces 4. Of course that could also just be because storms are so large. If we were to ever rewrite Forces I would much prefer to make magnitude solely a function of successes and use things like complexity and intricacy to divide between lower and higher level forces. <br /> <br /> Another possible distinction would be the Forces we can easily perceive with our senses (momentum, heat, visible light, sound, etc) from the ones we can't (radiation, magnetism, etc.). That does leave electricity in a strange position, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-30T07:24:49-08:00","id":1529714,"title":"","content":"I'd go with the former, as the latter runs into the dual problem that the Forces <i>mage </i>has no problem sending any of them and that what you're describing seems to have more to do with the Coincidental/Vulgar divide than the number of dots required for an Effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-30T07:30:37-08:00","id":1529716,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that the reason why magnitude is a factor in Forces is because someone pointed out to Brucato while he was writing M20 that the higher difficulty that comes with higher Sphere requirements means fewer successes, which in turn means that if you want a powerful Effect you're better off using a two-dot Effect than a five-dot Effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-30T08:33:36-08:00","id":1529719,"title":"","content":"That certainly explains a lot, including why I keep seeing higher sphere ranks than necessary, extraneous spheres, and two different rank options presented as if they are interchangeable. It also doesn't really tackle the problem of distributing effects across Forces and it interacts badly with Correspondence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-30T12:52:33-08:00","id":1529732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1529714#post1529714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd go with the former, as the latter runs into the dual problem that the Forces <i>mage </i>has no problem sending any of them and that what you're describing seems to have more to do with the Coincidental/Vulgar divide than the number of dots required for an Effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea was less that they were more noticeable by sleepers, and more that the energies we can easily perceive are more familiar and therefore good candidates for the simple side of the simple/complex divide many spheres divide into. It's not a good division per se, though I would argue that it is better than the current one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T08:19:00-08:00","id":1530029,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Life from M20</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">422 (Thunder Punch Sidebar) \u2013 The Life 3 variant is to boost strength or damage the enemy internally. I think a Life 2 variant that allows a mage to go into levels of exertion that tear muscle and tendon, but heals the damage as it happens should be viable, but I\u2019m not going to complain that no one thought of that.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">429 (Bullet Catching Sidebar) \u2013 Time 3/Forces 2/Life 2 to catch bullets. The role of Life here is in hardening the skin, which is unnecessary to the spell as written, and is also Life 3.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">435 \u2013 Life 2 can protect against blizzards, sandstorms and the like. Life 3 is suggested as a protection against Hard Vacuum or Deep Sea Pressure. This is shaky but potentially viable. Almost any change that would actually protect someone from extreme cold, heat, or scouring falls under Life 3, though Life 2 could heal the damage as quickly as it happens. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">436 \u2013 It takes Life 3 to protect against open flames, even with Body Control.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">438 (Dodging the Blast sidebar)\u2013 Life is one of the spheres that can be used for the optional Dodging the Blast rule.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">440 \u2013 When using the optional object duration rules, Life can be used to attack the durability of wood and plants. If those rules are used, Durability needs to be overcome to transmute those things.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">441 \u2013 Life 3 can restore someone to life within the first few minutes of death by suffocation. This isn\u2019t so much a new rule but an obvious application of healing based on how suffocation works. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">After 10 minutes without air the brain begins to deteriorate and it takes Life 5. That\u2019s ill thought out. That is indeed a point of no return with modern medicine, but modern medicine can't heal brain damage the way the Life sphere can. If the brain is alive it can be repaired. Life 5 is only necessary when it isn\u2019t. It would be within the realm of reason to require Mind 3 (maybe 4) along with Life 3 to restore memory and personality, though.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">442 \u2013 Life 2 for a mage to cure a disease or toxin for himself and Life 3 for someone else. This is correct, </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">although the phrase \u201cLife 2 effects to alter the mage himself, and Life 3 to alter someone else\u201d is the wrong terminology.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c55a11\">443 (Awakening Substances sidebar) \u2013 It takes Spirit 3 to rouse the spirit of a drug but Spirit 3 to rouse the spirit of a disease in someone\u2019s body. This appears to pertain to the difficulty of isolating the disease in a body, as if it is part of the pattern. Same for the Life 3/Matter 2 spell to enhance the properties of a substance in a body. Same for Life 3 to enhance microbes in someone\u2019s body vs Life 2 to enhance them outside. Except\u2026 why. The disease/substance is not part of the pattern, so a mage isn\u2019t affecting a partial pattern. I could see Life 1 in order to even see them, but nothing beyond that.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c55a11\">Admittedly, I can see a counter argument where pulling the DNA, or the hemoglobin, or the oxygen out of someone\u2019s body should count as part of their pattern and should require Life 3. That doesn\u2019t mean that everything that is in the body is part of the pattern.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">467 \u2013 Astral Immersion into the digital web is Life 4/Correspondence 2/Forces 2. Since the idea is that the character becomes pure information, this is a transmutation effect which requires Life 4(5) and Forces 3. It also means a character will need Correspondence 4+ even if they only use Rank 2.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">478 \u2013 Agama Sojourn \u2013 Entropy 4/Spirit3/Life 2 for self passage and Entropy 4/Spirit 4/Life 3 for others. Life is keeping the body alive, so it is a healing effect. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">479 (Avatar Storm Sidebar) \u2013 Life magic to increase soak may help soak damage from the storm, but its an ST call.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">483 (Acclimation sidebar) \u2013 Optional acclimation rules. After 4 to 5 weeks in Otherworlds, mages have a +1 difficulty to pattern magics for 1-2 days.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">485 \u2013 Life and Matter don\u2019t work on umbral creatures or objects unless the originated in the material world (or presumably in a realm where Life and Matter work).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">485 \u2013 Life and Prime are always vulgar in the Low Umbra.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">494 \u2013 Spirit 4/Life 3/Prime 2 to exorcise a spirit in a completed possession. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">Life 3 is likely to isolate the spirit, which in the case of a full possession might reasonably be integrated enough to count as part of the same pattern.</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\"> Prime does nothing.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">505 \u2013 Mind 3/Life 3 for an illusory attack that does aggravated damage.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">508 \u2013 Life 2 (3) to adapt to an environment. This depends a great deal on the type of adaptation, but anything within the realm of a person to acclimatize to without magic should be possible at Life 2(3).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c55a11\">508 - Life 2/Prime 2 to animate a corpse. I'd still like more details on how this functions. I need to know what Life is doing before I can tell if 2 is high enough rank.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">508 \u2013 Life 2(3) Cause/Cure Disease. Correct as long as we specify this is inflicting the symptoms/results of a disease. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Creating actual microbes is going to be Life 3/Prime 2.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">508 \u2013 </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Life 2/Prime 2 to create a simple body</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Transmutation of simple life is Life 3. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">508 - Life 5/Prime 2 to create a complex lifeform.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">508 \u2013 Life 5/Prime 2 to duplicate body. This is the correct combination to duplicate a complex body. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">A simple body can be duplicated with Life 3/Prime 2.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">508 \u2013 Life 3 (4) to grow new limbs. Growing limbs apparently doesn\u2019t count as a radical transformation. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">508 \u2013 Life 2 (3) to heal or harm. True as long as the damage is not aggravated.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">508 \u2013 Life 3/</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Mind 3</span></span> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">to heal or harm Fae. Life 3/Matter 2 to heal or harm Vampires. Life 3/Spirit 2 to heal or harm werecreatures. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">I maintain Mind 3 is too high for Fae, </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">otherwise this is good.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">508 \u2013 Life 3 (4) to Increase Physique/Traits.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c55a11\">508 \u2013 Life 4/Spirit 4/Prime 3 to Revive recently dead. It\u2019s very unclear how recent is recent and what each sphere is doing. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">508 \u2013 Life 4 to Rot Body. This should be Life 2 (3). </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">508 \u2013 Life 4(5) to shapeshift is correct as long as we are talking about people and other complex lifeforms. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Shapeshifting a simple creature is Life 3.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">508 \u2013 Life 3 or Mind 4 to compel instant slumber. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">There\u2019s also a Life 3/Mind 4 variant which works but the Magical Chart is supposed to be for the simplest versions.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">508 \u2013 Life 3 to allow someone to soak Aggravated Damage.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">508 \u2013 I need to copy this one verbatim because it is atrociously written: Life 3+/ [appropriate elemental Sphere] 3+ (Life 4+/ 3+[appropriate Sphere]). I interpret this to mean Life 3+/[Appropriate Sphere] 3+ for self transformation and Life 4+/[Appropriate Sphere] 3+ to transform others. This is wrong. It takes Life 4 for self transmutation and Life 5 for others. Also [Appropriate Sphere] 3+ is wrong in both directions as some classical elements fall under Matter 2 and none of them need over Matter or Forces 3. This is Life 4(5)/[Appropriate Sphere]2+.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">508 \u2013 Entropy 3/Life 3 to bless or curse. Life isn\u2019t necessary here.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">508 \u2013 Craft Living Periapt is Life 5/Prime 3. Why?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">508 \u2013 Mind 3+/Life 3+ for mental illusions that inflict damage. No need for the plus signs for Life.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">509 \u2013 Life 3/Prime 2 to summon living wood.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">509 \u2013 Forces 2/Life 2 for invisibility on a living being. Life is functioning as an anchoring sphere.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">509 \u2013 Time 3+/Life 4 to age or de-age a living being. Time and Life can do this on their own, and only Life 2 is necessary for simple creatures.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">509 \u2013 Correspondence 4/Life 2 to summon a living being. Life is unnecessary and this is Correspondence 2 or Correspondence 4 depending on the size of the creature.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">509 \u2013 Mind 3/Life 3 for a psychic blast that does Aggravated damage.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">511 \u2013 In the example of conjunctional effects Mind 2 alone is enough to give someone euphoria, while doing so by altering body chemistry is Life 3/Mind 2. That\u2019s wrong. Life can alter body chemistry without help.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">513 \u2013 Adding Life to Correspondence 2 allow a mage to summon organisms. Again, Life is not necessary for teleporting whole patterns.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">513 \u2013 Combining Correspondece 3 with Life (or other pattern spheres) allows a mage to \u201cmove things around from a distance, levitating them, manipulating or teleporting them without physical contact.\u201d Most of these can be done with Correspondence alone, and those that can\u2019t, can\u2019t be done with Life\u2019s help.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">513 \u2013 Correspondence 4 combined with Life can ward against life patterns. This is one case where correspondence does need the help. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">However, this section advises checking HDYDT for the rules. Since posting the Forces list, I took a deeper look at the Ward section from that book and it\u2019s a strong contender for the worst sections in there.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">513 \u2013 Correspondence 4/Life 2/Mind 1 allows a mage to be, act, and think in multiple places at once.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c55a11\">513 \u2013 As in the Forces list, Life + Corr 5 to stretch or compress energies. This is too vague to be useful. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\"> If it means a special distortion locked to a pattern it technically works. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">If it means stretching or compressing a space such that those inside don\u2019t notice, I don\u2019t think you need a pattern sphere at all. If you are stretching or compressing the patterns you don\u2019t need Correspondence at all. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">513 \u2013 Correspondence 5, combined with Life 3 allows a mage to expand her senses to perceive many places at once. Correspondence can do that at rank 3, and I don\u2019t see anything Life is doing to help.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">515 \u2013 Forces 2 combined with Life lets a mage make an organism that can attract or repel forces. That\u2019s a Forces 2 effect locked to a creature, so yes, that works.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">515 \u2013 Life 5/Forces 3 lets a mage transform people into electricity.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">515 \u2013 Forces 3 combined with Matter 3 or Life 3 attaches forces to material forms, letting them fly, pinning them to the ground, etc. This is a Forces effect locked to a pattern, it doesn\u2019t take Matter 3 or Life 3, it takes Matter 2 or Life 2.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">516 \u2013 The Life 1 conjunctional examples are really poor. The Time and Correspondence ones work as they are extending normal Life senses. The Entropy and Prime ones can be done by Entropy and Prime respectively.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">518 \u2013 Matter 1/Life 1 allows a mage to detect implants, enhancements, and other integrations of living tissue and inert matter. I daresay the combo would give a mage more information than either one alone, though when it comes to just detecting implants, either one would probably work.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">519 \u2013 Matter 4/Life 2 can turn pumpkins into carriages. This would require Life 3. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">519 \u2013 Life 5/Matter 4 to turn someone into a throne. Presumably this is a complex throne made of multiple different materials. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">An ornately carved stone throne would likely only need Matter 2.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">519 \u2013 Life 5/Matter 5 can turn vampires into lawn chairs. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">520 \u2013 Mind is combined with the pattern spheres to pull off a number of effects, most of which don\u2019t need Mind or don\u2019t need anything else. Of the listed ones only psychophysical assault and influencing people with the power of the mind pertain to Life. Influencing people is Mind alone. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">However psychophysical assault could mean a psychic attack that does lethal or aggravated damage, and that is a Mind/Life combo. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">520 \u2013 Switching a mind to another body is listed as Mind 5/Life 4, but it is unclear how this works. If it is grafting, that is full human transmutation and requires Life 5. If it is anchoring it requires Life 2.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">520 \u2013 Life + Prime 2 to create new Life patterns.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c55a11\">520 \u2013 This is a badly written moment. Consecration in general is listed as a power of Prime 1. In the text though, Prime 1 only mentions consecrating objects. Consecrating Life is not listed as one of the powers of Prime 2, but in that section there are rules for consecrating living things. Because Enchanting Patterns and Creating Periapts are both split up with the living version being a higher rank of Prime, I read this as an editing mistake. Prime 1 should say Consecrate Object and Prime 2 should say Consecrate Life</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">520 \u2013 Consecrating living things requires Life 2/Prime 2 for simple organisms and Life 3/Prime 2 for complex. This is wrong on multiple levels, but the biggest is that consecrating objects doesn\u2019t require Matter so consecrating living things doesn\u2019t require Life. It\u2019s both or neither on this.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">520 \u2013 Same issue as above, enchanting living creatures with quintessence is stated to be Life 3/Prime 3. If you don\u2019t need Matter for the object you don\u2019t need Life for the being.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">521 \u2013 Same issue as above, enchanting living periapts is stated to be Life 5/Prime 5. If you don\u2019t need Matter for the object you don\u2019t need Life for the being.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">521 \u2013 Spirit 2/Life 2 to help other living creatures sense or contact the spirit realm. Neither of these should require Life.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">522 \u2013 Time 2, combined with Life, lets a mage read the probable past or future of a living thing. Presumably this is a locking effect to let the time sight track the creature.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c55a11\">523 \u2013 Time 3 with Forces, Life, or Matter 2 to affect other patterns. This would make sense as a specific version of the previous Rewind Time paragraph. It would be a Rewind Time effect anchored to a living creature rather than the entire area. However, this is part of a list of other effects, \u201caffect other patterns is all we get and it is not at all clear what this means.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">523 \u2013 Time 3/Life 3/Mind 1 for a mage to go back in time while recalling events from the future. There is no need for Life 4 or Mind 1 for this. If the mage chose to include himself in a rewinding time effect (because two paragraphs previously it was stated he\u2019s normally pulled out of the flow of time for that) then he\u2019d need Life or Mind to preserve memories. For actual time travel his memories will be unaffected.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">523 \u2013 Time 4 and Life to capture beings in a bubble of time. If it\u2019s just the being and not anything else it\u2019s an effect locked to the being, so yes, that\u2019s Life 2.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">533 (Axis of Coincidence sidebar) \u2013 Life 5/Mind 5/Matter 4/</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Forces 3</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">/Prime 2 to create a fully functional taxi and driver. Forces is wrong, but the rest, including Life, is correct.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">543 \u2013 Life 3/Correspondence 3 to teleport a person into several different destinations at once. This is an example of making Correspondence damaging, so it is an example of Life being added to separate parts of the pattern. I was going to flag this from the Correspondence point of view too, as teleporting people is Corr 4, but this is teleporting smaller pieces of a person. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">543 \u2013 Time allegedly does not inflict damage unless paired with Life to age living things. There\u2019s no reason Time can\u2019t age living things on its own and ageing is not something that causes damage in the traditional sense. You certainly can\u2019t heal from it. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">However, causing damage by speeding up time across part of a living pattern would have quite damaging consequences and would be an example of a Time attack made possible by adding Life. In other words, the Life requirement was right but for the wrong reason. This is backed up by the next section, where a Life/Time attack would do agg damage because Life was involved. Ageing isn\u2019t aggravated damage, but massive internal bleeding from bloodflow problems might be.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">547 \u2013 Life magic alone cannot affect vampires, werebeasts, ghosts, spirits, or the fae. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Speaking for myself, I would let Life affect the purely physical side of werebeasts and fae, but the fera would get a bonus to resist and the chimerical side of the fae should be unaffected. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">562 \u2013 Entropy 2/Life 2/Spirit 1 to manipulate the probability of someone giving the mage a free lunch. This is an example of player thinking so the redundancy is fine. Still, Entropy alone can do this, and if Life is involved it is just a sensory effect, so it is Life 1.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">602 \u2013 The Life 3 version of Hands of Death allows the mage to target a target\u2019s pattern with a punch.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">602 \u2013 The Life 1 option for Right-Click allows Life senses to be incorporated into the effect. The Life 1/Matter 1 allows for x-ray vision on structures or organisms. Presumably, Life 1 could do that for living things on its own, but since the effect is both, the combo works.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">608 \u2013 Bullet Catch. Forces 2/Life 2/Time 2. Same effect as earlier. Same complaint as earlier.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">609 \u2013 Talons. Life 3, or 4 for others.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">610 \u2013 Witch\u2019s vengeance, as always, is a very open ended effect that basically just does bad things to the target (take your pick). Life 3 is the appropriate level for it, though.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">610 \u2013 The Notorious Vampire Lawn Chair is listed as Matter 5/Life 5. </span><span style=\"color:#548235\">Life 5 is correct and is close to the only thing in this entry that is.</span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\"> Matter 5 was chosen because, as the book explains it, Vampire is not on the Periodic Table of Elements. I can\u2019t say for certain that this is wrong, but the entire VLC entry is written up in a hostile manner (including calling it a \u201ctruly stupid spell\u201d) and invents rules to nerf the entire idea: </span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">It\u2019s allegedly always vulgar, even in sanctums. It\u2019s just so vulgar no paradigm allows it. No really, reality itself hates the very idea of this. Have we mentioned how vulgar this is.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">Vampires have natural resistances</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">It takes enough successes to damage the vampire to incapacitated. Transmutation doesn\u2019t usually do damage, but you need to pay for damage anyway. This is not a rule that applies to any other kind of transmutation. Even in the optional durability rules, a spell has to overcome durability (soak) not structure (health levels).</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">If you are using the optional divided successes rule, you then need additional successes for duration.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">If you are not using the optional divided successes rule\u2026 yes you are, because you still have to pay for duration with <i>additional</i> successes.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">Vampires with Protean or Vicissitude can transform back at a cost of 1 blood point per success the mage rolled.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Kindred automatically have to make a Frenzy roll at difficulty 8, regardless of if the spell succeeds. This is at least partially due to the utter humiliation of being a lawn chair.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">A frenzying vampire suddenly have the option of spending their entire blood pool to turn back.</span></span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Given all that, and that the Periodic Table of Elements is equally glib, I\u2019m inclined to say the Matter 5 requirement is another made up restriction. After all, carriages, computers, and robots aren't on the Periodic Table either, but they fall under Matter 4 just fine.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Harming a Vampire with Life requires Life 3/Matter 2. This is either because the matter part of vampires counts as simple matter (unlikely), or because Life is the main spell and Matter is augmenting it to work properly. In the former case, going from harming to transmuting is a jump from Matter 2 to Matter 2, no change. In the latter case the augment is likely also Matter 2 (the first level of manipulation), though I could see an argument for needing Matter at one rank lower than Life. Whichever of those three we use, lawn chairs still fall under Matter 4, so the spell is Life 5/Matter 4. </span></span></span><br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T10:12:45-08:00","id":1530649,"title":"","content":"I took a break from going through M20 to try and give a similar treatment to HDYDT. So I started at the beginning and tried tracking the uses of Correspondence in that book. That was not a wise decision. I'd forgotten how rough the Ward and Co-Location sections were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T06:27:16-08:00","id":1532155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1529714#post1529714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd go with the former, as the latter runs into the dual problem that the Forces <i>mage </i>has no problem sending any of them and that what you're describing seems to have more to do with the Coincidental/Vulgar divide than the number of dots required for an Effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forces is my least favorite sphere because of its arbitrary character.<br /> <br /> The way I do it is divide &quot;Higher Forces&quot; as nuclear and &quot;Lower Forces&quot; as everything else.<br /> <br /> Coincidental/Vulgar is not the case here, if you give someone radiation poisoning out of the blue, it won't be considered coincidental. Just ask the Russians if how many of the opposition to Putin suddenly drinking Polonium's teas is just a coincidence....<br /> <br /> Edit: I guess there's a case to be made as to place Electromagnetism under Forces 4/5, along with nuclear forces/radiation.<br /> <br /> Every single Sphere differ from its levels by theme/complexity. Not a single one is simply &quot;just the same as previous, but more&quot;. More of the same is not a higher level, but simply more successes in the die. Thus, if you wanna implant a simple false memory into someone, that may be a 1 or 2 successes only with Mind 4, but if you want to completely mind-grape them, brainwashing someone into a completely new person, that might be 20+ successes.<br /> <br /> Creating a &quot;simple&quot; AI however, will still be Mind 5, even if it requires less successes than brainwashing someone into oblivion with Mind 4.<br /> <br /> I consider Nuclear Forces (radiation) to be more complex than Heat, Light, Movement or Magnetism, that's my reasoning behind such differentiation.<br /> <br /> I even call &quot;Radiation&quot; as &quot;Hellish/Celestial Fire&quot; for all those medieval mages that knew nothing about &quot;Nuclear Forces&quot;.<br /> <br /> That has a... Peculiar phenomenon on my games... Where yes, it opens up the possibility for &quot;demons&quot; and &quot;angels&quot; to actually be using RADIATION as a source of &quot;purifying fire&quot;. That's not necessarily true, but it's something that can be explored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 03-07-2024, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T07:09:28-08:00","id":1532158,"title":"","content":"Very late to the minor vs major Forces discussion, but I always envisioned it as more the complexity/magnitude of the force pattern vs the type of force. Making a burst of radiation would still be minor. The severity of it is limited by your ability as a mage to muster successes for it. Trying to exert control over weather patterns, plate tetonics, the tradewinds, the tides? Things that might just require a simple nudge to produce catastrophic results? Those are major forces. Want to introduce your own complex pattern into the mix? Like a fully formed hurricane in the middle of the Sahara? You ain't doing that until you've mastered Forces","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T08:49:25-08:00","id":1532163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1529716#post1529716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bear in mind that the reason why magnitude is a factor in Forces is because someone pointed out to Brucato while he was writing M20 that the higher difficulty that comes with higher Sphere requirements means fewer successes, which in turn means that if you want a powerful Effect you're better off using a two-dot Effect than a five-dot Effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohhhhhhh... Yeah, that absolutely explains a lot.<br /> <br /> That however, was a poor rationalization of the aspects of the game, and has also created a lot of unnecessary confusion.<br /> <br /> It conflates 2 aspects that are not mutual: complexity and difficulty.<br /> <br /> For example: a heart surgery is highly complex, and while I'm not suggesting that it is an easy process by any means, we still have thousands of heart surgeons worldwide.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, spreading paint into a canvas is pretty simple, but there's only one Michelangelo in the world and only one Sistine Chapel.<br /> <br /> So, maybe we could roughly say that, while a heart surgery may be dif 8, it may &quot;only&quot; require 3 successes (just a some random numbers here, that's probably unrealistic but it's just to illustrate), painting something may be just did 4, but &quot;David and God&quot; at the Sistine Chapel may very well be in the realm of 30+ successes for Michelangelo.<br /> <br /> Therefore, keeping the analogy... In fact, let's come up with some concrete examples:<br /> <br /> For all of the bellow, let's consider that it is being done in the Magus Chantry (therefore it is all &quot;Coincidental&quot; - AKA dif = highest sphere +3):<br /> <br /> Life 2: let's go with Harry Potter's willow tree - you know, that one that actively attacks anyone in close proximity<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200bLife 2 +3 = dif 5<br /> <br /> Plants don't naturally move around, they don't have muscles or nervous systems or even nervous cells, after all.<br /> <br /> Therefore, this might require at least 10 successes, maybe more, given how you would basically be needing to &quot;rewrite&quot; its entire pattern for that accomplishment (needless to say, this is a super Paradox magnet outside of your Chantry)<br /> <br /> So, while this effect is relatively simple, it is nevertheless very hard.<br /> <br /> Mind 4: let's change somebody's memory.<br /> <br /> Mind 4 +3 = dif 7<br /> <br /> A very minor &quot;brainwash&quot;, here we will change the color of the dress of a girl that a subject saw yesterday, from purple to red.<br /> <br /> So, the target will remember the girl he has wearing red, instead of the true color that was purple.<br /> <br /> Maybe a single success or 2 would suffice.<br /> <br /> Therefore, while it being more &quot;complex&quot;, it is still easier to accomplish.<br /> <br /> Keeping up with the analogy: building a hut may be very simple, but building a large and cozy hut may require lots of successes, while surgery may be highly complex and require many years of study, but many minor surgeries can be accomplished very easily and quickly by skilled doctors.<br /> <br /> If Bruccato had come with this approach from the beginning, a lot of the messes would be different","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T09:16:18-08:00","id":1532166,"title":"","content":"Also, Matter has the same problem but solves it completely differently. The vast majority of the forms of matter mages will work with fall under Matter 2/3. Rocks, water, air, plastics, metals, etc are all there. Only radioactive materials are such a strange form of Matter they naturally go higher. So instead of making a division between simple and complex types of matter, Matter makes a distinction between simple and composite matter. Matter made of a single or simple substance, like rock, falls under Matter 2, but complicated assemblies of different matters, like computers, fall under Matter 4.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying this is the right way of handling things because Matter certainly has its own problems, but if we applied the same philosophy to Forces, simpler applications of a single force would fall under Forces 2/3 and more complicated applications involving multiple forces would be 4/5. Levitation (momentum), invisibility (light), and lightning bolts (electricity) for the former, Storms (momentum, electricity, and heat) and multisensory illusions (light, sound, momentum) would be the latter.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T09:31:41-08:00","id":1532167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Becksworth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1532158#post1532158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very late to the minor vs major Forces discussion, but I always envisioned it as more the complexity/magnitude of the force pattern vs the type of force. Making a burst of radiation would still be minor. The severity of it is limited by your ability as a mage to muster successes for it. Trying to exert control over weather patterns, plate tetonics, the tradewinds, the tides? Things that might just require a simple nudge to produce catastrophic results? Those are major forces. Want to introduce your own complex pattern into the mix? Like a fully formed hurricane in the middle of the Sahara? You ain't doing that until you've mastered Forces</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is that &quot;controlling the tectonic plates&quot; is not &quot;more complex&quot;, it is &quot;simple&quot; movement. Making a coin fly is NOT more complex than making a mountain fly, it's just a lot easier. But it is basically the same process.<br /> <br /> In game mechanic terms, that is reflected in amount of successes required, instead of higher sphere / difficult requirements.<br /> <br /> Just think about it in terms of any of the other 8 spheres. Imagine for example turning an entire city into Silver.<br /> <br /> Hard? No doubt that would be hard. 100 success required? Maybe more.<br /> <br /> Regardless, that would STILL be only Matter 2. Transmuting things into a simple pattern, no matter how outlandish the feat, is still only Matter 2, because basic transmutation is a fairly simple process.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, turning a small knife into &quot;Adamatium&quot; or &quot;Vibranium&quot; may require just 3 successes, but it would be Matter 5.<br /> <br /> Creating a highly improbably &quot;Looney Tunes Coyote&quot; style of a trap that require hundreds of sets of unlikely circumstances to set off would be Entropy 2 with a ton of successes, while making your new business prosper just a little bit beyond on a safe basis would be Entropy 5 with maybe just 5 successes.<br /> <br /> In keeping up with this trend, there's no real difference between summoning a gentle breeze and the hurricane in Jupiter that is 2 times bigger than Earth (the red spot in Jupiter); the only difference between those is a matter of scale rather than complexity.<br /> <br /> Likewise, turning a small rock into gold or turning the Mount Everest into gold, both are just Matter 2, the difference is simply one of scale, not of complexity.<br /> <br /> It's like the difference between walking around the corner or doing a &quot;Flash&quot; thing of walking around the entire planet. It's still &quot;just&quot; walking. Sure, if you decide to &quot;walk&quot; the entire circumference of the globe (and assuming you can walk over water), that may take you a few years to accomplish, but it's still the same simple process of moving one leg after the other.<br /> <br /> The difference between walking around the corner or around the world, is a simple difference between 15 minutes of effort versus a few years (AKA the &quot;amount of successes&quot;).<br /> <br /> Differentiating between &quot;movement, light, heat, electromagnetic&quot; and &quot;nuclear&quot; forces is a way to make that distinction being made for complexity.<br /> <br /> We can after all say that nuclear forces, being connected to the interior of the atom, is more &quot;complex&quot; than forces that are inherently at the molecular level - heat is the movement of the particles, light is photons, electromagnetic is the movement of the electrons. Meanwhile, the strong and weak nuclear forces are the ones that allow all the different atoms to exist.<br /> <br /> This is just an idea; maybe you could come up with some different categorization; the Life Sphere for instance turns anything other than Vertebrates as &quot;simple life&quot;, while Vertebrates is &quot;complex&quot;. That's likewise debatable, but it is very functional for game purposes. I favor the idea of having nuclear forces as &quot;complex&quot;, because I also like to call it &quot;Hell Fire&quot; for traditionalist non-scientific views. Therefore, for non Technocrats/Technomamcers, &quot;Higher Forces&quot; would be something akin to the &quot;Fire of the Gods / Demonic Fire&quot; or something like it, and I really liked that idea (playing with the idea that &quot;radiation&quot; would be a completely alien concept for a medieval person, which would most likely view it as some sort of divine/demonic power). So, in my opinion, that would be an interesting division that plays out for both &quot;scientific&quot; and &quot;mystical&quot; classifications, which is one of the core points of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T09:57:27-08:00","id":1532169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1532166#post1532166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Matter has the same problem but solves it completely differently. The vast majority of the forms of matter mages will work with fall under Matter 2/3. Rocks, water, air, plastics, metals, etc are all there. Only radioactive materials are such a strange form of Matter they naturally go higher. So instead of making a division between simple and complex types of matter, Matter makes a distinction between simple and composite matter. Matter made of a single or simple substance, like rock, falls under Matter 2, but complicated assemblies of different matters, like computers, fall under Matter 4.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying this is the right way of handling things because Matter certainly has its own problems, but if we applied the same philosophy to Forces, simpler applications of a single force would fall under Forces 2/3 and more complicated applications involving multiple forces would be 4/5. Levitation (momentum), invisibility (light), and lightning bolts (electricity) for the former, Storms (momentum, electricity, and heat) and multisensory illusions (light, sound, momentum) would be the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be problematic because turning one Force into another is already Forces 3. For instance, absorbing environmental light to turn it into a fireball is Forces 3. <br /> <br /> As it currently stands, turning a hurricane into an earthquake would be forces 5 (although I would also disagree here because both are just movement, but alas)<br /> <br /> By doing what you propose, Forces 3 and 5 would become redundant, since any such interactions between different types of Forces would automatically require higher Sphere levels. Therefore, turning heat/cold into light/darkness would no longer be Forces 3, but Forces 4, and Forces 3 would not really have anything about it...<br /> <br /> I agree about Matter... Matter is a solution but perhaps, an inelegant one... In theory, I could create a computer using Matter 2 alone, as long as I transmute each component separately and assemble them later on, so I could do it by a huge amount of effects done in sequence. Yeah... A bit not ideal perhaps.<br /> <br /> As for a &quot;lightning storm&quot;, or hurricane with thunderbolts, sure, 2 &quot;forces&quot; at once. But still, I don't think that's a good solution because then Forces 3 would have no role. Besides, I'm not sure that's exactly more complex rather than just harder; heat and &quot;movement&quot; or &quot;sound&quot; are basically the same thing - it's all just movement, merely at different scales. Even electromagnetic forces can essentially be boiled down to just movement. <br /> <br /> Gravity and nuclear forces are different thou (oh yes, I had forgotten about Gravity previously), which is why I lump them up under Forces 4 and 5.<br /> <br /> By doing this division, that has allowed me to create a somehow more &quot;grounded&quot; Forces 6 Arch-Sphere that doesn't involve something silly as &quot;throwing Jupiter out of orbit&quot;. For my Arch Sphere Forces, I use &quot;Unnatural Forces&quot; and &quot;Force Immunity&quot;. Force Immunity turns the subject completely immune to one (or more) Force types. You could &quot;walk&quot; inside the Sun using Forces 6 by rendering yourself immune to Heat and Pressure/Gravity for instance.<br /> <br /> Forces 6 &quot;Force Immunity&quot; turns you literally into the proverbial &quot;immovable object&quot;, since turning yourself immune to kinetic forces basically means that your body would behave like the fictional &quot;Vibranium&quot; metal - anything that hits you simply bounds back without losing ANY energy on the process.<br /> <br /> Using this on a frisbee means that this disco would bounce infinitely until finally being launched into the endless space.<br /> <br /> The part of the &quot;Unnatural Forces&quot; I'm still working on... I didn't want silly stuff like &quot;Force that turns dwarves green&quot;. Maybe human imagination just isn't enough for concocting something truly alien in that aspect, but I'm still working on it, and the concept still exists - AKA you can create a &quot;new force type&quot;. Maybe &quot;magnetism for non-metals&quot;? For instance, a &quot;magnet&quot; that attracts glass, or creating &quot;hidro-magnetism&quot;, or even &quot;earth-magnetism&quot;, and considering that you can already control fire or air movement with previous levels, now you can cosplay Aang, the last Airbender from the anime Avatar.<br /> <br /> Well, those are my thoughts on Forces, and that's what I have always applied on my tables.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T10:45:57-08:00","id":1532174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1532169#post1532169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would be problematic because turning one Force into another is already Forces 3. For instance, absorbing environmental light to turn it into a fireball is Forces 3.<br /> <br /> As it currently stands, turning a hurricane into an earthquake would be forces 5 (although I would also disagree here because both are just movement, but alas)<br /> <br /> By doing what you propose, Forces 3 and 5 would become redundant, since any such interactions between different types of Forces would automatically require higher Sphere levels. Therefore, turning heat/cold into light/darkness would no longer be Forces 3, but Forces 4, and Forces 3 would not really have anything about it...</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't suggesting taking it that far. Forces 3 would be the transmutation of the single forces covered by Forces 2, Forces 5 would be the transmutation of the complex forces of Forces 4. Light could become sound, or quintessence lightning at Forces 3 (with Prime 2 in the latter case). But light couldn't become a storm, nor a storm light without Forces 5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I agree about Matter... Matter is a solution but perhaps, an inelegant one... In theory, I could create a computer using Matter 2 alone, as long as I transmute each component separately and assemble them later on, so I could do it by a huge amount of effects done in sequence. Yeah... A bit not ideal perhaps. </div> </div> </div>Also Matter puts transmutation at Matter 2 but Alteration at Matter 3. That is, you can change ice into rock at Matter 2, but changing ice into water (which doesn't change its substance) is explicitly a higher rank. <br /> <br /> Also, also, the examples keep forgetting that simple and complex is 2 and 4 respectively, and keeps putting slightly complicated objects, like inlayed daggers, at Matter 3. It's not that that is unbalanced or wrong, per se, its just that there is no mention of this ability in the Matter 3 writeup.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gravity and nuclear forces are different thou (oh yes, I had forgotten about Gravity previously), which is why I lump them up under Forces 4 and 5. </div> </div> </div>True, gravity is consistently listed as Forces 4/5. I always forget that because there's very little a mage can do with gravity manipulation that he can't do at lower ranks by altering force and momentum. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By doing this division, that has allowed me to create a somehow more &quot;grounded&quot; Forces 6 Arch-Sphere that doesn't involve something silly as &quot;throwing Jupiter out of orbit&quot;. For my Arch Sphere Forces, I use &quot;Unnatural Forces&quot; and &quot;Force Immunity&quot;. Force Immunity turns the subject completely immune to one (or more) Force types. You could &quot;walk&quot; inside the Sun using Forces 6 by rendering yourself immune to Heat and Pressure/Gravity for instance.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> The part of the &quot;Unnatural Forces&quot; I'm still working on... I didn't want silly stuff like &quot;Force that turns dwarves green&quot;. Maybe human imagination just isn't enough for concocting something truly alien in that aspect, but I'm still working on it, and the concept still exists - AKA you can create a &quot;new force type&quot;. Maybe &quot;magnetism for non-metals&quot;? For instance, a &quot;magnet&quot; that attracts glass, or creating &quot;hidro-magnetism&quot;, or even &quot;earth-magnetism&quot;, and considering that you can already control fire or air movement with previous levels, now you can cosplay Aang, the last Airbender from the anime Avatar. </div> </div> </div>Unnatural Forces and Forces that don't already exist, such as the magnetism for non metals (which is a really good example) should probably be the stuff of Forces 5. That's the level that Matter gets the ability to make new and impossible substances. If magnetic alcohol is possible at Matter 5, a force that attracts alcohol should be available at Forces 5.<br /> <br /> Of course I'm not in favor of locking anything behind rank 6. I take the stance that all the things mages do should be theoretically possible with ranks 1-5. Maybe not feasible, but theoretically possible.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T12:50:31-08:00","id":1532181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1532174#post1532174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wasn't suggesting taking it that far. Forces 3 would be the transmutation of the single forces covered by Forces 2, Forces 5 would be the transmutation of the complex forces of Forces 4. Light could become sound, or quintessence lightning at Forces 3 (with Prime 2 in the latter case). But light couldn't become a storm, nor a storm light without Forces 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see, but I still find it a bit weird. I could use Forces 3 to turn the wind into a thunderbolt, or Forces 4 to make a wind thunderstorm? But them, what would Forces 5 do? Turn a windy thunderstorm into a rain of fire? Why not just simply summoning a Fire Rain with Forces 4 then?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also Matter puts transmutation at Matter 2 but Alteration at Matter 3. That is, you can change ice into rock at Matter 2, but changing ice into water (which doesn't change its substance) is explicitly a higher rank. </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, I forgot about that. Yes, turning a concrete wall into a solid gold wall is matter 2, but making a hole into it is matter 3. Pretty nonsensical if you ask me. Or turning ice into vapor is matter 3.<br /> <br /> Yes, that has always been another change that I make in my games. Transubstantiation I always put at Matter 3, while Changing Stage or Changing Form at Matter 2. Molding a rock with the power of your mind (or spirits or gods or &quot;da science&quot;) is undoubtedly less complex than transmutating it into napalm or sulphuric acid.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, also, the examples keep forgetting that simple and complex is 2 and 4 respectively, and keeps putting slightly complicated objects, like inlayed daggers, at Matter 3. It's not that that is unbalanced or wrong, per se, its just that there is no mention of this ability in the Matter 3 writeup. </div> </div> </div>That's what I always refer as &quot;going for the feeling&quot; rather than what the &quot;formula&quot; tells. An item is either simple - AKA no distinct parts to it - or complex - AKA 2 or more distinct parts.<br /> <br /> Therefore, filling a cup with water and 1 ice cube should be &quot;complex&quot;, while turning a rock castle into wood should be &quot;simple&quot;.<br /> <br /> But then, the writers &quot;feel&quot; that a simple dagger, although having two distinct parts to it (the blade and the wrist), is too &quot;simple&quot; to truly qualify, while at the same time they get cognitive dissonance due to the &quot;formula&quot; that clearly states that &quot;more than one part is complex&quot;, and thus to solve the dissonance they decide to &quot;go for a middle ground&quot; based on these feelings, and put a sample of &quot;that's Matter 3&quot;, just creating confusion because when anybody tries to check out what Matter 3 does (aka changing the physical stage of the matter or changing the form of the matter), none of that applies to the effect, and thus it just gives the impression that Sphere levels and proper effects are just randomly placed based on what &quot;feels right&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> True, gravity is consistently listed as Forces 4/5. I always forget that because there's very little a mage can do with gravity manipulation that he can't do at lower ranks by altering force and momentum. </div> </div> </div>Yes, the ability to alter gravity is very forgettable given exactly those factors that you listed.<br /> <br /> But that just adds insult to the injury. Why can't you &quot;manipulate lower gravity&quot; at levels 2/4 and &quot;greater gravity&quot; at levels 4/5?<br /> <br /> Can you see how nothing under Forces makes the slight sense, and why organizing them by &quot;Force type&quot; would be far better, turning it into a &quot;hierarchy of complexity&quot;?<br /> <br /> As for the practical uses of gravity manipulation, I can think of very little other than Weight control of objects. That would be useful for Deep Space projects, and of limited use elsewhere. It sure makes easier training Sayans into Super Sayans...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unnatural Forces and Forces that don't already exist, such as the magnetism for non metals (which is a really good example) should probably be the stuff of Forces 5. That's the level that Matter gets the ability to make new and impossible substances. If magnetic alcohol is possible at Matter 5, a force that attracts alcohol should be available at Forces 5.<br /> <br /> Of course I'm not in favor of locking anything behind rank 6. I take the stance that all the things mages do should be theoretically possible with ranks 1-5. Maybe not feasible, but theoretically possible. </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... Good point. I like the idea of &quot;Arch-Spheres&quot; as a concept, but it's hard to come by something that isn't cartoonish. I like to have a single Lvl 6 for Arch Spheres; those stuff from &quot;Masters of the Arts&quot; with lvls 6 to 9 is just silly. <br /> <br /> But in order for that to be possible, something has to be left out for them. And I always like to keep the level 6 for the &quot;stuff that is utterly impossible&quot;. I created a few ideas, but never implemented it exactly because I couldn't come up with solutions for all. For instance, Prime 6 allows you to turn objects or even living beings into NODES. Yeah, you could become a walking and talking Node by being a Prime Archmage. Life 6 would allow for the reproduction of your creations. Did you just use Life 5 to create Xenomorphs at your lab? Well, congratulations, now that you are an Archmage in Life, Xenomorphs are a new species that no longer needs your labs to exist (that would be a terrible, terrible idea, but you can do it). Time 6 of course is easy, is travel to the past.<br /> <br /> I had a few problems with other spheres. Correspondence was challenging. For Corr 6 I decided to go for &quot;Omnipresence&quot; which I already described somewhere else in this forum - you are no longer limited to being simply &quot;somewhere&quot;, instead being able to cohexist simultaneously &quot;anywhere&quot;, with the only limit being where your attention is focusing; this has also the implication that, no matter where or on what you're focusing an effect at, it is ALWAYS considered as &quot;targeting yourself&quot;, since everything is part of you and you are part of everything. Therefore, you don't need extra successes for &quot;targeting others&quot;. And a few other perks to it that I concocted.<br /> <br /> Mind 6 was almost mind blowing to imagine, so I tried to mind blown myself into it... The best I could come up with was &quot;Change the Collective Unconscious&quot;. I inspired myself in the ideas of the &quot;Newspeak&quot; from the book 1984, and how changing language can alter the thought. Therefore, an Archmage of Mind could for example change the collective idea of peace to &quot;non-war&quot;, and henceforth the entire Tellurian would no longer understand what &quot;peace&quot; means, just having the idea about intermissions between wars.<br /> <br /> I also took inspiration based on a Voormas story that he changed the concept of &quot;Necromancy&quot; to meaning &quot;uniting the world of the living and the dead&quot;. Let's suppose that the original idea of &quot;Necromancy&quot; meant &quot;keep the balance between life and death and separate the two worlds&quot;, but Voormas changed that using Mind 6 and now everybody dwelling in Necromancy always try to summon the dead into the world of the living because of that.<br /> <br /> Entropy 6 was my biggest challenge. So, I went with the &quot;Generator of Infinite Possibilities&quot; from the book &quot;The Hitckhiker's guide to the Galaxy&quot;. So, more or less a &quot;generator of impossibilities&quot;. Anything that is impossible, is possible for Entropy 6&quot;. That's the basic idea of it, I won't go into details because it's a bit long.<br /> <br /> But Matter 6 has proved to be impossible without being silly, because any sort of &quot;impossible&quot; that could be put into it, was already covered by Matter 6. Black Holes? Matter 5. Adamantium? Matter 5. A plastic that is &quot;insubstantial&quot; to anything except Leprechauns? Matter 5 (possibly with Life/Spirit 1 also). <br /> <br /> So, no room at all for anything else. But I gotta say, I liked your argument of simply getting away with all that idea of going for lvl 6 (or even more). So, maybe I should just put all of the above under the lvl 5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T17:00:49-08:00","id":1532211,"title":"","content":"For archspheres, I like setting 6 as \u201cwhatever 5 still doesn't cover\u201d; and 7+, if they exist at all, shouldn't be new Effects (there simply aren't enough of those to spread out over two levels let alone four or five). Instead, have archsphere ranks start providing ways to make successes provide more bang for the buck. <b>Prism of Focus</b> has a chapter suggesting some options in this regard. <br /> <br /> As well, one you start getting into the Archsphere levels, the difficulties start getting absurd: a rank 6 effect has Difficulty 9 when it's <i>Coincidental</i>; Vulgar is either Difficulty 10 (as in, the number of dice you roll doesn't matter; it's always a 50/50 crapshoot) or Difficulty 9 with an added success needed. By the time you get up to Rank 9, even taking the maximum difficulty reduction (\u20133) isn't enough to reduce a Coincidental effect below a Difficulty of 9. For this reason as well, I don't think there should be Effects that require more than 6 dots in a Sphere; and even that's pushing it. <br /> <br /> So more than 6 ranks shouldn't <i>unlock</i> more Effects; it should just let you do better with the Effects you <i>can </i>perform \u2014 which, at that point, could be all of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T21:00:26-07:00","id":1532536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1529438#post1529438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Special Mention - Consecration<br /> <br /> Prime 1 specifically mentions that a mage can consecrate an item to himself so that it will change metaphysically when he does. This includes when he shapeshifts and when he steps sideways. Indeed, having an item (or clothing) that travels with you is one of the primary purposes of this. Well don't tell that to the Otherworlds section. In that section, it is unnecessary for stepping sideways and not enough for astral or agama travel, which require Prime 2 + 5 successes on a willpower roll and Entropy 3/Prime 2 respectively.<br /> <br /> You can make the argument that the Agama Sojourn and the Astral Sojourn involve you leaving your body while just stepping sideways does not. That would certainly make sense. But then the two sojourn sections say to bring items they need to be metaphysically bound to the character and that's what consecration does.<br /> <br /> Given the explicit wording of Prime 1, I think it overrides the Otherworlds possessions sections and a lot of wordcount was wasted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just found this (man, I'll really have to revise this entire topic someday when I have some time). Absolutely. Consecration should absolutely allow things to &quot;join in&quot; during astral or agama journey, or entering the Digital Web or any other kind of &quot;spirit travel&quot; upon which you go as an ephemeral &quot;Body of Light&quot;, which is described under Prime 2, and leave your body behind.<br /> <br /> I do agree that is unnecessary for stepping sideways, since you are basically ripping the &quot;space-time-continuum&quot;, the fabric of existence that separates the material and the ephemeral planes.<br /> <br /> This does however requires some considerations about the differences between Spirit 3 and Spirit 4.<br /> <br /> Spirit 3 is &quot;stepping sideways&quot;. Or... Let's call it... Changing your &quot;quantum vibration&quot; so that you &quot;switch phases&quot;. And yes, there's a very didactic reason for my specific pseudoscience technobabble here. Because, unlike that, Spirit 4 is a literal &quot;wormwhole between dimensions&quot;. You rip apart the &quot;barrier&quot; between the material and the spiritual dimensions with Spirit 4. Meanwhile, with Spirit 3 you are simply &quot;switching phases&quot;.<br /> <br /> Let me use an example from DC comics: in the DC Comics, each universe of the multiverse exists in theory at the &quot;same space&quot;, but on &quot;different frequencies&quot;, or at different &quot;vibrations&quot; of their &quot;quantum packages&quot;... And this may very well be true for the real world, under many of the string theories of physics.<br /> <br /> So, bellow the atoms, bellow quarks and neutrinos and all subatomic particles, everything (theoretically) reduces to strings... Strings that vibrate.<br /> <br /> Therefore, each universe has its own &quot;frequence&quot;.<br /> <br /> And, if you could, theoretically, change the &quot;frequency&quot; of your entire body at a quantum level, and say, &quot;adjust&quot; said frequency to be in tune with the frequency of another parallel universe, then well.. Then you would &quot;step sideways&quot; into that other universe without moving into the axis of the space-time (so, a theoretical change of position on the axis of a 5th dimension while remaining still on the 4D axis of Space-Time?).<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's more or less how Spirit 3 works.<br /> <br /> Spirit 4 however would be like a Wormhole (or a &quot;Gate&quot;), but instead of connecting 2 different points at the Space-Time like Correspondence 4 does, it connects the &quot;Material Realm&quot; with the &quot;Spirit Realm&quot; (or, maybe what it actually does is to connect 2 points across a 5 dimensional plane? Rather than connecting space, it connects &quot;dimensions&quot;?)<br /> <br /> Which finally leads me with the problem: I recon that, if you wanna bring clothes and weapons and cars and a house to the spirit Realm using Spirit 3, yes you shouldn't need Prime 1, HOWEVER, the target of the spell no longer is only &quot;self&quot;, and therefore it should be necessary more successes to do so, depending on the amount of targets to be transported/overall size of the items, according to the table of successes required for feats.<br /> <br /> One other thing to take in consideration in this case and that is almost forgotten about Consecration, or at least I never heard about it anywhere else other than in the description of the effect, is that Consecration turns the item as basically the same as the saliva or blood sample of the Mage (or, if the Mage Consecrates an item towards another person or another living being or even Consecrate 2 objects towards one anothee), it's like having a hair of the subject.<br /> <br /> A Consecrated knife functions in Magikal terms as a finger of the subject. A Mage can use Corr 2 to find his consecrated keys in Japan without needing any extra successes, because it's like using Corr 2 to just look himself at a mirror. <br /> <br /> For this reason, Consecration would be VERY useful while stepping sideways, even if absolutely unnecessary, because it will make the process so much easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-13T12:20:01-07:00","id":1538532,"title":"","content":"Hey Ramnesis, how bout giving another spin at the sphere's inconsistencies? Which ones are still left?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T09:06:03-07:00","id":1538607,"title":"","content":"I'll post some soon. Matter is done, I'm working on Time and Mind now. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T09:09:52-07:00","id":1538608,"title":"","content":"Would you mind if I were to borrow ideas from here to produce more functional <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385360-fields-for-the-technocracy-reloaded\">Fields for the Technocracy</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T09:49:57-07:00","id":1538612,"title":"","content":"I have no problems with it. What kind of ideas are you finding useful?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T11:52:43-07:00","id":1538620,"title":"","content":"While my main focus has been on splitting up existing Spheres and recombining them into a new arrangement that's similar but not the same (e.g., dividing Correspondence into Data and Space, and dividing Entropy between Data and Time), I've been finding your examination of just what each Sphere does and doesn't do to be useful. As a simple example, you mention in the very first post here that Correspondence doesn't officially provide anything like flight or levitation, though that's a long-standing unofficial capability of that Sphere; I intend to make that an integral part of the Technocratic Field of Space.<br /> <br /> I had originally been planning on removing that from Energy (a Field that's largely the same as Forces) along with movement and gravitational effects in general; but your post suggests a way that the two can coexist (i.e., levitation is Forces 2 or Correspondence 3), and I'm now thinking of going with that. <br /> <br /> More generally, I'm planning to write up the Energy Field taking the thoughts in this thread about Forces into account. Likewise with the other Fields corresponding to the Pattern Spheres, once you're done analyzing them. Those will likely be the easiest to write up, since their purviews are the same; Mind, too, once you've posted your analysis of it. And while I'm completely doing away with Entropy, the analysis of what each level ought to provide will be useful in filling out the capabilities of Data (for probability-based Effects) and Time (for aging-based Effects). <br /> <br /> Things like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T14:06:38-07:00","id":1538624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538620#post1538620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While my main focus has been on splitting up existing Spheres and recombining them into a new arrangement that's similar but not the same (e.g., dividing Correspondence into Data and Space, and dividing Entropy between Data and Time), I've been finding your examination of just what each Sphere does and doesn't do to be useful. As a simple example, you mention in the very first post here that Correspondence doesn't officially provide anything like flight or levitation, though that's a long-standing unofficial capability of that Sphere; I intend to make that an integral part of the Technocratic Field of Space.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's a shame that. But we can make some assessments based on what we have. Initially I thought about placing it under Correspondence 4, since that's the level that allows you shrienk or enlarge space; however, after some though, I believe it could just be Corr 3, since that's the lvl that allows you to actually transport stuff around (aka teleport); this could even be seeing as a series of innumerable sequential instant teleportations, giving the impression of movement (like a movie).<br /> <br /> So I would say, Corr 3 fits well enough for telekinesis <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I had originally been planning on removing that from Energy (a Field that's largely the same as Forces) along with movement and gravitational effects in general; but your post suggests a way that the two can coexist (i.e., levitation is Forces 2 or Correspondence 3), and I'm now thinking of going with that. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I would also advise on that. Movement is Kinetic Force. It fits with the Forces Sphere like a glove.<br /> <br /> Besides, without it, there would be no feasible justification for Forces to control sounds or the wind, or even vibration. All of those are kinetic energy; it's not just levitation and telekinesis.<br /> <br /> Additionally, without it, Forces would get heavily crippled. Forces 1 allows you to hear conversations across walls, detect intruders by vibrations in the ground or by detecting movement, and even a sort of indirect &quot;emotional reading&quot; by analyzing the heart beat of a target.<br /> <br /> And yes, you can get Corr 3 to have &quot;telekinesis&quot; as an alternative way towards Forces 2. Both work, with the difference being that Corr 3 &quot;moves&quot; things by changing their position in space, while Forces 2 change the kinetic energy of it.<br /> <br /> Forces can remain with gravity too; given full control over kinetic energy already, it is almost (if not absolutely) useless. But hey, let it be there, maybe someone can come up with something useful.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More generally, I'm planning to write up the Energy Field taking the thoughts in this thread about Forces into account. Likewise with the other Fields corresponding to the Pattern Spheres, once you're done analyzing them. Those will likely be the easiest to write up, since their purviews are the same; Mind, too, once you've posted your analysis of it. And while I'm completely doing away with Entropy, the analysis of what each level ought to provide will be useful in filling out the capabilities of Data (for probability-based Effects) and Time (for aging-based Effects).<br /> <br /> Things like that. </div> </div> </div>So, how about you give us some idea about what Data is about?<br /> <br /> I don't know what people have so against Entropy. To me it is one of the best well written Spheres, if not the best overall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T14:22:04-07:00","id":1538625,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:black\">Matter in M20</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:black\">Matter has a rather funky division that constantly trips me up. For Forces and Life, altering simple substances starts at rank 2, while transmutation requires rank 3. For Matter this is almost the reverse. Transmutation of simple matter starts at rank 2, but a mage can\u2019t alter many properties of matter until rank 3. I see some game balance logic to this, but that doesn\u2019t make it less tricky.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">415 \u2013A Life 3/Matter 3/Entropy 1 that explicitly uses Entropy to spot weak points. Great. Life and Matter make the spell damaging to vampires and Life makes it Agg damage. However, it is explicitly Life 3/Matter 2 to damage vampires with Life. Also, Entropy isn\u2019t accomplishing anything mechanical here.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">416 \u2013 Matter can turn clothing into light armor. No rank is given. I think it would be Matter 3. This is confirmed in the trinkets section.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">418 \u2013 Life and Matter don\u2019t affect spirits unless they take on a material form.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">422 (Thunder Punch Sidebar) \u2013 The Matter 2 variant is to damage materials.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">437 \u2013 A mage who understands demolitions might be able to shape and direct explosions with Matter or Forces. Assuming that the Matter version means fashioning the explosive to affect the direction that it will explode in, this is plausible.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">438 (Dodging the Blast sidebar)\u2013 Matter is one of the spheres that can be used for the optional Dodging the Blast rule.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">441 \u2013 Using the optional structure and durability rules, Matter is required to magically repair structure. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">440 \u2013 If using the optional Durability and Structure rules, Matter attacks reduce object durability by -2, and Matter augmented transmutation spells reduce it by -2 per success for the purposes of overcoming Durability.</span></span> </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">440 \u2013 Forces 2/Matter 2 to make an attack on a pillar. Forces for the attack, Matter to reduce its durability (Optional Rule)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c45911\">443 (Awakening Substances Sidebar) \u2013 Same issue as it was with Life. It\u2019s Matter 2 to enhance a substance, or Life 3/Matter 2 to enhance it if it is in someone. Unless it is part of their pattern that doesn\u2019t make a whole lot of sense. I will admit, it is much easier to think of an ingested substance being part of their pattern, though.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">464 \u2013 Matter 2 or 3 can be used to make enhanced materials. This isn\u2019t wrong, per se, but it needs explanation. Matter 2 can perfect simple matter by transmutation and Matter 3 by changing its form in optimal ways. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Matter 4 is required to perfect complex matter, though, and Matter 5 is required for impossible materials. Cold fusion batteries are listed as an example of enhancement and those would likely be Matter 5 or Forces 5. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">483 (Acclimation sidebar) \u2013 Optional acclimation rules. After 4 to 5 weeks in Otherworlds, mages have a +1 difficulty to pattern magics for 1-2 days.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">485 \u2013 Life and Matter don\u2019t work on umbral creatures or objects unless the originated in the material world (or presumably in a realm where Life and Matter work).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">485 \u2013 Forces and Matter do not work at all in the Low Umbra.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">508 \u2013 Transforming an object into air is stated to be a Forces 3/Matter 2 effect. Incorrect. Forces 3/Matter 2 is the combination to transmute a simple object into energy (such as making a brick disappear in a flash of light). Transforming an object into air is changing from one form of Matter into another and is the explicit domain of Matter 3. Forces would only be used if you were heating the object to the point it evaporated (in which case Matter would not be needed) or to accelerate the air into wind (Matter 3/Forces 2) or to convert the object into the energy imparted into existing air to blow it (Matter 3/Forces 3)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">508 \u2013 Matter 2/Prime 2 to reanimate bones and remains. Like Animate Corpse I really want to know what each one does. That said, unless the Pattern Sphere is just a locking one, this time it doesn\u2019t make sense at all.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">508 \u2013 Heal/Harm a vampire with Life 3/Matter 2. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">508 \u2013 Craft Periapt/Matrix is allegedly Matter 5/Prime 3 for inanimate objects. Craft Periapt is a signature power of Prime 3, so without a good explanation, it shouldn\u2019t need help. Indeed, the only Periapt related effect in Prime 3 doesn\u2019t call for Matter or Life. Admittedly the verbiage sounds like it is talking about filling an existing periapt, but that should be a power of Prime 2, not Prime 3. Also, the formatting is clearly wrong as it uses a \u201c/\u201d not a \u201c+\u201d for conjunctional effects. \u201c(Sphere) X+\u201d is supposed to mean this rank or higher, and as M20 doesn\u2019t cover archspheres,, Life 5+ doesn\u2019t make sense in this regard.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">509 \u2013 Forces 3/Prime 2 to summon wind is wrong. This should be either Forces 2 to accelerate air, Matter 2/Prime 2 to make air, or Forces 2/Matter 2/Prime 2 to make air and move it. Also, making earth, metal, or water is listed as Matter 3/Prime 2, which is also wrong. Summoning simple matter is Matter 2/Prime 2.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">509 \u2013 Conjure New Object is listed as Matter 3+/Prime 2. It\u2019s Matter 2+/Prime 2. Transmutation for Matter begins at 2.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">509 \u2013 Disintegrate an object is listed as Matter 3. That is the proper level to do a magical Matter attack on an object, which can be done regardless of the complexity of the object. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">509 \u2013 Consecrate/Harden/Perfect an object at Matter 3+ or Prime 2. Consecration of objects is Prime 1 and there is no Matter variant I can think of. Hardening an object can happen at Matter 2 and while Prime 2 can enchant one to resist Agg damage I wouldn\u2019t describe it as Hardening. Perfecting an object depends on what perfecting means, but would also start at Matter 2.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">509 \u2013 Levitation is listed as Forces 2+/Matter 2 or Correspondence 3/Matter 2.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">509 \u2013Transform Objects is Matter 2+/Appropriate Sphere 2. It is actually Matter 2+/Appropriate Sphere 3+. The only sphere that can Transmute (as opposed to Alter) at 2 is Matter and we wouldn\u2019t say Matter 2+/Matter 2+ then.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">509 \u2013 Reverse ageing on an object is Time 3+/Matter 2. Time and Matter should each be able to do this on their own at relevant levels. It may be reasonable to incorporate Matter into the Time spell if the intent is to de-age one part of an object without affecting another (such as de-ageing a computer while preserving the data), however, that only applies to the Time variant and it would require Matter 4 for something complex like a computer.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">509 \u2013 Create Multiple Objects is listed as Correspondence 5/Matter3/Prime 2. As stated in the Correspondence list, that has to be a misprint and it should actually read Correspondence 5 [i]or[i] Prime 2/Matter 2+</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">513 \u2013 Adding Matter to Correspondence 2 allows a mage to summon objects. This is on the very same page as the rule that Correspondence does not need help to summon whole patterns.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">513 \u2013 Combining Correspondence 3 with Matter (or other pattern spheres) allows a mage to \u201cmove things around from a distance, levitating them, manipulating or teleporting them without physical contact.\u201d Most of these can be done with Correspondence alone, and of the rest none involve Matter. If we are extremely broad in interpretation, \u201cmanipulating\u201d could include manipulating the form or state of an object, but if so that uses the abilities of Correspondence 2, not 3.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">513 \u2013 Correspondence 4 combined with Matter can ward against matter patterns. This is one case where correspondence does need the help. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">However, this section advises checking HDYDT for the rules. Don\u2019t bother, they aren\u2019t consistent.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c45911\">513 \u2013 As in the Forces list, Matter + Corr 5 to stretch or compress objects. This is too vague to be useful. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\"> If it means a special distortion locked to a pattern it technically works. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">If it means stretching or compressing a space such that those inside don\u2019t notice, I don\u2019t think you need a pattern sphere at all. If you are stretching or compressing the patterns you don\u2019t need Correspondence at all. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">I will add one thought since last time: if you are stretching or compressing the space of only part of the pattern, and if this will have some significant effect on the pattern, then you might need Matter or Life.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">516 \u2013 Combining Forces 3 with Matter lets a mage transform objects into energies. This is correct, </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">however, the example is changing water into air as Forces 3/Matter 3. Changing water into air would be Matter 3. Changing water into [i]wind]/i] would need Forces though it would arguably only be Matter 3/Forces 2: Matter to change and Forces to accelerate. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">516 \u2013 Attaching energies to objects is listed as requiring Matter 3. This clearly mentions flight as one of the outcomes so we know that in this case Matter is functioning as a locking sphere. That should only take Matter 2.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">517 \u2013 Transforming complex life into objects is stated to require Matter 3, but simple objects are possible so this should actually be Matter 2+. M20 sometimes assumes there is semi-complex matter that exists somewhere between the simple matter of Matter 2 and the complex matter of Matter 4, but nothing like that is listed in Matter 3.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">517 \u2013 Really confusing wording here. In the main Matter section it says Prime and Matter create solid forms from energy. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">This is technically true in the sense that they can create solid forms from primal energy</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">, but it implies Prime is needed to make solid forms from normal energies like fire and lightning. That would be Forces.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">517 \u2013 Many of the other examples in this list either don\u2019t need Matter or don\u2019t need anything but Matter.</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">\u201cEntropy erodes or reinforces Matter.\u201d When Entropy is doing this it doesn\u2019t need Matter. When Matter is doing this it doesn\u2019t need Entropy.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">\u201cForces transmutes inert elements into active ones.\u201d As in the water to wind example earlier, there are cases where this is true. There are more cases where Matter or Forces alone do the job.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">\u201cTime alters the temporal state of Matter\u2026\u201d again, without Matter\u2019s help.</span></span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">518 \u2013 In the Matter 2 section it says transmuting matter into living tissue is Life 4 or higher. This is wrong in two ways. Firstly it forgets about simple creatures, which require lower ranks, secondly the transmutation levels for Life are Life 3 for simple life and Life 5 for complex. Life 4 would only be involved when the mage is transforming his own body.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">520 \u2013 None of the examples listed for Matter 5 are Matter 5. Armor and lawn chairs are complex matter, so Matter 4. The argument that \u201cVampires are not on the periodic table of elements\u201d from the Vampire Lawn Chair section also puts them at Matter 4, not 5. Melting steel is either changing its state to liquid, so Matter 3, molding its shape in such a way that it appears to melt, also Matter 3, or changing its temperature, which is not Matter at all. Matter 5 would allow a mage to create a new kind of steel that was liquid at room temperature but that\u2019s not at all what is described.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">518 \u2013 Matter 2/Spirit 3 to convert ephemera into matter or matter to ephemera. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#c00000\">518 \u2013 Matter 2/Spirit 3 to awaken the spirit of an object. Nonsense, this is Spirit 3 alone.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c55a11\">518 \u2013 Permanent changes require Matter 5. This is an odd rule but its not the only time I\u2019ve seen something like it. This really needs more explanation. Are we talking about perpetual spells or permanent effects that continue once the spell ends. Without knowing the actual rule I am inclined to just ignore this line.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">519 \u2013 By joining Matter 3 with other spheres a mage can</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">Join inert matter to living tissue</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Disintegrate it to dust (Matter alone can do this, as can Entropy alone)</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Shift objects with the power of thought (Matter isn\u2019t involved here, and really, neither is Mind</span></span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">519 \u2013 Mind 1/Matter 1 to read the psychic impressions on a place or object. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">I\u2019m not sure Matter is needed for a place</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">, but it makes sense for objects.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">519 \u2013 Life 5/Matter 5 can turn vampires into lawn chairs. I missed this in the Life list, but there\u2019s no good reason for Matter to be at rank 5. Lawn chairs are at most rank 4 and some could be rank 2. It\u2019s also not rank 5 because the target is a vampire because mages can already hit vampires with direct damage with Life 3/Matter 2. Now the specific logic for this isn\u2019t given but there are two options: 1) mages always need to add Matter 2 to use Life on vampires, or 2) mages need to add Matter at one rank less than the rank of Life being used. I find the latter one quite clunky, but either way this is Matter 2 or Matter 4, not Matter 5.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">520 \u2013 Mind 3, combined with Corr, Forces, Matter, or Life can employ telekinesis, pyrokinesis, psychophysical assault, influencing objects, elements, or people with the power of the mind. Not only is Mind not used in any of these (with the possible exception of psychophysical assault), Matter isn\u2019t either. The vast majority of \u201cinfluencing objects or elements\u201d in any kind of psychic context wouldn\u2019t involve Matter. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">520 \u2013 Matter/Prime 2 to conjure objects from thin air.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">521 \u2013 In a strange turnabout that is most likely an editing error, pulling quintessence from a living sacrifice doesn\u2019t involve Life, but pulling it from an object does. Possibly the mention of Life 3 previously was supposed to refer to several of the other things in the list, but if so, it is still bad formatting because it can\u2019t apply to everything. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">This is one case where it actually would make sense to require Life or Matter for the effect.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">521 \u2013 It allegedly takes Matter 4 to craft a soulgem. No explanation is given for why this rank of Matter or why Prime needs the help, especially when crafting Periapts doesn\u2019t. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c55a11\">521 \u2013 Spirit 2/Matter 2 to imbue material objects with ephemeral power. This is really nonspecific, but most of the things it could reasonably mean do make sense at Spirit 2/Matter 2.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">522 \u2013 Spirit 3/Matter 3/Prime 2 to create short lived ephemeral objects. I marked this down as wrong in the Spirit list, but it is the appropriate combination for creating an object and converting it to ephemera. Now I would normally think that if you can convert ephemera to matter and vice versa at rank 3, you can convert it from primal energies at rank 3. However, Spirit 5 claims to be the rank for creating ephemera, so possibly this is a workaround. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c55a11\">Why creating ephemeral objects needs to be locked behind Spirit 5 I\u2019m not sure.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c55a11\">522 \u2013 Instill a soul within an empty shell of Matter. The capitalization implies Matter is necessary but doesn\u2019t actually say it. I\u2019d say that yes it is required. Creating a soul may be a clear power of Spirit, but installing it is not, and probably involves at least some manipulation of the pattern it is installed into.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">522 \u2013 Time 2, with Matter, can read the probably past or future of objects. Since spells need to be locked to patterns to follow them, this makes sense.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">523 \u2013 And we are back to the hazy rule that Time 3, along with Matter 2, can affect other patterns. There\u2019s not even enough meaning here to call wrong. This is only in red because of how badly it is written.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">523 \u2013 Trapping objects in a bubble of time is Time 4 and Matter. As with Life this could be a locking effect so this is at least plausible.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">524 \u2013 Data 2 and Matter lets a Technocrat modify Union tech from a distance. As a technocratic explanation of extending an effect at a distance this works.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">533 \u2013 Axis of Coincidence Sidebar \u2013 Matter 2/Prime 2 to create a flask from midair.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">533 \u2013 Axis of Coincidence Sidebar \u2013 Correspondence/Matter to conjure objects. Matter is not needed for complete patterns.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">533 \u2013 Axis of Coincidence Sidebar \u2013 Matter 4/</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Forces 3</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">/Life 5/Mind 5/Prime 2 to create a taxi driver from thin air. Forces only makes sense if it is important that the car is actively running. Batteries and gas can be Matter alone.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">562 \u2013 Corr 4/Time 3/Forces 2/Matter 2 to make a car go really fast. Correspondence and Time are making the car go fast and either one alone could do this. Forces and Matter are explicitly to handle the extra forces and stresses involved. There\u2019s no reason Correspondence or Time based movement should produce those. If the car is going to change speeds mid teleport then I could see the need for Forces, but Time would handle that too and it is already involved. Matter isn\u2019t necessary at all. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">Since this is a player generated effect and players can use more spheres than necessary if they want I\u2019m not going to complain about the addition of Forces or Matter, </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">however cars are complex objects so if the player did want to incorporate Matter, he would need Matter 4. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">563 \u2013 Correspondence 2/Matter 2/Mind 2 to set up a ward around a location that blocks scrying, sends out a <i>go away</i> impulse, and warns the mage if anyone breaches the barrier. Correspondence 2 tracks with setting the ward, the impulse and making the warning long distance. Wards are not a stated power of Corr 2 but apparently that was part of what thickening space was supposed to mean. Mind also tracks with both uses in the spell. Matter, has a use, but not a necessary one. It\u2019s clearly being used as a locking sphere. However, since the spell is explicitly on a location, it doesn\u2019t need to move with any object. That said, there are other benefits to locking, so this isn\u2019t completely superfluous.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">602 \u2013 The Matter 1 add on to Right Click is essentially a Matter perception spell. The Life 1/Matter 1 add on provides X-ray vision to living things and objects. No problem with either one.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">603 \u2013 Sanitize Evidence uses Matter 2/Forces 2 to evaporate evidence, but this should vary with the type of Matter being evaporated. Matter 2+/Forces 2. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">604 \u2013 The Matter part of the effect detects physical evidence, which is reasonable. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">608 \u2013 Penny\u2019s New Penny uses Time to determine what an object looked like when it was new and Matter to restore it to that state. The Matter 3 variant restores it to that condition. The Matter 4 recreates it from scratch. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Prime is not actually needed for either one</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">, though it <i>could</i> be used in the Matter 4 variant if the mage wanted to be especially convoluted (obliterating the original and creating the new one out of thin air, rather than just transmuting the old one into the new one). </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Prime has no place in the Matter 3 version.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">609 \u2013 Talons. The Matter 2 option lets the mage incorporate inorganic substances like silver into the talons.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">610 \u2013 The Vampire Lawn Chair. I don\u2019t really have anything to add since the Life list. This spell writeup is actively hostile to anyone who wants to use it, and because of that is actively hostile to any understanding of the rules. Wordcount was taken away from other things and given to this and that is a tragedy.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">612 \u2013 Jodi\u2019s Riot sidebar. Matter to warp bells so they sound discordant. No rank is given but it should be Matter 3.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">626 \u2013 Reprogramming a HIT Mark requires Matter 3/Mind 3/ Forces 2. This isn\u2019t altering the structure or form of the HIT Mark so I don\u2019t see what Matter is doing.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T14:33:58-07:00","id":1538626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, how about you give us some idea about what Data is about?<br /> <br /> I don't know what people have so against Entropy. To me it is one of the best well written Spheres, if not the best overall. </div> </div> </div>On Entropy, it's not so much that I have anything against it, as it is that the concept of entropy as a thing in and of itself doesn't seem to fit the Technocratic mindset. The forces of decay make more sense as the ravages of time, and matters of probability strike me as more appropriate to the \u201cmath Field\u201d, a.k.a. Data. And breaking Entropy up between those two allows me to keep the total number of Fields at nine.<br /> <br /> Frankly, the only \u201coddity\u201d that creates is the notion that afterlife-related stuff becomes a conjunction between Time and Void instead of Entropy and Spirit.<br /> <br /> But really, this is stuff that ought to be discussed over on the Technocratic Fields thread I linked to in my earlier post; I don't want to derail this thread any further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  Added quote for context 07-15-2024, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T15:29:03-07:00","id":1538627,"title":"","content":"I think I have some idea about why people make funny faces when talking about Entropy, and it is the whole &quot;Death&quot; stuff. Which is the most asinine thing that unfortunately MtA brought through. <br /> In actuality, Entropy has NOTHING to do with &quot;Death&quot;, no more at least than Life has (and Life has much more to do with &quot;death&quot; than Entropy). But sadly, this silly concept have being ingrained in it for whatever reason, to the point that they created the &quot;Death Sphere&quot; in Awakening, which in my opinion is the most stupid idea ever.<br /> <br /> Entropy deals with chaotic systems. In physics, chaotic systems are not &quot;random&quot;; they are deterministic. What &quot;chaos&quot; means is our incapability to make accurate predictions in long spams of time.<br /> <br /> For example, if I throw a dice or flip a coin, the result is NOT random. It is a measure of the applied force, angular momentum, gravity, air resistance and so on.<br /> <br /> If we knew all of the variables involved, we could calculate the results EVERY SINGLE TIME.<br /> <br /> Likewise, things like the weather have the same characteristics. If we knew the movements of every single particle of air, of every single particle of water, of every single photon emitted by the Sun, then we could make weather predictions with exact precision forever.<br /> <br /> But that's NOT the case. We can't possibly know all of those.<br /> <br /> Therefore, for any type of system, there's an upper limit of time upon which predictions have trustworthy results. For the weather for example, that goes for a week; for the movement of galaxies, that goes up to 1 million years.<br /> <br /> After that, new data and new measurements must be acquired and calculated for new predictions to be reliable.<br /> <br /> This is what chaos means. It's our incapability to have all the relevant data about any system - and that's not a matter of equipment precision or better computers, but rather that it is IMPOSSIBLE to have all those variables (in fact, you would need to know the position and momentum of every single particle in the universe).<br /> <br /> THAT'S what Entropy controls. It control all of those tiny variables that affect any system.<br /> <br /> The beauty of it is that, since those are Deterministic systems, you can just as easily call it DESTINY or FATE.<br /> <br /> Thus, Entropy 1 allows you to see those hidden connections between apparently disconnected variables<br /> <br /> Entropy 2 is the alteration of variables on a small scale... What does it make to have a dice go 1 or 6? Small changes of angular momentum and applied force could make all the difference. Or the difference of a bullet hitting or missing its mark? One tiny millimeter of difference during the gun's recoil, or some tiny variations of air resistance could be all that it takes.<br /> <br /> For Entropy 3, let's make a thought experiment. Have you ever dropped a glass cup, but it didn't break? Sure, most of the times it's the announcement of a bad day, but on rare occasions, nothing happens.<br /> But why does that happen?<br /> &quot;Luck&quot; some would say.<br /> In terms of physics, it relates to the strength of the impact, angular movement, and perhaps you were just &quot;luck&quot; that the cup fell in a stronger point.<br /> Well, Entropy 3 deals with all of those variables in a matter pattern. Sure, when we see a Mage turning a castle to dust with it, we can't understand this and that's what gives us the impression that Entropy is just an &quot;amalgamation of weird random &quot;death and destruction&quot; powers&quot;. But that has nothing to do with it.<br /> Entropy 3 deals with the natural processes inside of matter patterns, with all the tiny hidden variables within it.<br /> <br /> For instance: how long does it take to make an iron gate to get rusty?<br /> And what is rust to begin with?<br /> <br /> Well, rust turns out to be nothing more than Iron Oxide. That is, atoms of Iron combining with atoms of Oxygen in the air.<br /> <br /> That process occurs in a &quot;random&quot; (meaning: chaotic, which is, deterministic but undeterminable, as in, we have no way to measure with precision). Water molecules in the air can also speed up that process.<br /> <br /> Thus, turning Iron to Rust is a NATURAL process that occurs over time.<br /> <br /> What Entropy 3 does is to speed up or slow down those variables; nothing more and nothing less.<br /> <br /> On a molecular level, if we could see the results, we would see the oxygen molecules in the air that are constantly moving and due to that, sometimes combine with the iron atoms forming rust due to &quot;random&quot; motions, we would see that sequence of interactions being accelerated, and the &quot;randomness&quot; of the process being strongly tilted towards forming more (or less) rust than should be expected.<br /> <br /> Of course, when a Mage throws a very vulgar effect that disintegrates a sword in an instant, we immediately just think about &quot;death magic&quot;, but that's NOT the case AT ALL.<br /> <br /> In such a vulgar display of Magik, the Mage is simply accelerating this process towards supernatural speeds, in a way that should NOT be possible.<br /> <br /> But hey, that's exactly why such use of Entropy would be highly VULGAR, because it goes above any possible means of a natural occurrence; nevertheless, the process is the SAME as the natural process, just with the randomness accelerated and direct into unnaturally impossible outcomes (hence why it is &quot;Magik&quot;, vulgar).<br /> <br /> Now, living beings are directed by the same &quot;random&quot; mechanisms are solid matter, with the difference being that living beings are massively complex biochemical systems with constant chemical interactions. But be sure, all those &quot;random&quot; processes occur inside our bodies and, in fact, our bodies have evolved to capitalize on them.<br /> <br /> For example, our hemoglobins don't just &quot;conjure&quot; oxygen. The molecules of oxygen that enter our lungs are transported RANDOMLY inside of our blood. But the molecules of hemoglobin have a high affinity towards oxygen, therefore, when a molecule of oxygen randomly approaches the hemoglobin, it has a HIGH PROBABILITY (but NOT CERTAINTY) to combine with it.<br /> <br /> Given the trillions of molecules of hemoglobin that we have travelling randomly inside of our blood (inside of the red cells of the blood), that means that the probability of combination between oxygen and hemoglobin is high enough, given the vast amounts that we have, that it is sufficient to transport the necessary oxygen that we need to survive throughout our body.<br /> <br /> Notice however that all of those biochemical interactions inside our body are RANDOM (aka chaotic systems).<br /> <br /> This means that, since Entropy is able to control randomness...<br /> <br /> And that's why Entropy 4 deals with that randomness inside living beings; because living beings are far more complex systems than inert matter. But are just as controlled by chaotic systems as a rock.<br /> <br /> And finally, Entropy 5 has been very poorly described in the books as &quot;control mind&quot;. In fact, it is to control results over far bigger variables. For example, let's think politics. We have all this &quot;left vs right&quot; nowadays.<br /> <br /> Well, it just happens that there's no &quot;left&quot; or &quot;right&quot; entities, just individuals that, individually, adhere to some or another.<br /> <br /> But even that is too little to describe it, because it individual is rather unique, so it is much more complex than just this dichotomical view of the world.<br /> <br /> But, how come then it determines the outcome of a society?<br /> <br /> How could, for example, the Nazis take hold in Germany?<br /> <br /> Well, there's no such a thing as the &quot;Nazi entity&quot;. Much like there's not a being called &quot;the government&quot;.<br /> <br /> Those are collections of people. But why then did Nazis succeed where others failed? There were fascist movements in the UK and the US at the time too, but they failed to take power. And there are many reasons for those, but one I could come up with is the &quot;lack of a critical mass&quot;. So, how many would be necessary for the fascists to control the US in the 1930's? 1 million? 10 millions?<br /> <br /> But what if there were only 9.999.999 fascists when you need 10 millions? Would that single person make all the difference between success and failure?<br /> <br /> And what determines having a single individual to adhere towards a right wing worldview, or a left wing worldview or a fascist worldview?<br /> <br /> Well, we could consider that to be a result of several previous experiences that person has throughout its entire life. That's a chaotic system that is even more complex than living systems themselves; even the food the person eats (determining the nutrients that individual has or that he lacks) could influence that.<br /> <br /> And that's just a single individual! Now, imagine how many variables are present when you're trying to social engineer an entire society!<br /> <br /> For example, if you spray accid in a rock, it will make a hole; if you inject someone with massive amounts of adrenaline, you give that person a heart attack.<br /> <br /> Convincing someone to change their ideas, is far harder. You have to go very, very deep into the psyche of that person in order to do that.<br /> <br /> And that's for a single individual.<br /> <br /> Now, imagine that, instead of doing something grandiose like using Entropy 5 to make the US turn communist, I just want to increase the sales of my business.<br /> <br /> Well, that's also a random event. For instance, if 10 out of 10.000 individuals were seeing my adds, now that number will jump to 100 out of 10.000.<br /> <br /> Why? Mere happenstance. Those extra 90 potential clients will be randomly changing the channel on TV or switching videos on YouTube, and by &quot;mere coincidence&quot; (or &quot;Magik conspiracy of Fate), will stumble upon my ad.<br /> <br /> Random conversations between people in the city will also randomly and coincidentally drift towards discussing my product. Discussions about my &quot;delicious&quot; cakes will spike 10 times; people that have long not seeing each other will cross, and after the initial animation about their reunion, they'll talk about the birthday of a third member of their group that just happened yesterday, and how that was just the most delicious cake of their lives, and that will spike the interest of the other person.<br /> <br /> So, there will be billions of casual &quot;coincidences&quot; that will happen, guiding the ending results. And all those, pointing towards a determined outcome.<br /> <br /> And for that, literally the universe will &quot;conspire&quot; in imperceptible ways for the desired outcome.<br /> <br /> That's how Entropy works. It has NOTHING to do with &quot;Death Magic&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T15:37:52-07:00","id":1538628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538626#post1538626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Entropy, it's not so much that I have anything against it, as it is that the concept of entropy as a thing in and of itself doesn't seem to fit the Technocratic mindset. The forces of decay make more sense as the ravages of time, and matters of probability strike me as more appropriate to the \u201cmath Field\u201d, a.k.a. Data. And breaking Entropy up between those two allows me to keep the total number of Fields at nine.<br /> <br /> Frankly, the only \u201coddity\u201d that creates is the notion that afterlife-related stuff becomes a conjunction between Time and Void instead of Entropy and Spirit.<br /> <br /> But really, this is stuff that ought to be discussed over on the Technocratic Fields thread I linked to in my earlier post; I don't want to derail this thread any further.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... Yeah, that's what I say. Entropy has no direct relation to &quot;decay&quot;. It is JUST probability, randomness and chance. &quot;Decay&quot; is just a part of chance, but Entropy doesn't deal with it any more than Life or Matter or any other Spheres. I hold a personal grudge towards this misconceived idea of &quot;Death Magik&quot; that has been imprinted into the Entropy Sphere.<br /> <br /> I would much rather have this Sphere be called &quot;Fate&quot; if that implied removing that preconceived (and erroneous) notion than to have that silly connection of Entropy to &quot;Necromancy&quot; for reasons","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T15:45:32-07:00","id":1538630,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> <br /> The relationship between death and Entropy is simply that Entropy is the sphere of end points. That is essentially what fate or destiny entails. Defining a specific end point.<br /> <br /> Even when dressed up as probability, it is regarding probability of a particular event coming to be, of a particular endpoint.<br /> <br /> and there is no fate more ultimate, no end point no more certain, than death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T15:47:21-07:00","id":1538631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538625#post1538625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:black\">Matter in M20</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:black\">Matter has a rather funky division that constantly trips me up. For Forces and Life, altering simple substances starts at rank 2, while transmutation requires rank 3. For Matter this is almost the reverse. Transmutation of simple matter starts at rank 2, but a mage can\u2019t alter many properties of matter until rank 3. I see some game balance logic to this, but that doesn\u2019t make it less tricky.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>That has always bothered me. Transmutation with Matter 2? Meanwhile, Shaping Matter or changing state is Matter 3?<br /> <br /> Let's be honest here, which is more complex, to turn lead into gold or to turn water into ice?<br /> <br /> That makes no sense. In my tables, I ALWAYS invert the two. Transmutation is Matter 3, Shaping or Changing State is 2. It's the only sensible approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T16:24:49-07:00","id":1538634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538630#post1538630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a><br /> The relationship between death and Entropy is simply that Entropy is the sphere of end points. That is essentially what fate or destiny entails. Defining a specific end point.<br /> <br /> Even when dressed up as probability, it is regarding probability of a particular event coming to be, of a particular endpoint.<br /> <br /> and there is no fate more ultimate, no end point no more certain, than death.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can be onboard of that. But not to adhere to &quot;death&quot; as some metaphysical building block of reality.<br /> <br /> Besides, the &quot;ending point&quot; of something is not the END. If I use Entropy 2 to determine the results of a dice, the simulation doesn't end after the results; the dice are still there and so is the gambler.<br /> <br /> Entropy does define the &quot;endpoint&quot; of a determined outcome in a CLOSED SYSTEM. But there's no closed systems in nature. Even death is not &quot;the end&quot;, not even to a skeptical atheist such as myself. Yes, it is the &quot;end&quot; of a very particular set of molecular arrangements that form my &quot;living body&quot;. <br /> <br /> But my &quot;living body&quot; is not the same as it was when I was a baby; I could say that the baby me DIED long ago. The Child me died when I became an adult.<br /> <br /> The only constant in the universe is change. So, after I die, my body will become food for the worms and fertilizer for the plants. It will change and no longer do what it currently does. <br /> <br /> <br /> And for some, there's a &quot;soul&quot; that will go into another journey. In Mage, there's even reincarnation.<br /> <br /> So, it's not exactly about &quot;end points&quot; but perhaps about &quot;end results&quot;. Entropy makes the universe conspire towards coalescing into a desired outcome, but afterwards, fate resumes its course. <br /> <br /> It's about pulling the threads of fate into a specific direction. That's what Entropy really is.<br /> <br /> It has nothing to do with &quot;Death and Decay&quot;, except in the indirect sense that &quot;Death and Decay&quot; are unavoidable destinations of Fate.<br /> <br /> Death is, after all, the fate of all that which lives, and decay is the unavoidable destiny of all that exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T16:35:33-07:00","id":1538635,"title":"","content":"The progression of Matter sphere is a question of how drastic the change is.<br /> <br /> transmutation of material is actually a very subtle change compared to anything else. You can only affect a single material, it\u2019s shape cannot be altered, but the material it is made of can be altered for a limited amount of time. And you cannot transform it in to anything that would change its state.<br /> <br /> changing an objects shape is a more drastic change, and fits in with the other effects that Matter 3 enables. That of fusing objects together or breaking them apart, both of which enable the changing of the end product\u2019s shape. In fact this breaking apart or fusing is essentially how one is able to cause an object to change its state, by dispersing the material into a gas or bringing a liquid together into a solid, though such a thing will only be temporary unless the melting/boiling point of the object is changed (which requires Matter 5 to do so)<br /> <br /> The Melt and Reform rote exemplifies the differences between said progression quite well. At matter 2 you can change a bar of metal in to clay. For the duration you may mould it or shape it using your mundane skills, before it returns to metal in whatever shape you shaped it.<br /> <br /> whereas with Matter 3, you can directly shape the metal bar without transforming it first.<br /> <br /> this fits the progression quite nicely to matter 4, where you can force the metal bar to essentially transform into whatever object you desire, such as the ever popular gun.<br /> <br /> <br /> i suspect the reason it feels strange is we consider an objects material to be less immutable than its shape, but in honesty, besides being harder, softer, or holding slightly different properties like whether or not it conducts heat or electricity better, changing the material of an object doesn\u2019t really do very much compared to changing its shape. Once you have access to changing an object\u2019s shape, you have a great deal of utility open to you, which to me befits a 3rd rank effect far better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T16:49:11-07:00","id":1538638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538634#post1538634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can be onboard of that. But not to adhere to &quot;death&quot; as some metaphysical building block of reality.<br /> <br /> Besides, the &quot;ending point&quot; of something is not the END. If I use Entropy 2 to determine the results of a dice, the simulation doesn't end after the results; the dice are still there and so is the gambler.<br /> <br /> Entropy does define the &quot;endpoint&quot; of a determined outcome in a CLOSED SYSTEM. But there's no closed systems in nature. Even death is not &quot;the end&quot;, not even to a skeptical atheist such as myself. Yes, it is the &quot;end&quot; of a very particular set of molecular arrangements that form my &quot;living body&quot;.<br /> <br /> But my &quot;living body&quot; is not the same as it was when I was a baby; I could say that the baby me DIED long ago. The Child me died when I became an adult.<br /> <br /> The only constant in the universe is change. So, after I die, my body will become food for the worms and fertilizer for the plants. It will change and no longer do what it currently does.<br /> <br /> <br /> And for some, there's a &quot;soul&quot; that will go into another journey. In Mage, there's even reincarnation.<br /> <br /> So, it's not exactly about &quot;end points&quot; but perhaps about &quot;end results&quot;. Entropy makes the universe conspire towards coalescing into a desired outcome, but afterwards, fate resumes its course.<br /> <br /> It's about pulling the threads of fate into a specific direction. That's what Entropy really is.<br /> <br /> It has nothing to do with &quot;Death and Decay&quot;, except in the indirect sense that &quot;Death and Decay&quot; are unavoidable destinations of Fate.<br /> <br /> Death is, after all, the fate of all that which lives, and decay is the unavoidable destiny of all that exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t believe we are in disagreement here. More a question of what we mean by terms<br /> <br /> What I refer to as \u2018end points\u2019 is essentially a defined outcome to an event or series of events. Be it a dice roll, a day out, a party, a bloodline, or even a life.<br /> <br /> you can have multiple end points for the stages of one\u2019s life, and ai would say Entropy can indeed have a hand in determining the shape of each of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T23:47:25-07:00","id":1538646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538625#post1538625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c55a11\">522 \u2013 Instill a soul within an empty shell of Matter. The capitalization implies Matter is necessary but doesn\u2019t actually say it. I\u2019d say that yes it is required. Creating a soul may be a clear power of Spirit, but installing it is not, and probably involves at least some manipulation of the pattern it is installed into.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Isnt that just creating a fetish and forcing a spirit inside? thats pure spirit 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T06:37:13-07:00","id":1538651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538646#post1538646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isnt that just creating a fetish and forcing a spirit inside? thats pure spirit 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say we are dealing with different effects. This binds the two in the way human has a soul rather than the way that a fetish has a bound spirit. The way I would put it is that the mage is giving the body a soul and the soul a body in such a way that they are a single entity.<br /> <br /> Whether or not you'd agree with that description, the Life version of this is the effect required to turn a magically created empty human shell into a full person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T07:13:06-07:00","id":1538654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538635#post1538635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The progression of Matter sphere is a question of how drastic the change is.<br /> <br /> transmutation of material is actually a very subtle change compared to anything else. You can only affect a single material, it\u2019s shape cannot be altered, but the material it is made of can be altered for a limited amount of time. And you cannot transform it in to anything that would change its state.<br /> <br /> changing an objects shape is a more drastic change, and fits in with the other effects that Matter 3 enables. That of fusing objects together or breaking them apart, both of which enable the changing of the end product\u2019s shape. In fact this breaking apart or fusing is essentially how one is able to cause an object to change its state, by dispersing the material into a gas or bringing a liquid together into a solid, though such a thing will only be temporary unless the melting/boiling point of the object is changed (which requires Matter 5 to do so)<br /> <br /> The Melt and Reform rote exemplifies the differences between said progression quite well. At matter 2 you can change a bar of metal in to clay. For the duration you may mould it or shape it using your mundane skills, before it returns to metal in whatever shape you shaped it.<br /> <br /> whereas with Matter 3, you can directly shape the metal bar without transforming it first.<br /> <br /> this fits the progression quite nicely to matter 4, where you can force the metal bar to essentially transform into whatever object you desire, such as the ever popular gun.<br /> <br /> <br /> i suspect the reason it feels strange is we consider an objects material to be less immutable than its shape, but in honesty, besides being harder, softer, or holding slightly different properties like whether or not it conducts heat or electricity better, changing the material of an object doesn\u2019t really do very much compared to changing its shape. Once you have access to changing an object\u2019s shape, you have a great deal of utility open to you, which to me befits a 3rd rank effect far better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... That's... Something I haven't considered before.<br /> <br /> So, in a sense, or at least from a metaphysical way rather than &quot;da sCience&quot; (aka the fake forgery of the techie boys), turning lead into gold is a lesser alteration compared to changing the shape of the material?<br /> <br /> Yeah... I guess that, in the setting of Mage (which basically adhere to the ideas of Immaterialism from Kant), it does make sense.<br /> <br /> Yet... I can't do it lol. See what I mean by bias? Despite my rational side being fully capable of understanding the argument, my emotions continue to bang on my head... This just feels... Wrong.<br /> <br /> I guess my Technocratic conditioning is just too strong. I... Yeah. I agree with you. And despite that.. I just can't accept it nevertheless... Curses! I hate to feel that way, to have this conflicting cognitive dissonance.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I must concede... You're right. From a metaphysical point of view (which is the one that truly matters in MtA), that reasoning cannot be argued with. So, I just have to throw away my entire real life worldview of a materialistic mechanicist universe and go with it... Easy \ud83d\ude21\ud83d\ude21\ud83d\ude21<br /> <br /> Ok ok. Emotions be damned. You convinced me. I'll change it back to Matter 2 being transmutation, even if it gives me pain on my stomach.<br /> <br /> But you see, this is exactly why I think that each level and each effect on the books should have very thorough explanations. It would cost nothing to for example have a little explanation about how &quot;the properties of matter are much more metaphysical rather than being tied to physical/chemical scientific properties&quot;. This is necessary for players - and given the many nonsensical effects from official books, even to the writers themselves","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T07:26:17-07:00","id":1538655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538651#post1538651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say we are dealing with different effects. This binds the two in the way human has a soul rather than the way that a fetish has a bound spirit. The way I would put it is that the mage is giving the body a soul and the soul a body in such a way that they are a single entity.<br /> <br /> Whether or not you'd agree with that description, the Life version of this is the effect required to turn a magically created empty human shell into a full person.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I agree, in terms... But that creates some problems of its own.<br /> <br /> With Spirit 4 what you're basically doing is &quot;enveloping&quot; a Spirit inside an object with a &quot;piece of the Gauntlet&quot;. That's what Spirit 4 does, it is Gauntlet manipulation, and in order to create a Fetish, that's essentially what you're doing, you're &quot;enveloping&quot; the Gauntlet around an object with a spirit inside in a way that the Gauntlet is weak enough to let some of the &quot;essence&quot; (or power) of that Spirit to &quot;leak&quot; into the Material World.<br /> <br /> Regardless of how you view it, it is a sort of Gauntlet manipulation at the end of the day, and nothing more.<br /> <br /> The spirit inside will slumber by the way, due to the procedure endured.<br /> <br /> Now, with Life 5 Spirit 5, you're creating a true &quot;soul&quot;. You're not just making that spirit inhabit (or possess) a body; in fact, I think that the best way to describe it would be that you're FUSING the body and spirit into a single pattern.<br /> <br /> So, following the same logic, I think you could do that with a rock... But doesn't the rock already have a sleeping spirit?<br /> <br /> What happens if I awaken the spirit of the rock with Spirit 3, and then try to fuse another spirit into it with Matter 5 Spirit 5? Would that rock have &quot;2 souls&quot;?<br /> <br /> And while we are at it, could we use Life 5 Spirit 5 to give &quot;2 souls&quot; to somebody? \ud83d\ude2e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T08:23:45-07:00","id":1538660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538655#post1538655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, with Life 5 Spirit 5, you're creating a true &quot;soul&quot;. You're not just making that spirit inhabit (or possess) a body; in fact,<b> I think that the best way to describe it would be that you're FUSING the body and spirit into a single pattern</b>.<br /> <br /> So, following the same logic, I think you could do that with a rock... But doesn't the rock already have a sleeping spirit?<br /> <br /> What happens if I awaken the spirit of the rock with Spirit 3, and then try to fuse another spirit into it with Matter 5 Spirit 5? Would that rock have &quot;2 souls&quot;?<br /> <br /> And while we are at it, could we use Life 5 Spirit 5 to give &quot;2 souls&quot; to somebody? \ud83d\ude2e</div> </div> </div> </div>That does remind me of Heylel Teomim's infamous magickal feat of fusing two souls (and bodies), albeit imperfectly.<br /> <br /> In Ascencion there's also a spell to create Anakims by fusing the Avatar with a Psychopomp, if I remember correctly. I don't remember if it needed Life (other than on the corrupted Heylel's version to fuse two bodies)<br /> <br /> ON these examples it's not so much as a being with two souls, but a being with an amalgam or fusion of souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T09:05:21-07:00","id":1538661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538655#post1538655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Now, with Life 5 Spirit 5, you're creating a true &quot;soul&quot;. You're not just making that spirit inhabit (or possess) a body; in fact, I think that the best way to describe it would be that you're FUSING the body and spirit into a single pattern.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good way of putting it, yes.<br /> <br /> So, following the same logic, I think you could do that with a rock... But doesn't the rock already have a sleeping spirit?<br /> <br /> What happens if I awaken the spirit of the rock with Spirit 3, and then try to fuse another spirit into it with Matter 5 Spirit 5? Would that rock have &quot;2 souls&quot;?<br /> <br /> And while we are at it, could we use Life 5 Spirit 5 to give &quot;2 souls&quot; to somebody? \ud83d\ude2e[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> I wouldn't say the spirit of a rock, awakened or otherwise, is the same thing as a soul. It's certainly not at all the same thing as the classical idea of a soul. If the situation did arise I would probably handle it a lot like a case of possession.<br /> <br /> As for two souls, I don't think there's anything that would prevent it and the canonical history of MtA has at least one figure, Heylel Teonim, who either had two souls or one soul fused from two. It's not an unheard of concept in fiction either. I do think its one of those issues that is a minefield, though, as it touches on issues like identity and player/character agency, so I'd double check with the players at the table before introducing the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T11:18:16-07:00","id":1538664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538661#post1538661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a good way of putting it, yes.<br /> <br /> So, following the same logic, I think you could do that with a rock... But doesn't the rock already have a sleeping spirit?<br /> <br /> What happens if I awaken the spirit of the rock with Spirit 3, and then try to fuse another spirit into it with Matter 5 Spirit 5? Would that rock have &quot;2 souls&quot;?<br /> <br /> And while we are at it, could we use Life 5 Spirit 5 to give &quot;2 souls&quot; to somebody? \ud83d\ude2e</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wouldn't say the spirit of a rock, awakened or otherwise, is the same thing as a soul. It's certainly not at all the same thing as the classical idea of a soul. If the situation did arise I would probably handle it a lot like a case of possession.<br /> <br /> As for two souls, I don't think there's anything that would prevent it and the canonical history of MtA has at least one figure, Heylel Teonim, who either had two souls or one soul fused from two. It's not an unheard of concept in fiction either. I do think its one of those issues that is a minefield, though, as it touches on issues like identity and player/character agency, so I'd double check with the players at the table before introducing the idea. </div> </div> </div>It just crossed me, this would probably be like the process of &quot;Fomori-zation&quot; from WtA - aka becoming a Fomori.<br /> <br /> The setting from WtA explains that a human &quot;infected&quot; by the spirit (sorry, I don't know the name of this category of spirits in English, in Portuguese they called them &quot;malditos&quot; which roughly translates as &quot;cursed&quot;, by I remember that this is not the name for the spirits of the Wyrm in English, I just can't remember the proper word) has his soul fused with that of the evil spirit, and that's why it is impossible to be cured.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 07-16-2024, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T14:49:35-07:00","id":1538679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538661#post1538661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I wouldn't say the spirit of a rock, awakened or otherwise, is the same thing as a soul. It's certainly not at all the same thing as the classical idea of a soul. If the situation did arise I would probably handle it a lot like a case of possession.<br /> <br /> As for two souls, I don't think there's anything that would prevent it and the canonical history of MtA has at least one figure, Heylel Teonim, who either had two souls or one soul fused from two. It's not an unheard of concept in fiction either. I do think its one of those issues that is a minefield, though, as it touches on issues like identity and player/character agency, so I'd double check with the players at the table before introducing the idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>From WTO a soul is a wraith, and a wraith can be bound by a fetish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T18:45:27-07:00","id":1538687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538679#post1538679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From WTO a soul is a wraith, and a wraith can be bound by a fetish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... That's a rather complicate matter...<br /> <br /> In fact, there's no real evidence that Wraiths are &quot;souls&quot;.<br /> <br /> They might just be &quot;impressions of the living&quot;...<br /> <br /> Let's try some imagination:<br /> <br /> Now, we know that some items destroyed in the Material World can end up &quot;appearing&quot; in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> But... Is that really true?<br /> <br /> Stuff in the Underworld are not really made of carbon and silicon... They are made of Corpus.<br /> <br /> And what is &quot;Corpus&quot;? It is some weird &quot;spiritual&quot; stuff.<br /> <br /> We also know that stuff in this plane of existence are highly affected by emotions... Memories, emotions, all of that shape the environment and even it's inhabitants.<br /> <br /> The Corpus of the Wraiths itself is highly dependant on their emotions - a Wraith that has no more passions simply ceases to be, their very &quot;Corpus&quot; dissipates into nothingness.<br /> <br /> Therefore, this is a Realm of pure emotion... It is an abstract Realm of thought.<br /> <br /> In that sense... It might not even be real! It could just be a &quot;theater of the mind&quot; for all we know. A sort of &quot;collective acid trip&quot;.<br /> <br /> But that's not the point. The point is that Wraiths may not be &quot;souls&quot;, but just simply a &quot;mental reflection&quot; of the deceased!<br /> <br /> This is a Realm that could copy the minds of those that died with far too strong will - so, if your will is too strong, it will &quot;imprint&quot; your mind into this Realm.<br /> <br /> But it is NOT &quot;you&quot;, but a mental copy of what you once were.<br /> <br /> There's actually some indication that this might be true. First of all, everything points out to there being a difference between &quot;soul&quot; and &quot;mind&quot;. Proof of that is that you actually need Spirit 5 in order to create a real human being, rather than just Mind 5.<br /> <br /> Secondly, there's indication that &quot;souls&quot; mostly don't carry over details of the &quot;mind&quot;, except for few fragments, with a few exceptions. How do we know this? Because Mage actually has reincarnation, and almost all of the time save very rare exceptions, you NEVER get details from &quot;past minds&quot; except for some disconnected flashes. <br /> <br /> Therefore, Mind (memory and emotions) is NOT the same as &quot;Soul&quot; (whatever that might be).<br /> <br /> The thing is thou, that Wraiths keep their full Minds upon their &quot;transition&quot;. They remain essentially the SAME as they &quot;were&quot; when alive, the same memories, the same psychology, the same emotions (sure, colourful due to their environment).<br /> <br /> Reincarnated Mages on the other hand, are different persons from their previous lives (different memories, different experiences, different minds)<br /> <br /> That is a strong indication that Wraiths are the &quot;Mind&quot; of the dead, rather than their &quot;Soul&quot;.<br /> <br /> The other problem we have relate to &quot;Avatars&quot;.<br /> <br /> What is an Avatar you might ask?<br /> <br /> I have no freaking idea, but but there's a strong implication that &quot;Avatars&quot; have something to do with &quot;Souls&quot;, whatever a &quot;Soul&quot; is either.<br /> <br /> And while I might not know what a Wraith is... I'm sure as hell that they aren't Avatars.<br /> <br /> Therefore, I believe that there's a strong possibility that Wraiths aren't really souls, but rather just &quot;psychic reflections&quot; of the living upon the dreadful Underworld... As in, this is a Realm that &quot;copy&quot; the minds of strong willed individuals.<br /> <br /> That would make Wraiths be something akin to the Chimeras from the Dreaming. The Spirits of the Dreaming, the Chimeras, they are &quot;born&quot; out of the dreams and imagination of the dreamers (or sleepers or just simply &quot;humans&quot;). Wraiths could then, be something similar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T19:28:27-07:00","id":1538691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538679#post1538679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From WTO a soul is a wraith, and a wraith can be bound by a fetish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regardless, even if Wraiths really are &quot;souls&quot;, that says nothing about the effect. Yes, you can bound Wraiths to fetishes with the basic Spirit 4. That doesn't mean that Spirit 4 can be used to fuse a Wraith with a body.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which: Life 5, Spirit 5, Mind 5 - instead of creating a new soul and a new mind for a new body, you create a new body to &quot;resurrect&quot; a Wraith.<br /> <br /> Why is this different from creating a fetish from a body and a Wraith with Spirit 4?<br /> <br /> Because even if you create a new body for this purpose, the Wraith inside it would simply be &quot;possessing&quot; it, inhabit it, but it wouldn't be part of it. It would be like a puppeteer pulling the strings behind the curtain.<br /> <br /> With the Spirit 5 and Life 5 version however, you're actually fusing the two Patterns into a single one. You would be turning the Wraith and the body into a singular and indissoluble entity.<br /> <br /> You know, like most living beings.<br /> <br /> Now, the only question would be if Wraiths really count as &quot;souls&quot;, or if as I said about they are just &quot;spiritual impressions of the Mind&quot;.<br /> <br /> If they really are souls, given that they already have minds of their own, you would &quot;only&quot; need Life 5 and Spirit 5 to resurrect a Wraith.<br /> <br /> If however they are just simple minds floating in the &quot;Dark Ether&quot; of the Underworld, then you would also need to add Mind 5, because you would be fusing the Mind (which is the Wraith) into the body, but you would also need to create a real proper &quot;soul&quot; for it.<br /> <br /> But there's also a third option, upon which yes, Wraiths are &quot;mental constructs&quot; and not real &quot;souls&quot;, but they are mental constructs made of &quot;Spiritual Matter&quot;, which means that their &quot;Ephemera&quot; (Corpus) is akin to the Ephemera of any other kind of Spirit, and therefore serves as a &quot;soul&quot; just as same. This would be a special case of &quot;mind making spirit manifest&quot;, as in, despite being &quot;born from the mind&quot;, they are beings of spirit.<br /> Or, if I can explain it better, the Underworld uses &quot;spiritual matter/energy&quot; to create &quot;spirits&quot; using the minds of the deceased.<br /> <br /> In this case, once again you could do it (resurrect Wraiths) with Life 5 Spirit 5 alone (the Wraith will bring the Mind with himself as a bonus).<br /> <br /> Now... Could this &quot;resurrect Wraith&quot; be something akin to a mummy?<br /> <br /> Because this process is not the same as creating a &quot;normal&quot; human &quot;soul&quot;. I think, for example, that using a spirit of the Wyrm as the base for the &quot;soul&quot; of somebody would just create a Fomori.<br /> <br /> Therefore, a &quot;resurrected Wraith&quot; would probably be a kind of Mummy - or even better, perhaps a Projector from Morpheus or a Sin Eater Geist from the CoD, a living that is &quot;touched by the Underworld&quot;, maybe even able to use some Arcanoi (like a Risen, but truly alive)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T00:07:00-07:00","id":1538709,"title":"","content":"Now, &quot;soul&quot; does give a sense of &quot;consciousness&quot;.<br /> <br /> Because the MiB clones that are created without &quot;souls&quot; behave as beings that aren't self conscious.<br /> <br /> Could this be it? Most &quot;lesser&quot; spirits don't appear to be self conscious either. They don't have &quot;free will&quot;, they just blindly follow their natures, even if they appear to be intelligent.<br /> <br /> So yeah, a rock spirit awakened may indeed not count towards being &quot;a soul&quot;. It's just a &quot;drone spirit&quot; that blindly does whatever the hell is that rocks do.<br /> <br /> Now, since it has been brought up, we now what Life 5, Spirit 5 Mind 5 does, and what it does is create a cloned person with intellect and personality and self conscious. Because it has a &quot;soul&quot;.<br /> <br /> But... What if we do it to a rock? Or maybe not a rock, but rather a statue? Would then that piece of inanimate object become a &quot;real person&quot;, in the sense that it can not only think (because even our computers can &quot;think&quot;, which is just the capacity to process information), but also be self conscious?<br /> <br /> A self conscious piece of marble that has its own dreams and aspirations and don't want to become a sculpture like its father but rather loves advocacy and wants to become a lawyer to the horror of its painted father and picture mother? Could this be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T00:28:34-07:00","id":1538713,"title":"","content":"Acording to WTO and DTF wraiths are souls. So for me thats evidence enough,<br /> Wraiths alone may be delusional. But the shadowlands were created to keep souls safe by the Slayers. Its even mentioned in DTF of souls being used in a artefact making process like soluforging (the same thing basically).<br /> <br /> As for what a soul is. For me its a special maliable kind of spirit with power. I personally think the shadow and the avatar are the same thing one is just insane cause no body keeping in check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 07-17-2024, 03:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T05:58:39-07:00","id":1538732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538713#post1538713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Acording to WTO and DTF wraiths are souls. So for me thats evidence enough,<br /> Wraiths alone may be delusional. But the shadowlands were created to keep souls safe by the Slayers. Its even mentioned in DTF of souls being used in a artefact making process like soluforging (the same thing basically).<br /> <br /> As for what a soul is. For me its a special maliable kind of spirit with power. I personally think the shadow and the avatar are the same thing one is just insane cause no body keeping in check.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you wish to add on to this, a soul is pretty well defined in Mummy the Resurrection. There it confirms that wraiths are actually parts of a soul in the process of decay. The Shadow, Psyche, Eidolon, Corpus, and the aura which formed the cauls start to disentangle themselves upon death. The process of achieving transcendence is in many ways an attempt to put these bits of soul back together.<br /> <br /> So I think it makes sense to consider a wraith a fractured soul. It should also be noted that wraiths already have very strong ties to objects, these are their fetters, and it is quite possible to forge a new fetter like connection between yourself and a wraith.<br /> <br /> it is difficult to keep a wraith captive indefinetly however their loss of corpus, fetters, or passions, causes them to fall through the cracks in the underworld and enter the labyrinth. You could possibly resummon them however.<br /> though long term keeping of a wraith can be rather dangerous as in time without proper care, said wraith will succumb to their shadow and become a spectre. When that happens, the hivemind becomes aware of what you are doing, which becomes another thing you\u2019ll need to deal with, assuming your mage is even aware of this","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T07:11:49-07:00","id":1538740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538713#post1538713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Acording to WTO and DTF wraiths are souls. So for me thats evidence enough,</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if they are souls (and my opinion on that is complicated but sums up to &quot;sort of&quot;), the relationship between spirit/soul and fetish is a different one than the relationship between soul and body in a living being. I am not familiar with what happens when wraiths are made into fetishes but I'm fairly certain it doesn't look a thing like resurrection. <br /> <br /> Also, consider the Risen. That's a wraith in a body but the relationship between soul and body is clearly not that of a human. Clearly when wraiths enter objects or bodies they don't naturally become one with that body. Not in the sense that a human soul is bonded with a human body.<br /> <br /> All of which is enough for me to say that incorporating a soul into a body to make a human or human equivalent is a metaphysically different effect than binding a spirit into an object. Just being in an object is not the same thing as being the object.<br /> <br /> Instead, incorporating that body and soul together into one pattern is much more complicated. It is a grafting effect and grafting effects typically require the relevant spheres of everything being grafted together.<br /> <br /> Now I will add one important thing I missed. Grafting usually requires the spheres at Transmutation levels. That's Matter 2 or 4 and Life 3 or 5, depending on complexity. So while I think Spirit 5 is appropriate, Life and Matter are quite possibly overstated. I suppose someone could argue that [Pattern Sphere] rank 5 is necessary to give the body the exotic quality: &quot;capable of having a soul&quot; though I am inclined against that because that is classically a quality of living bodies.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T07:21:26-07:00","id":1538742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538732#post1538732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you wish to add on to this, a soul is pretty well defined in Mummy the Resurrection. There it confirms that wraiths are actually parts of a soul in the process of decay. The Shadow, Psyche, Eidolon, Corpus, and the aura which formed the cauls start to disentangle themselves upon death. The process of achieving transcendence is in many ways an attempt to put these bits of soul back together.<br /> <br /> So I think it makes sense to consider a wraith a fractured soul. It should also be noted that wraiths already have very strong ties to objects, these are their fetters, and it is quite possible to forge a new fetter like connection between yourself and a wraith.<br /> <br /> it is difficult to keep a wraith captive indefinetly however their loss of corpus, fetters, or passions, causes them to fall through the cracks in the underworld and enter the labyrinth. You could possibly resummon them however.<br /> though long term keeping of a wraith can be rather dangerous as in time without proper care, said wraith will succumb to their shadow and become a spectre. When that happens, the hivemind becomes aware of what you are doing, which becomes another thing you\u2019ll need to deal with, assuming your mage is even aware of this</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's what I was hoping for (although I won't lie, the idea of having Wraiths as forged &quot;doppelgangers&quot; excited me, it would be a nice touch of additional insult thrown into their hellish world to be mere Spirits only created to suffer). But yes, I agree, particularly with the part of being &quot;fractured&quot;, specifically because the Avatar don't follow them. <br /> <br /> Ancient Egyptian mythology believed that the &quot;soul&quot; was divided in 7 parts, and that's what Mummy went for (and I like it). <br /> <br /> Still, it is possible to &quot;resurrect&quot; a Wraith with Spirit 5 and Life 5 nevertheless. And what is a Mummy by the way if not exactly that? A resurrected Wraith?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T07:32:15-07:00","id":1538745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538740#post1538740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even if they are souls (and my opinion on that is complicated but sums up to &quot;sort of&quot;), the relationship between spirit/soul and fetish is a different one than the relationship between soul and body in a living being. I am not familiar with what happens when wraiths are made into fetishes but I'm fairly certain it doesn't look a thing like resurrection.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it's not. Basically, a Fetish Wraith gives access to the Arcanoi of the Wraith to the user and that's about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, consider the Risen. That's a wraith in a body but the relationship between soul and body is clearly not that of a human. Clearly when wraiths enter objects or bodies they don't naturally become one with that body. Not in the sense that a human soul is bonded with a human body. </div> </div> </div>Exactly. The Risen is &quot;possession of a body&quot;. The Wraith animates the body like a puppeteer.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All of which is enough for me to say that incorporating a soul into a body to make a human or human equivalent is a metaphysically different effect than binding a spirit into an object. Just being in an object is not the same thing as being the object.<br /> <br /> Instead, incorporating that body and soul together into one pattern is much more complicated. It is a grafting effect and grafting effects typically require the relevant spheres of everything being grafted together.<br /> <br /> Now I will add one important thing I missed. Grafting usually requires the spheres at Transmutation levels. That's Matter 2 or 4 and Life 3 or 5, depending on complexity. So while I think Spirit 5 is appropriate, Life and Matter are quite possibly overstated. I suppose someone could argue that [Pattern Sphere] rank 5 is necessary to give the body the exotic quality: &quot;capable of having a soul&quot; though I am inclined against that because that is classically a quality of living bodies. </div> </div> </div>Hmmm.... Yeah. I think you're right.<br /> <br /> But I still have one question: what would it mean to have a Three with a &quot;soul&quot;? Would that mean a self conscious three? Would that three become animated, able to walk around like an Ent, or would it become a conscious mind forever trapped in its place, and unable to communicate with others for having no mouth and no lungs?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T08:08:38-07:00","id":1538750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538745#post1538745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But I still have one question: what would it mean to have a Three with a &quot;soul&quot;? Would that mean a self conscious three? Would that three become animated, able to walk around like an Ent, or would it become a conscious mind forever trapped in its place, and unable to communicate with others for having no mouth and no lungs?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't think of that. We generally would assume that the resulting entity is capable of movement and communication. <br /> <br /> Now that is a good justification for Matter 5 and Life 5 for most objects and many life forms. Installing a soul in a rock might be Spirit 5/Matter 2, but making it capable of independent movement and communication and thought without changing its &quot;rockness&quot; is Spirit 5/Matter 5. I think robots and puppets could get away with Matter 4, but almost every other form of matter and many, many forms of life will need rank 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T08:29:26-07:00","id":1538752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538745#post1538745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But I still have one question: what would it mean to have a Three with a &quot;soul&quot;? Would that mean a self conscious three? Would that three become animated, able to walk around like an Ent, or would it become a conscious mind forever trapped in its place, and unable to communicate with others for having no mouth and no lungs?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest strictly possesing a soul does nothing. Its there thats it.<br /> When we awaken the spirit of a tree or bind a spirit to the tree its asumed the spirit controlls the item/plant with its powers. A tree has no brain nor mind so it would not be able to act just possesing a soul.<br /> If the soul is a wriath then if he has apropriate arcanoi then he could move it. I would asume that in fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T15:29:49-07:00","id":1538797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538752#post1538752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest strictly possesing a soul does nothing. Its there thats it.<br /> When we awaken the spirit of a tree or bind a spirit to the tree its asumed the spirit controlls the item/plant with its powers. A tree has no brain nor mind so it would not be able to act just possesing a soul.<br /> If the soul is a wriath then if he has apropriate arcanoi then he could move it. I would asume that in fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, if that &quot;Soul&quot; doesn't have a &quot;Mind&quot; (aka if doesn't already have an intellect of its own), then you would need Mind 5 in addition to prove it for this thing. However, if by &quot;Soul&quot; we refer to consciousness, as it seems to be the implications throughout most of the games, then that weird science project will eventually develop one over time. What kind of a &quot;Mind&quot; a three or a marble statue that are unable to hear, see, feel or communicate in any way, would develop, I do not know. Probably just sheer madness from a soul feeling trapped within itself in the most gruesome kind of torture I could think of.<br /> <br /> Now, &quot;souls&quot; by themselves don't really have &quot;powers&quot;. Human souls have Avatars; Avatars have powers, but only if they are Awaken.<br /> <br /> Non Avatar Spirits turned into souls? I don't know. <br /> <br /> And again, this is not the same as &quot;binding&quot; a spirit to a body or an object. This is fusing matter and soul together. Binding a spirit to an object creates a Fetish, a &quot;conduit&quot; for the spirit's powers into the material world. Binding a spirit to a body is possession, it's a foreign agent taking control of that body.<br /> <br /> Integrating body and spirit is not the same. Likewise, awakening a spirit of an object works on the same level as that.<br /> <br /> Turning that Spirit into a &quot;soul&quot; gives it free will, self consciousness, dreams and aspirations. Besides, since most Avatars get into the world asleep, it could very well mean that the old spirit also slumbers as it gives way to its new existence in a material body and with a free willed mind.<br /> <br /> For example, let's suppose we decide to turn a spirit of the Wyrm into a &quot;soul&quot; inside of a human body. Now, this won't create a Fomori. Instead, the evil spirit, merged with flesh, &quot;goes to sleep&quot;. It will have a new mind - or perhaps it even retains memories from the Umbra, probably in the form of disconnected thoughts.<br /> <br /> This new &quot;person&quot; - because it now is indeed a person - will probably be sadistic, machiavellic and evil. Most likely a sociopath. And with good chances of turning Nefandi.<br /> <br /> But this new person would have free will and would be self conscious, something that it was not while it was a spirit of Wyrm. He may even decide to go against its original nature, something that would be impossible when it was a simple spirit. He could start going to the church, get married and be a lovely husband and father and completely change his original nature. Something that no spirit is capable of.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Wyrm powers that his &quot;soul&quot; possess as vestiges from its spirit past would remain dormant inside, since the &quot;soul&quot; is asleep. That person would have the potential to &quot;re-learn&quot; or awaken those powers again perhaps, but it doesn't necessarily mean that he would automatically have them from the get go.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T07:39:25-07:00","id":1538836,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Time from M20</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Time is notable both in how much like Correspondence it is and how much not like Correspondence it is and it really shows how the Spheres are set up around intuition rather than consistency. Correspondence finds it remarkably easy to move things, but remarkably hard to alter space itself. Reaching across distance starts at Rank 2, but warping space is locked behind Rank 5. Time is close to the reverse as warping the flow of time starts at Rank 3 while moving through it is mostly behind Rank 5.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There\u2019s no real reason that warping space should be harder than warping time, but it is much harder to envision what warping space looks like, so it is higher. Likewise, there\u2019s no reason time travel should be harder than teleportation, but time travel is more likely to derail plots, so it is higher.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">68 \u2013 At rank 1, Time initiates can sense the ebb and flow of time</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">68 \u2013 At rank 2, Time students gain limited pre- and post cognition. It is unclear what the limit is.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">68 \u2013 At rank 3, the devotee can speed up or slow down time.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">68 \u2013 At rank 4, the adept can stop time.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">68 \u2013 At rank 5, the master can step outside of time, travel in time, and gain limited immortality.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">69 \u2013 Time combined with Matter takes objects out of the time stream. Depends on the effect.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">372 \u2013 Entropy 2/Forces 2/Time 2 as a description of the effect in the movie Ink. The effect is to manipulate events to cause a car crash. I have not seen the movie, but Entropy and Forces are there for the purpose of moving objects without touching them. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">I\u2019m going to interpret this as moving some things directly and manipulating the probability of others, so that works. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\"> Time, though, is unnecessary.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">389 \u2013 Time 3 is one of the ways of getting multiple actions without penalties. This gets repeated a lot in this area of the book.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">417 \u2013 Time 2 and an active sensory effect in Corr, Mind, or Time lets a mage ignore the multiple opponents penalty.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">422 \u2013 Time 2 increases the damage of a punch by noting the perfect opening. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c55a11\">This really isn\u2019t a listed power of Time, and ideal moments are more the province of Entropy. However, Correspondence 1 can sense more than just distance and direction so it makes sense that Time 1 can sense more than just the time of day. A sense of opportune moments or junctures or just where things will be would be appropriate.</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\"> It would not be Time 2 though. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">424 \u2013 Time Sphere perceptions can allegedly counter the effects of an opponent using Drunken Style. I object to this because Time 1 doesn\u2019t do that.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">429 \u2013 Bullet Catching is listed as Time 3/Forces 2/Life 2. Time is stated as increasing the characters reflexes, which is a terrible way of saying slow down time. While it is reasonable to say Time doesn\u2019t actually change the energy of a bullet, Life or Forces should be enough of an addition.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">438 \u2013 Time is a sphere that can be used for the Dodging the Blast Optional Rule. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">485 \u2013 Time and Forces have a +1 difficulty in Otherworlds. Time is unreliable in the Low Umbra.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">504 \u2013 Time and Correspondence inflict no damage unless combined with other spheres. It only now occurred to me how strange the wording is. As written, this means you can make direct attack spells with them, but they don\u2019t cause any kind of damage without another appropriate sphere. It\u2019s not a bad way of understanding what is going on, I have to admit, but it is a little strange.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">508 \u2013 Time 3 to increase or reduce speed. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c55a11\">509 \u2013 Entropy 3/Time 3 to disintegrate an object. As I\u2019ve said before, I think Entropy or Time can do this alone, but I also think the two in combination should actually do the job much better. That said there are no actual rules how. Call this one correct but less helpful than it should be.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">509 \u2013 Prophecy/Hindsight is Mind 2/Time 2 or </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#385723\">Time 2. Time 2 is the only correct one here. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Mind 3/Time 2 would be the combination to read someone\u2019s mind in the past or future, which is a different effect.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">509 \u2013 Age or Reverse Age is given as Time 3+/Life 4 or Time 3+/Matter 2. Time shouldn\u2019t need the help unless it is only altering the age of part of the target. If it is, the amount will be based on the complexity of the target so Life 2/4 or Matter 2/4. Also, why is it Time 3+?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">509 \u2013 Rewind Time at Time 3. This is also +3 difficulty, which is a really clunky way of adding difficulty.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">509 \u2013 Time Triggers are Time 4</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">509 \u2013 Speeding and slowing time is Time 3. This is true, it is also the exact same effect as the effect on 508 to increase or reduce speed, just with a larger focus. I only bring this up because I think it is sometimes forgotten.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">509 \u2013 Time Travel is Time 5 and arbitrarily +3 difficulty. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c55a11\">Again, I don\u2019t like the wording. It\u2019s not wrong because we can easily say that Time Travel is an Impressive Feat, but the terminology makes it seem like an arbitrary tax rather than a well thought out position.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">511 \u2013 Reprise of the time trigger at Time 4. The effect it is paired with is badly calculated but Time 4 is correct.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c55a11\">515 \u2013 Time 4/Forces 3 to set triggers for energy fluctuations. A very useless description. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">If it means, transmute forces at a future time, this is correct. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">If it means trigger a spell based on energy fluctuations, I think it is too high. M20 is not clear on what spheres are needed for adding sensing to a spell, but it\u2019s not going to be Forces at transmutation levels just to detect energy fluctuations.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">516 \u2013 Time 2/Life 1 to detect past or future states of life. Assuming this means extending basic Life senses across time, it is correct.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">517 \u2013 Life 5 plus Entropy 4 or Time 3 to radically age or de-age. This is just bloated nonsense. The three spheres are all capable of this on their own. Time would only need help if the goal is to preserve something like memory. Also this isn\u2019t a substantial change of form or being, so it is an alteration not a transmutation. Even when Life is necessary it is 2, 3, or 4, not 5. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">517 \u2013 Time plus Matter alters the temporal state of matter. In most cases Time or Matter can do this alone.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">518 \u2013 Time 3/Matter 2 to move an object through Time. Matter is not necessary.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">522 - <span style=\"color:black\">Note that unlike its compatriot, Correspondence, Time does not need to be as high as any other spheres in the conjunctional effect. Why it gets a pass on this and Correspondence doesn\u2019t is anyone\u2019s guess. It should probably be the same for both spheres.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">522 \u2013 There is nothing in the main Time section saying that Time needs Pattern Spheres to move things through time. Indeed in the paragraph about conjunctional effects moving things through time isn\u2019t even mentioned. This isn\u2019t as direct as in Correspondence but it certainly seems like Time doesn\u2019t need help moving things through time.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">522 \u2013 Extending the duration of a spell until a condition is met is Time and Entropy 3. It doesn\u2019t matter what the condition is apparently.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">522 \u2013 UberParadox rules for Time Travel. I don\u2019t like it. I think it is a terrible way of handling the difficulty of Time Travel that mixes up magical Paradox with traditional sci-fi ideas of paradox. It is, however the rule given here.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">522 \u2013 Combined with other spheres, Time can detect the influence of Time on other spells or patterns. I really can\u2019t see why Time needs the help. Seeing the effects of the sphere is a basic part of perception effects. I suppose it would be difficult to see that a rock that is no longer present was sent forward in time, but Time can at least see that something was sent forward and Matter isn\u2019t going to make that easier.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">522 \u2013 The combinations of Pattern Spheres and Correspondence with Time 2 to view the past or future in other areas works.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c55a11\">522 \u2013 Combining Time 2 and Entropy 2 lets a mage glimpse multiple futures and pick the one most likely to occur. This is an interesting idea, but its not clear what this means. If it means the mage can tell which one is most likely, this isn\u2019t significantly different from Time 2 alone. If it means the mage can set which one is most likely to happen, that isn\u2019t that much different from Entropy 2 alone. We need more information on how this works.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c55a11\">523 \u2013 If thickening space is a justification for a Rank 2 Correspondence Ward, I have to read Thicken the Walls of Time as a justification for a low level Time Ward. This would be more relevant if it was easy to understand what a Time Ward would do. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">523 \u2013 Time 3/Pattern Sphere 2 to affect other Patterns. In context I interpret affect other patterns to mean apply time contraction, dilation, or rewind to other patterns and that these are locking spheres. That works.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">523 \u2013 Time 3/Correspondence 3 to cast effects across distance and time. Minor quibble here: While a mage would need to have Correspondence 3 to do this, they are actually using Correspondence 2 here.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">523 \u2013 Time 3/Life 3/Mind 1 to move back in time while recalling events from the future. The paragraph before this says that rewinding time already pulls the mage outside of the normal flow of time so in this specific case adding extra spheres is unnecessary. Also, if it was necessary it would be Life 3 or Mind 1.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">523 \u2013 Time plus Correspondence/Forces/Life/Matter/Spirit to capture things in bubbles of Time. Time hasn\u2019t needed help from other spheres before now and there\u2019s no reason to start here. Also the specific example of Time/Forces/Entropy to capture a tornado is particularly ridiculous.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">523 \u2013 5 yard penalty for referencing HDYDT.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">529 \u2013 Spells with Time based triggers do not count towards a mage\u2019s max # of effects.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">543 \u2013 Time only inflicts damage when paired with Life (for creatures) or Matter (for objects. This is correct, </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">but the book says that the damage comes from advanced decrepitude and there are multiple ways these combos could cause damage, especially for Life. Indeed, on the next page it describes Life/Time effects as doing aggravated damage, which doesn\u2019t line up will with decrepitude.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">562 \u2013 Corr 4/Time 3/Forces 2/Matter 2 to make a car go really fast. Really, Time can do this alone. Forces and Matter are just to compensate for the speed and that wouldn\u2019t be necessary because the car isn\u2019t really going faster, it\u2019s just operating at a different rate of time. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">Since this is a player generated effect and players can use more spheres than necessary if they want I\u2019m not going to complain about the addition of Forces or Matter.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">603 \u2013 Golden Gunman, Time 3/Forces 2. Time lets the operative take multiple actions without penalty while Forces eliminates and difficulty penalties from movement or recoil.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">607 \u2013 Bullet Catch. Same combination and same problems as on page 429.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">608 \u2013 Penny Dreadful\u2019s Shiny New Penny at Matter 2 or 3/</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Prime 2/</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">Time 2. There is nothing wrong with this use of Time. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Only Prime is sketchy here.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">610 \u2013 Witch\u2019s Vengeance is essentially a waste of wordcount as it isn\u2019t a rote so much as an open ended idea of cursing. Time 3/Life 3 is listed as ageing the target, which either one can do alone.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">I haven\u2019t usually gone into the Appendices, however:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">663 \u2013 An artifact that uses Life 5/Mind 5/Prime 5/Spirit 5/Time 4 to completely rebuild someone from their \u201csave point.\u201d Assuming Time is used as a trigger for when the person dies, its use is fine. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">The only real problem is that Prime is ridiculously overinflated. This is a Prime 2 effect.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T07:42:22-07:00","id":1538837,"title":"","content":"Note, at least one entry in Time is marked red because I forgot to change it. I can't edit yet, but I'll point out the one I see now: 529 - Time based triggers do not count for max # of effects. That should be purple as it is a time rule stated outside of the Time writeup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T08:58:28-07:00","id":1538841,"title":"","content":"Awseome<br /> Just a few notes:<br /> - <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">422</span></span></span> - this could be explained by divination for the perfect moment<br /> - <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">429</span></span></span>\u200b - speeding up yourself with time is a valid requirement in this one, arguably time 1 would also work to know exactly when to stop the bullet with forces<br /> - <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">562</span></span></span>\u200b - It could be a combined effect of the car moving faster with time and disturbing space so he has to travel less to the destiny, forcess speeds up the engine, matter to lock the effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T09:16:26-07:00","id":1538842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538841#post1538841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awseome<br /> Just a few notes:<br /> - <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">422</span></span></span> - this could be explained by divination for the perfect moment</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it could, though if so &quot;spotting the perfect opening&quot; is not a great description. It gives the impression, to me at least, that the mage is spotting the moment without spotting why it is the perfect moment. I'd probably also require Mind 1 for multitasking if the mage is trying to divine the future at the same time as pay attention to the fight.<br /> <br /> I'd say if Time has the ability to see perfect moments its probably Time 1 not Time 2.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538841#post1538841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">429</span></span></span> - speeding up yourself with time is a valid requirement in this one, arguably time 1 would also work to know exactly when to stop the bullet with forces</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no complaints about Time 3 in the effect, my complaint is that once that is done Forces or Life alone can accomplish the catch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538841#post1538841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">562</span></span></span> - It could be a combined effect of the car moving faster with time and disturbing space so he has to travel less to the destiny, forcess speeds up the engine, matter to lock the effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, and quite plausible as a player effect. However, the book itself states why Forces and Matter are there, and the explanation does not make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 07-18-2024, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T11:13:31-07:00","id":1538847,"title":"","content":"The fact that Time travel is more difficult that teleportation actually tells us something about the nature of the tellurian, in particular that the arrow of time is a far more fundamental part of how things function, while the relative distance of locations is actually far less fundamental.<br /> <br /> it implies that space is far more mutable while time is more resistant.<br /> <br /> This is further supported by how much more paradox probe Time effects tend to be.<br /> <br /> i see this less as an inconsistency and more as difference between how Time work in the tellurian differently from what space is.<br /> <br /> it is of course poignant to remember that correspondence isn\u2019t the space sphere, but the connections sphere. And that piercing space is a means to strengthening your connection to a location elsewhere than where you are.<br /> <br /> less \u2018traveling\u2019, more \u2018altering relationships\u2019","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 07-18-2024, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T13:49:48-07:00","id":1538858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538847#post1538847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that Time travel is more difficult that teleportation actually tells us something about the nature of the tellurian, in particular that the arrow of time is a far more fundamental part of how things function, while the relative distance of locations is actually far less fundamental.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am aware that you consider the sphere system to describe the underlying functioning of Mage and/or the WoD. I do not. It is first and foremost a rule system meant to allow for as many different types of mage as possible to use the same mechanics. It doesn\u2019t always succeed, I\u2019ll admit, but that\u2019s what it is.<br /> <br /> After going through the system I really can\u2019t accept that these rules point at an underlying reality. A few do, specifically the ones that deal with a WoD specific thing like the Umbra. Most, though, make far more sense as the product of intuition, game balance, attempted game balance, and active hostility for specific effects.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s not a criticism, though, except for of the active hostility. The rules don\u2019t need to be comprehensive or metaphysically coherent. They need to be understandable, consistent and useable. The very fact that I can go through and rate the entries for accuracy shows that they mostly are.<br /> <br /> That I\u2019ve marked so many of the entries as red indicates that they are not well explained, but that\u2019s another issue.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T13:52:02-07:00","id":1538859,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:black\">I want to break down the similarities and differences in Correspondence and Time in a little more depth.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:black\">First there are the situations where they are equivalent. These powers might have different names, but they are similar enough to consider the same thing at the same rank:</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:black\">Rank 1</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:black\">They each provide basic perceptions of their respective mediums (distances and directions vs an internal clock) and the ability to sense changes and manipulations of that medium (sense spacial anomalies and sense disturbances in the time stream).</span><br /> <br /> <b>Rank 2</b><br /> <br /> Each sphere allows a mage to extend his senses across the respective medium (extend senses across space/time) and both can thicken their mediums to resist others senses (these are even named, Thicken Space vs Thicken the Walls of Time)<br /> <br /> <b>Rank 3</b><br /> <br /> Time and Correspondence have almost nothing in common at this rank. Time can speed or slow time, which is equivalent to two different things, one of them is changing how fast things move through space and Correspondence can do that. There\u2019s also one ability Correspondence has that Time may reasonably have as well. More on that later.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank 4</b><br /> <br /> Both spheres have the ability to make pockets of their own mediums to trap things in (\u201cisolate [things] into their own tiny realms\u201d vs Time Bubble (named ability). Both can also stop movement within their mediums (ward vs Time Determinism/stopping time).<br /> <br /> <b>Rank 5</b><br /> <br /> No real similarities.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now here are the abilities that Correspondence gets and Time has to wait on.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank 2</b><br /> <br /> At this rank of Correspondence a mage can extend his reach and his spells through space. Time can allow sensory effects across time but can\u2019t really cast on anything in another time until rank 3.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank 3</b><br /> <br /> Correspondence gets the ability to teleport across distances at Rank 3, but Time can\u2019t move through time until Rank 5.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank 4</b><br /> <br /> Correspondence can open up gates between two spaces. Time is never stated to get this ability, though it can be safely assumed to be possible at Time 5. Likewise, Time never gets the stated ability to co-locate in time, but it can be assumed possible at Time 5.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And the ones Time gets that Correspondence has to wait on:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rank 3</b><br /> <br /> At Rank 3, Time can speed up or slow down time, this is also equivalent to stretching out or contracting space, and Correspondence can\u2019t do that until rank 5. Time can also reverse time, and reversing directions is also a Correspondence 5 thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Finally, here are the ones that one sphere has and the other may reasonably have if we can figure out what it would do:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:black\">Rank 1</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:black\">Correspondence can sense things within the vicinity. Time is not stated to see the outlines of things that just happened or are just about to happen, but it isn\u2019t unreasonable.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Rank 2</b><br /> <br /> Thicken space makes scrying and presumably reaching through space more difficult, but Thicken the Walls of Time makes all Time effects more difficult. Thicken Space probably has the same reach.<br /> <br /> Likewise, Thicken Space was intended to allow minor wards so Thicken the Walls of Time can probably do minor time wards, whatever those are.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank 3</b></span><br /> <br /> Edit: At Rank 3, Correspondence gets Co-Local Perceptions. Presumably, Co-Temporal Perceptions can also happen at Time 3. Given that both can see across their respective mediums at Rank 2, this would be reasonable.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Rank 4</b><br /> <br /> Correspondence can do Wards, Time probably can do the same but for time. Possibly that is what stopping time is.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank 5</b><br /> <br /> Correspondence can superimpose two locations on top of each other. Presumably time can do this with two times.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 07-19-2024, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T14:40:29-07:00","id":1538869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538859#post1538859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Rank 3</b><br /> <br /> Time and Correspondence have almost nothing in common at this rank. Time can speed or slow time, which is equivalent to two different things, one of them is changing how fast things move through space and Correspondence can do that. There\u2019s also one ability Correspondence has that Time may reasonably have as well. More on that later.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Something worth adding is Corr 3 is the level at which you can change the closeness of relations between objects or people. Changing where they appear on the correspondence chart in relationship to one another. Indeed that is the principle of how Pierce Space works, you are changing the strength of connection between yourself and another location (corr 4 allows you to do this between locations, while corr 5 allows to make them more than connected, they become the same location)<br /> <br /> this tampering of the relationship of connections between objects is not unlike how Time 3 is used to change the relationship of how time interacts with a subject relative to its surroundings. Fast or slow it matters not, the point is that their traversal through Time is a step (or several steps) removed from the \u2018usual\u2019 flow of time, of which most people are otherwise in lockstep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T11:43:00-07:00","id":1538909,"title":"","content":"I realize I left one thing off my last entry. If Correspondence can do Co-Local Perceptions at Rank 3, Time can probably do the equivalent at Rank 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T12:15:53-07:00","id":1538912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538909#post1538909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I realize I left one thing off my last entry. If Correspondence can do Co-Local Perceptions at Rank 3, Time can probably do the equivalent at Rank 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>You did also leave out the Chain rote","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T13:45:35-07:00","id":1538917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538912#post1538912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You did also leave out the Chain rote</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean Chain of Whispers? I thought I had it in the Correspondence list and I definitely have it in the Mind one that's coming up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T14:49:10-07:00","id":1538925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538917#post1538917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mean Chain of Whispers? I thought I had it in the Correspondence list and I definitely have it in the Mind one that's coming up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chain - A chain is a magical bond which links two objects or creatures to each other through sympathetic resonance. Such bonds often already exist, but a mage with Correspondence can strengthen them or create one where none was before. For each success with this Effect, a Mage may take an object or creature up (or down) a level on the Correspondence Range Chart.<br /> M2e Pg189","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T15:25:10-07:00","id":1538927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538925#post1538925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Chain - A chain is a magical bond which links two objects or creatures to each other through sympathetic resonance. Such bonds often already exist, but a mage with Correspondence can strengthen them or create one where none was before. For each success with this Effect, a Mage may take an object or creature up (or down) a level on the Correspondence Range Chart.<br /> M2e Pg189</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Oddly enough that one was left out of M20. That\u2019s the version I\u2019m going through for this thread<br /> <br /> I do agree that is a power Correspondence should have. In fact there is an effect in HDYDT called Tether, I think, which does something like that. I don\u2019t remember what rank of Correspondence it used<br /> <br /> The closest thing to it in Time is Time Anchor I think, but that one is pretty light on details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T17:34:27-07:00","id":1538932,"title":"","content":"Part of it is that Time really doesn't have a parallel to the Correspondence Range Chart; and for good reason, because the latter is a bit of a misnomer: what the Correspondence Range Chart actually measures is the strength of the connection or familiarity. By contrast, the Time Sphere operates in terms of \u201chow many years can I transcend?\u201d This makes it more akin to the Void Correspondence chart found in the <b>Void Engineers Convention Book</b>, p.83, where \u201cRanges\u201d phrased in terms of \u201cline of sight\u201d, \u201cvery familiar\u201d, \u201cfamiliar\u201d, \u201cvisited once\u201d, and \u201cdescribed location\u201d get replaced by Literal Distances (1 km, Earth's horizon, low Earth orbit, high Earth orbit, near translunar space, etc.). Conceptually, \u201chow far away is it?\u201d is very different from \u201chow intimately aware of it am I?\u201d, and Time operates on the former basis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-20T05:03:35-07:00","id":1538941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1538927#post1538927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah. Oddly enough that one was left out of M20. That\u2019s the version I\u2019m going through for this thread<br /> <br /> I do agree that is a power Correspondence should have. In fact there is an effect in HDYDT called Tether, I think, which does something like that. I don\u2019t remember what rank of Correspondence it used<br /> <br /> The closest thing to it in Time is Time Anchor I think, but that one is pretty light on details.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think its lack of inclusion was more of a lack of thoroughness than a deliberate desire to remove it. There are many examples of effects which are mentioned in the text but given no official writeup beyond the mention in M20, the most apparent being Forces 2 force fields and Matter 4 Alloy effects.<br /> <br /> this is part of the reason why I tend to look at what is consistent across editions to fill in omissions, and why my approach with M20 is to avoid considering omission as confirmation of intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-20T18:45:15-07:00","id":1538958,"title":"","content":"I agree, there\u2019s no indication it was meant to be removed.<br /> <br /> Checking the previous editions has been helpful. If I didn\u2019t know Correspondence based flight was an idea of previous incarnations I would have considered it a mistake when I saw it in the common magical effects chart. There\u2019s nothing about that in the correspondence write up.<br /> <br /> Thats also one of the few safe uses of HDYDT. It\u2019s terrible for ranks but it can be useful for figuring out what is intended to be possible.<br /> <br /> That being said, those sources are secondary. If M20 is clear about an issue it doesn\u2019t much matter what another edition or HDYDT says. Even if it\u2019s not, they are still, at best, optional sources. Not everyone with M20 has the luxury of accessing previous editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 07-21-2024, 07:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T08:34:45-07:00","id":1539022,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mind in M20</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">311 \u2013 Mind 3 to pull a sleeping target into a Demense. Mind 4 to pull one who is awake.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">408 \u2013 Mind does bashing damage and is soaked with willpower, not stamina.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">417 \u2013 If a mage has Mind 1 and an active sensory effect in Corr, Mind, or Time can ignore multiple opponents penalty.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">418 \u2013 For some reason, Mind attacks on umbral entities tend to affect the mage. This is contradicted later.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">422 \u2013 A dot in Mind or Correspondence and any perceptual effect lets a mage read an opponent from a distance. I really don\u2019t like these natural abilities inherent in knowing a sphere.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">422- The Mind 2 addition to Thunder Punch sends a mental impulse to surrender.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c45911\">424 \u2013 Mind reading cannot bypass the advantage of Drunken Style Martial arts on the grounds that the martial artist doesn\u2019t know what he\u2019s going to do next. This says more about the assumptions the author is making than Mind.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">438 \u2013 Mind is pretty much the only sphere that can\u2019t be used in the optional dodging the blast rule.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">442 \u2013 Mind can make psychotropics more or less effective. The way this is written it sounds like a mage can use Mind <i>on</i> a substance to make it affect the mind more. This doesn\u2019t work as the substance has no mind. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">However, if the intention is the mage can use Mind on the person who takes the substance, that does work. Also, if the mage locks a Mind effect on the substance so it affects whoever takes it, that also works though likely needs Time 4.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">442 \u2013 A mage can use Mind to counteract a mind altering toxin. This does work. It is also said to need Int+Pharm to make sure he knows what he\u2019s doing. This is teetering on the edge of reasonableness and I don\u2019t think I\u2019d make it a hard roll.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">476 \u2013 Astral Travel, via projecting consciousness takes Mind 4 for the self and Mind 5 for others. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">477 \u2013 Astral travelers do not bring objects with them without a Prime 2 ritual that requires 5 successes and a willpower point. This is incorrect, There's already a Prime effect, Consecration, that accomplishes something like this and it is Rank 1 and there\u2019s no reason to consider it a Mighty Feat.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">477 \u2013 The Astral Sojourn projects the astral form in a more robust body made of primal energy and ephemera. This is Mind 4 or 5/Spirit 3/Prime 2. Prime 2 is the correct level for Body of Light so this works. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">477 \u2013 It takes Mind 5 and a direct psychic attack aimed at disconnecting the target to break the silver cord.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">477 \u2013 Mind 2/Prime 2 to set up an Astral Beacon to attract a lost astral traveler back to their body. Mind should be capable of doing this alone.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">477 \u2013 Mind 4 for a drifting mage to possess a different body. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\"> But it takes Spirit 2 to see potential bodies across the gauntlet\u2026 which isn\u2019t really thematic to astral travel. Honestly this is a really big hole in astral travel as if a mage can cross into the High Umbra with Mind alone, they should be able to see into it or from it with Mind alone.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">480 \u2013 Entropy 5/Mind 5 for someone on the Agama Sojourn to move from the Underworld to the High Umbra. Without an explanation for why this suddenly requires both higher levels of Entropy than the Agama Sojourn and higher levels of Mind than just going to the High Umbra, this is wrong.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">484 \u2013 Mind works normally or at -1 difficulty in the Otherworlds.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">485 \u2013 Mind works normally but with a +2 difficulty in the Underworld.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">504 \u2013 Restatement that Mind attacks do bashing damage. I only just now realized that the Magical Damage chart doesn\u2019t mention that Mind attacks are soaked with Willpower.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">505 \u2013 Mental illusions are Mind 2+. Assuming the illusions are small enough, short enough, or purely impressions or emotions, they should be possible at 2.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">506 \u2013 Immersive illusions with \u201cholodeck\u201d levels of apparent reality are Forces 4+/</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Prime 4+</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\"> and can probably be done with Forces 2 at smaller levels. Importantly, Mind is not listed here. Remember this for later.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">505 \u2013 Adding Mind 3/Life 3 makes the damage from mental illusions aggravated.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">508 \u2013 Life 3/Mind 3 to harm fae. No reason is given for why this needs Mind 3 rather than 2 like it is for the other supernaturals.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">508 \u2013 Mind 2 to suggest sleep, Mind 4 to command it. Mind 4/Life 3 is given as a possible but unnecessary option.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">508 \u2013 Mental illusions that cause bashing damage are Mind 3 or Mind 3/Life 3 for agg damage. The latter should also be capable of lethal.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">508 - Immersive Illusions are now listed as Forces 4+/</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Mind 4/Prime 4+. Prime is still wrong. Mind is also wrong since it is clear Forces doesn\u2019t need the help. Of course this all depends on what Immersive Illusions means, but since it was already stated that this is supposed to be Holodeck like, Mind doesn\u2019t have a place here. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">508 \u2013 Mind 4/Spirit 4 to command spirits. Spirit 4 can do this alone. Mind is either capable of doing this on its own, completely incapable of doing this, or can do this but needs the help of Spirit, depending on how seriously we take the statement on page 418. Even if we take that last option, though, it is a joke to require Spirit to be so high that it could do the task on its own.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">509 \u2013 Astral Projection is Mind 4+ like before.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">509 \u2013 Astral Body of Light is Mind 4+/Spirit 3/Prime 2 like before.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">509 \u2013 Clairvoyance is Corr 2 or Mind 3/Corr 2. The former is correct for distant viewing, the latter is correct for distant mind reading. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">However, if the intention is that psychics need to add Mind 3 for distant viewing just because they are psychic (which M20 does quite a bit) that is wrong. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">509 \u2013 Conceal Aura is Mind 1. Since Auras tend to change appearance with emotion, it makes sense this would be possible at the same level as conceal thoughts. I\u2019m honestly not sure why Mind gets so many little perks at Rank 1 </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">509 \u2013 Conceal Avatar at Spirit 2/Mind 1. I brushed this off earlier as Avatar\u2019s being strange, but really, I don\u2019t have an explanation for why this needs Spirit 2. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">Mind 1 works, at least, as it matches the level of concealing thoughts.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">509 \u2013 Conceal Thoughts is Mind 1.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">509 \u2013 The third appearance of Mental Illusions at Mind 2+</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">509 -- Enter a dream is Mind 3. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">509 \u2013 Influence mood is Mind 2 which tracks.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">509 \u2013 Influence subconscious mind is Mind 3.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">509 \u2013 Mind control is Mind 4.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">509 \u2013 Prophecy/Hindsight is Time 2 </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">or Time 2/Mind 2. Psychics don\u2019t need to add Mind just because they are psychic. Even if I give this the benefit of the doubt and say that it is meant to read the mind of someone in the past or future, that takes Time 3.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">509 \u2013 Psychic Pain Blast is Mind 3 or Mind 3/Life 3 for agg damage.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">509 \u2013 Scramble thoughts is Mind 3 which is appropriate if we interpret that as an attack, though I imagine something very similar can be accomplished by sending a lot of mental impulses with Mind 2.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">509 \u2013 See Auras is Mind 1 or Spirit 1.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">509 \u2013 See Avatars is Mind 3/Prime 2/Spirit 1. Again, avatars may be strange, but there\u2019s no reason why it would take Mind 3 to see one or why seeing one requires Prime and hiding one does not. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">509 \u2013 See through another\u2019s eyes is Mind 3.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">509 \u2013 See through mental illusions is Mind 4\u2026 why? You can detect them at Mind 1 and shield your mind at Mind 2.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#990000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">509 \u2013 Share perceptions is Mind 2 + the intended perception effect combo. I initially considered this fine, but I'm less certain. 1) I don't see a good reason why those perception effects can't be cast on someone without Mind. 2) Sharing your actual perceptions should be Mind 3.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">509 \u2013 Shield Mind is Mind 1 or 2 for others.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">509 \u2013 Telepathy is Mind 3. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">509 \u2013 Translating Languages is Mind 3, or Mind 3/Forces 2 to translate it so others can understand it too. Mind 3 should be enough to make it so that others think they\u2019ve seen or heard it translated. The Forces variant, though is the one to manipulate the light or sound such that they actually do see or hear it in a different language. </span><span style=\"color:#d35400\">We do run into a conundrum here, though... where is the mage pulling the translation from? The collective unconscious? Or does someone nearby need to actually speak/read the language?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">509 \u2013 Notably Telekinesis is correctly stated as Forces 2+.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">511 \u2013 Mind 2 can influence someone\u2019s mood.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">511- Manipulating biochemistry to influence mood is Life 3/Mind 2. This is wrong, Life 3 can do this on its own.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">513 \u2013 Correspondence 4 needs the help of other spheres like Mind to isolate things or people in a pocket realm. This is incorrect, by default spells can be cast on areas so the pocket realm can just isolate anything it is cast on, it doesn\u2019t need tailoring. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">However, if the mage wants to cast the effect on an area but only isolate some things in that area into the pocket dimension, then additional spheres would be necessary. Isolating only those people with bad intent would be Mind.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">513 \u2013 Correspondence 4 needs the help of other spheres like Mind ward against certain things or people. This is fine. Without help, the ward would just block everything. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">The reference to HDYDT is as wrong as HDYDT's Ward rules.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">513 \u2013 It takes Mind 1 to be able to process the input from Co-Location.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">516 \u2013 Mind 3/Forces 3 to manifest thoughts into energies. It really isn\u2019t clear what this means, but if it means take the idea of a fireball and turn it into a fireball (without Prime) or take a dream or a memory and convert it into a fireball (again without Prime) or to turn a point of Willpower into a fireball (again, without Prime) it works.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">519 \u2013 Matter 5/Mind 3 to melt steel with a thought. Matter 3 is the rank for changing the state of matter, but more importantly, Mind isn\u2019t doing anything here.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">519 \u2013 Special Mind Rules. The difficulty for Mind effects against a single target is their Willpower, unless it is an extreme effect which has a difficulty of Willpower +3. Mind effects against multiple targets is calculated like normal.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">520 \u2013 One of the infamously badly written sentences. \u201cCombined with Correspondence, Forces, Matter, or Life he can employ telekinesis (doesn\u2019t need Mind), pyrokinetics (doesn\u2019t need Mind), and </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">psychophysical assault (possibly legit)</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">, influencing objects, elements, </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">or people </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">with the power of his mind (unhelpfully vague, </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">and only influencing people would use Mind </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">and then only sometimes).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">520 \u2013 Mind 5/Life 4 to swap someone else's mind. I\u2019m not set on if Mind 5 needs Life to swap minds, but if it does it would be a grafting effect and would require Life 5 for others (complex) and Life 3 for others (simple). Life 4 would only apply to the self, and the mage would still need the requisite level of Life for the other target. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">521 \u2013 Projecting thoughts across the gauntlet is said to be Mind 4 or 5/Spirit 2. The Spirit level is correct, but projecting thoughts is a Mind 3 effect.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">522 \u2013 Spirit 3/Mind 2 to read resonance, synergy, and spiritual energies. Spirit 3 should be able to do the last one on its own, and Mind might be able to as well. I\u2019m not convinced this is the combo for the other two.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">523 \u2013 Time 3/Life 3/Mind 1 to move back in time while recalling events. 1) Time 3 doesn\u2019t move anyone back in time, it rewinds time. 2) The previous paragraph already said Time 3 lets a mage pull themselves outside the flow of time during the rewind so there are no special requirements for memory. 3) Life 2 or Mind 1 alone could accomplish memory preservation.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">525 \u2013 Life and Mind and Data allow for the mage to manifest multiple versions of himself. This is the same effect as correspondence so presumably the same Life and Mind requirements for independent thought and motion. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Unfortunately this also includes Primal Force and that shouldn\u2019t be necessary.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">533 \u2013 Axis of Coincidence Sidebar \u2013 </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Correspondence 3 to find a taxi (too high), </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">Mind 2 to nudge the driver over and Entropy 2 to increase the odds of finding one.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">533 \u2013 Axis of Coincidence Sidebar \u2013 Matter 4/ </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Forces 3/ </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">Life 5/Mind 5/Prime 2 to create a taxi and driver (presumably a soulless one as Spirit isn\u2019t involved). </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Forces is unnecessary unless it is vital that the car already be running.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">543 \u2013 A new method of making Mind attacks is mentioned here: adding Prime 2 and a point of quintessence.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">557 \u2013 Mind 4/Prime 4 to soothe Quiet by driving out the paradox in the target\u2019s mind.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">559 \u2013 Mind 3 to dreamwalk into a Quiet mindscape, Mind 4/5 to astrally project into one.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">563 \u2013 Correspondence 2/Matter 2/Mind 2 to set up a ward around a location that blocks scrying, sends out a <i>go away</i> impulse, and warns the mage if anyone breaches the barrier. Correspondence 2 tracks with setting the ward, the impulse and making the warning long distance. Wards are not a stated power of Corr 2 but apparently that was part of what thickening space was supposed to mean. Mind also tracks with both uses in the spell. Matter has a use, but not a necessary one. It\u2019s clearly being used as a locking sphere. However, since the spell is explicitly on a location, it doesn\u2019t need to move with any object. That said, there are other benefits to locking, so this isn\u2019t completely superfluous.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">563 \u2013 Mind 2/Correspondence 2/Entropy 1 for an effect that gets opponents to reveal things they least want to reveal. Correspondence is for distance, Entropy to find the weak points, Mind 2 for an impulse to slip up. I\u2019m not convinced Entropy is vital, but as a player action it is reasonable, I think</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">601 \u2013 Little Black Card \u2013 Corr 2/Forces 2/Mind 2 \u2013 The mage still has to hack like normal, so Mind isn\u2019t translating code or altering his mental skills. It isn\u2019t doing anything as far as I can tell.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">601 \u2013 Hot-Shotting \u2013 The optional Mind 2 effect here adds a psychological intimidation threat. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">602 \u2013 Right Click \u2013 Mind 3/Data 3 for a readout of data pulled from the internet and nearby surface thoughts. Because this explicitly reads surface thoughts, it should only require Mind 2.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">603 \u2013 Hypernarrative \u2013 Mind 4. The Mind 4 effect influences the target to follow a the script or expectations of a popular meme or trope.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">604 \u2013 Secure the Scene \u2013 Mind 2 or 3/Forces 1/Matter 1. Mind is discouraging trespassers. Mind 2 suggests avoidance, Mind 3 drives them away</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">. I didn\u2019t catch this before but Mind 3 doesn\u2019t control people, so this effect is actually Mind 4. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c45911\">This would have been a great place to show how to use a ward too.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">606 \u2013 Social Conditioning \u2013 Initial Processing \u2013 Mind 3/Prime 2. Since this could be considered, broadly, as a willpower reducing attack, Mind 3 is the appropriate level. Prime 2 does not make sense here, there is no listed power of Prime 2 that is doing anything.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">606 \u2013 Reinforcing the Programming \u2013 Often uses Mind 4 instead of Mind 3. That\u2019s good as controlling a mind actually is Mind 4. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">The wording does not mention Prime, but implies it is still there since Mind 4 is only replacing the Mind 3 part. Prime is still nonsense.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">607 \u2013 Breaking Conditioning \u2013 Willpower or Mind 3 effect to break a level of conditioning. This is, strictly speaking, the wrong level. This is a control mind effect which is Mind 4. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">However, spells on the self are often one rank easier than usual, and this is true in Mind (projection is Mind 4 for the self and Mind 5 for others). This is not true as written, but it is quite plausible.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">608 \u2013 Chain of Whispers \u2013 Mind 3/Correspondence 2 \u2013 Send a message by rumor. Mind is a compulsion to share the information, Correspondence pulls it from person to person. I would have thought speaking the information, sharing it online, or in any other way sharing it is what moves it from person to person. This isn\u2019t an ability of Correspondence. Also, I think I missed this the last time, but compulsions are Mind 4 not Mind 3, though something close probably could be done at 3.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">608 \u2013 Psychic Interface \u2013 Mind 3 or 4/Data 2/Forces 2 to mentally interface with computers without a physical link. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">I think I\u2019ve said before that Correspondence could probably substitute for Data when Forces is involved though it would have to be Forces 3, and Data might not need Forces. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">The Mind ranks are at least correct, Mind 3 for a psychic interface and Mind 4 for self-projecting into the Digital Web.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">612 \u2013 Jodi\u2019s Riot Sidebar \u2013 Mind is used to seduce and Life and Mind effects are used to push people over the edge or tempt them.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">626 \u2013 Hacking a HIT Mark is Matter 3/Mind 3/Forces 2. I still don\u2019t know what Matter is doing here </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">but Mind and Forces are at least plausible.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">653 \u2013 Trushades use Mind 1 to see auras.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">654 \u2013 Bafflejackets use a Mind 2 effect to blur perceptions. That\u2019s reasonable for influence mind.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">655 \u2013 Falconi Elite Business Attire uses Mind 2 for Empathic Bonds.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">656 \u2013 VDAs use Mind 1 for multitasking.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">661 \u2013 DDGR Cards use Data/Forces/Mind Effects to pull up information form an ATM. If we presume that Mind can just translate information without needing a source for how, this is possible.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">662 \u2013 Madness Grenade \u2013 Entropy 5/Mind 4/Matter 3. Given all the effects, I think this is a reasonable spread, though some of the effects do seem to overlap quite a lot.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T08:47:50-07:00","id":1539024,"title":"","content":"For point 477, consecration doesn\u2019t work for astral projection because consecration makes items an extension of your Life pattern, but you aren\u2019t bringing your Life pattern with you when you astral project.<br /> <br /> if you want to change how you appear, it is the Body of Light rote you need for astral projection, and consecration has no impact on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 07-22-2024, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T08:49:38-07:00","id":1539025,"title":"","content":"662 - Madness Grenade<br /> Why having Mind thrown into it when Entropy 5 is perfectly capable of doing it by itself? Adding Mind here is an unnecessary addition.<br /> Also, what is the function of Matter 3 in this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T09:04:54-07:00","id":1539026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539024#post1539024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For point 477, consecration doesn\u2019t work for astral projection because consecration makes items an extension of your Life pattern, but you aren\u2019t bringing your Life pattern with you when you astral project.<br /> <br /> if you want to change how you appear, it is the Body of Light rote you need for astral projection, and consecration has no impact on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The description of the effect is that items don't follow the traveler unless they've been metaphysically bound. If that is the requirement, well Consecration does that. There also isn't anything in Prime 2 that metaphysically binds except for Consecration (and in Prime 2 it is only for living things).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539025#post1539025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">662 - Madness Grenade<br /> Why having Mind thrown into it when Entropy 5 is perfectly capable of doing it by itself? Adding Mind here is an unnecessary addition.<br /> Also, what is the function of Matter 3 in this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Entropy can probably do everything in this effect. Mind can probably do the insanity bit better than Entropy, but Matter can't do physical disruption better than Entropy 4.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T09:11:58-07:00","id":1539028,"title":"","content":"for 520, the way I imagining it working is telekenisis works differently than levitation. With Forces 2 you can cause something to levitate, but with Mind 3 Forces 3 you can transmute your own thoughts in to momentum, letting you telekinetically move things simply by thinking on them<br /> <br /> the difference is one requires you to target the object, while the other is a duration effect on yourself.<br /> <br /> the same for pyrokenisis.<br /> <br /> 523 Time 3 here is about creating a time loop similar to Run Lola Run, where you restart yourself from a while ago. The difference between this and the time warp reversal is time warp works on a specific area. Anyone outside of that area can observe the reversal, including yourself.<br /> <br /> What the time loop does instead is reverse time itself, and the interval here is measured not in turns, but in scenes.<br /> <br /> with Time 3 on its own you would only know something happened because of your awareness being able to sense that a time effect had happened (and perhaps know via Time 1 that time had just been reversed)<br /> <br /> but to bypass that, you could isolate your mind from the effect to retain the information of the first go around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T09:14:45-07:00","id":1539030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539026#post1539026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The description of the effect is that items don't follow the traveler unless they've been metaphysically bound. If that is the requirement, well Consecration does that. There also isn't anything in Prime 2 that metaphysically binds except for Consecration (and in Prime 2 it is only for living things).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Prime 1 binds it to your life pattern though, the idea with Prime 2 is to incorporate the objects in to your body of light such that they can have utility beyond being decorative.<br /> (and Prime 2 needs Life to consecrate living things as of M20)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T09:20:38-07:00","id":1539033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539028#post1539028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">for 520, the way I imagining it working is telekenisis works differently than levitation. With Forces 2 you can cause something to levitate, but with Mind 3 Forces 3 you can transmute your own thoughts in to momentum, letting you telekinetically move things simply by thinking on them<br /> <br /> the difference is one requires you to target the object, while the other is a duration effect on yourself.<br /> <br /> the same for pyrokenisis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have to disagree. There's nothing anywhere I know of that says that you need to target yourself for <i>any</i> Effect: if you are the subject of your own Effect, you don't need to do any targeting. <br /> <br /> As such, there's no need to factor Mind into it; Forces \u2022\u2022 by itself is sufficient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T09:23:10-07:00","id":1539034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539030#post1539030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Prime 1 binds it to your life pattern though, the idea with Prime 2 is to incorporate the objects in to your body of light such that they can have utility beyond being decorative.<br /> (and Prime 2 needs Life to consecrate living things as of M20)</div> </div> </div> </div>Prime 1 doesn't say \u201clife pattern\u201d; it says \u201cpersonal pattern\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T09:25:53-07:00","id":1539035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539033#post1539033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll have to disagree. There's nothing anywhere I know of that says that you need to target yourself for <i>any</i> Effect: if you are the subject of your own Effect, you don't need to do any targeting.<br /> <br /> As such, there's no need to factor Mind into it; Forces \u2022\u2022 by itself is sufficient.</div> </div> </div> </div>A nice idea is to lock the effect to your own mind so you can do this with your mind as a stable buff as long as the spell duration lasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T09:39:53-07:00","id":1539036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539033#post1539033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll have to disagree. There's nothing anywhere I know of that says that you need to target yourself for <i>any</i> Effect: if you are the subject of your own Effect, you don't need to do any targeting.<br /> <br /> As such, there's no need to factor Mind into it; Forces \u2022\u2022 by itself is sufficient.</div> </div> </div> </div>You misunderstand what I am proposing.<br /> <br /> i am suggesting that it is an ongoing transmutation effect that transmutes your thoughts in to movement. You basically turn on the \u201ctelekenisis\u201d ability.<br /> <br /> with just forces you have to roll for each object you wish to levitate, and possibly for each time you wish to change direction depending on how finicky your ST is<br /> <br /> but with what I propose, you basically become Carrie. For the duration of the effect, any object you see, you can move, you can cause them to dance, you can spiral them together, and you can keep this active as you go about your day without needing to reroll arete.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T09:58:11-07:00","id":1539037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539034#post1539034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prime 1 doesn't say \u201clife pattern\u201d; it says \u201cpersonal pattern\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, if you want to be word specific, it doesn\u2019t say \u2018personal pattern\u201d either. It says \u201cWhen infusing her Quintessence into an object, that mage may also consecrate the object with her personal energy\u201c<br /> <br /> it also says \u201cWhen she shapeshifts, steps sideways, or otherwise alters her Pattern\u2019s metaphysical nature, that consecrated object will then change with her.\u200b\u201c<br /> <br /> In mage there are only 4 patterns. Matter patterns, Forces patterns, Life patterns, and ephemera used to describe Spirit patterns. <br /> <br /> Your mage\u2019s pattern is initially their Life pattern unless altered. When you step sideways you transform your pattern in to ephemera. When you astral project, you leave your pattern behind. That is the difference between the two methods. As such consecration does not change what you can and can\u2019t take with you when engaging in astral projection","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T12:06:39-07:00","id":1539048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539036#post1539036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You misunderstand what I am proposing.<br /> <br /> i am suggesting that it is an ongoing transmutation effect that transmutes your thoughts in to movement. You basically turn on the \u201ctelekenisis\u201d ability.<br /> <br /> with just forces you have to roll for each object you wish to levitate, and possibly for each time you wish to change direction depending on how finicky your ST is<br /> <br /> but with what I propose, you basically become Carrie. For the duration of the effect, any object you see, you can move, you can cause them to dance, you can spiral them together, and you can keep this active as you go about your day without needing to reroll arete.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually not bad.<br /> <br /> With that, Mind 3 could actually be used to &quot;control&quot; any spells after their initial &quot;unleashing&quot; without needing to concentrate on them. This could be most useful for permanent effects (such as those used to protect your Sanctum) so that they just conform to your thoughts without the need to re-use Magik.<br /> <br /> You could use it for instance for Mind 3 Life 2 made permanent to have a garden at your chantry that conforms to your thoughts and emotions, with plants that grow or shrink and move according to your thoughts and/or emotions without needing to spend a single turn casting a spell.<br /> <br /> A long time ago I imagined an Arcane Library that could make great use of this. Said library has a Forces 2(3) effect that makes all of its books be constantly fluctuating around in apparently random patterns, but those &quot;random&quot; patterns are actually controlled by Entropy.<br /> <br /> The result is that, you just need to name the book you're looking for and it will float in front of you, thanks to Entropy 2.<br /> <br /> However, by adding Mind 3, you wouldn't need to name any book, you wouldn't even need to know the name of the book. You'd just need to enter inside, and the information you want would trigger the best possible source for it to float directly towards you, even if comes from a place you weren't expecting at first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T09:23:23-07:00","id":1539101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539028#post1539028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">for 520, the way I imagining it working is telekenisis works differently than levitation. With Forces 2 you can cause something to levitate, but with Mind 3 Forces 3 you can transmute your own thoughts in to momentum, letting you telekinetically move things simply by thinking on them<br /> <br /> the difference is one requires you to target the object, while the other is a duration effect on yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what you describe, it is at least reasonable to consider using Mind. After all, converting mental energy to forces was mentioned on 516 and I did color that one green (with the caveat that that was only while Prime was not involved).<br /> <br /> That said, even if it is a reasonable effect, I can't say it is a reasonable interpretation of the passage. The text on 520 doesn't say anything like that. It doesn't define a new meaning for telekinesis that only includes lasting, mentally controlled spells. It just says telekinesis, which is a much broader definition and one that most readers are already familiar with. The way the text is written it applies to anyone using a levitation spell with a psychic focus and that is wrong.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539028#post1539028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">523 Time 3 here is about creating a time loop similar to Run Lola Run, where you restart yourself from a while ago. The difference between this and the time warp reversal is time warp works on a specific area. Anyone outside of that area can observe the reversal, including yourself.<br /> <br /> with Time 3 on its own you would only know something happened because of your awareness being able to sense that a time effect had happened (and perhaps know via Time 1 that time had just been reversed)<br /> <br /> but to bypass that, you could isolate your mind from the effect to retain the information of the first go around.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good explanation, but there is a sticking point. Once it was established that the mage could put himself outside the flow of time during time manipulations for one effect, we have to treat that as an option for others. So I would restate it in this way:<br /> <br /> With Time 3 alone a mage can rewind time. He has the option of being part of the effect or stepping outside the flow of time, but it is an all or nothing thing. If he steps outside of time he doesn't get any benefits of the rewind (e.g. injuries stay, he remains where he is rather than going back to where he was, etc) but if he does, he goes back to where he was as he was. If he wants to keep his memories but still rewind the rest of himself, he will need Mind <i>or</i> Life.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T09:32:20-07:00","id":1539102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539030#post1539030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Prime 1 binds it to your life pattern though, the idea with Prime 2 is to incorporate the objects in to your body of light such that they can have utility beyond being decorative.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539037#post1539037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you astral project, you leave your pattern behind. That is the difference between the two methods. As such consecration does not change what you can and can\u2019t take with you when engaging in astral projection</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll say up front, that is a well thought out line of reasoning, but I can't accept it. Astral projection doesn't use a Body of Light, that's an Astral Sojourn thing. Your argument is a better one for why mages have no way of taking things with them on an Astral Projection than for Consecration not working. Indeed, if that was M20s position I'd be in complete agreement with you.<br /> <br /> Since M20 says that it is possible to take things on Astral Projections, though, we have to look into how that is intended to work and what it actually takes.<br /> <br /> I already said part of why I am giving this section the rating I am. When M20 states sphere rank requirements for an effect it is important to check what is happening against the stated abilities of the spheres themselves. Sometimes we have to try and intuit what the effect is, but here we are fortunate to have a direct explanation of the logic: &quot;<i>Certain objects can follow the astral form if they have been metaphysically bound to the mage by a ritual and a Prime 2 Effect.</i>&quot; The key to bringing things over is a Prime effect that metaphysically binds the object to the mage.<br /> <br /> <br /> So now I go over to the Prime section and check if Prime can do that, and I find that there is indeed such an effect. Consecration, at Prime 1: &quot;<i>When infusing her Quintessence into an object, that mage may also consecrate the object with her personal energy. When she shapeshifts, steps sideways, or otherwise alters her Pattern\u2019s metaphysical nature, that consecrated object will then change with her. In the process, it also picks up her personal Resonance\u2026 which, because it both identifies her and becomes essentially connected to her, is not always a good thing</i>&quot; The wording isn't precisely the same but it is very close. There's also nothing in Prime 2 that sounds anything like a metaphysical binding. <br /> <br /> At this point, it is fairly straightforward to me that Consecration accomplishes the intended effect and the Otherworld Travel section is wrong about the rank (and probably the # of successes too).<br /> <br /> But let me take this opportunity to show why I take this approach, because the Otherworlds Travel section makes a good example. It is not a very reliable section. As I've said elsewhere, it is quite inconsistent with sphere ranks, often tacking on extra with no explanation.<br /> <br /> More importantly, it really appears Consecration was completely forgotten when this section was written as there's a special method for bringing objects along for Astral Projection, another special method for bringing items on the Agama Sojourn, there's no method at all listed for the Astral Sojourn, and regular stepping sideways automatically brings most things along without any special method. That last one is especially notable because stepping sideways with objects is one of the main purposes of Consecration. We could perhaps argue that leaving Consecration out was intentional for the other three, but not for stepping sideways. Here it is clearly an error.<br /> <br /> That is why I take the approach I do in general and that is why I am saying that pg 477 is wrong in this specific case. Not only is it clear that Prime 1 can accomplish the stated effect, there are major issues with the entire section's approach to the spheres.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539030#post1539030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(and Prime 2 needs Life to consecrate living things as of M20)</div> </div> </div> </div>And I called that out on page 1 of this thread as being a flaw. Requiring Life to cast a spell on a living thing when you do not need Matter to cast it on an object is bad design and I will always consider it wrong unless there is a convincing and well stated reason otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 07-23-2024, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T14:06:44-07:00","id":1539162,"title":"","content":"That's pretty much it for the spheres in M20. I've definitely changed my mind on a few things over time, mostly when I've realized there's a reasonable interpretation that I didn't initially think of. <br /> <br /> I do have one other list I wrote though. I tried making lists for How Do You Do That? I got as far as Correspondence and had to stop. I'll release that list soon, but to give some perspective here, I went through and did quick counts of the M20 and HDYDT Correspondence lists to see how many were marked right, how many wrong, and how many things were wrong when an example was wrong.<br /> <br /> For M20, there were 43 Correspondence entries. 37% (16) were good. 37% (16) were flawed. 9% (4) were ambiguous. 16% (7) were a new rule. And the average number of errors per flawed entry was 1.125. The greatest number of errors per flawed entry was 2.<br /> <br /> For HDYDT there were 51 Correspondence examples. 35% (18) were good. 61% (31) were flawed. There were, surprisingly, no ambiguities so great that I couldn't tell if they were right or wrong. There were 4% (2) new rules. The average number of errors per flawed entry was <b>6.032</b>. The greatest number of flaws per entry was <b>17</b>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T14:32:02-07:00","id":1539165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539102#post1539102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I called that out on page 1 of this thread as being a flaw. Requiring Life to cast a spell on a living thing when you do not need Matter to cast it on an object is bad design and I will always consider it wrong unless there is a convincing and well stated reason otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Specially considering this has never been the case in any previous edition <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T14:37:24-07:00","id":1539166,"title":"","content":"Also, it doesn't make sense to need anything other than Consecration for either Agama or Astral Sojourn, because Consecration turns the consecrated object as basically a &quot;body part&quot; of the Mage. It even says as much on both 2ed and rev. A consecrated object is like one of your fingers for any sort of magikal considerations. That's why its resonance is the same, it is shared, and affecting a consecrated object is like using a body sample of the Mage for purposes of correspondence for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T07:22:15-07:00","id":1539207,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Right, here we go...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#c00000\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Correspondence from HDYDT</span></b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">22 \u2013 Corr 4/Life 4/Mind 2 to turn into multiple creatures. HDYDT uses different notation for the Correspondence rank restriction. While M20 will give the correct level of Correspondence used, HDYDT gives the rank a mage has to have to use it. M20 would call this Life 4/Corr 2/Mind 1 though a mage would still need Corr 4 to cast it. I\u2019m only going to count this difference as a mistake once. This also requires Mind 1, not 2.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">25 \u2013 Wow this one is hard to muddle through. Corr 5/Mind 5/Life 3 is given to control your own clones. I should specify that this effect presumes the clones were already created with Life5/Mind5/Prime 2, so this is not a co-location effect. Nevertheless the section also specifically references the Everywhere At Once section, which is a co-location effect. As best I can tell Corr 5/Mind 5/Life 3 is a mix of the two effects that manages to accomplish neither one, and sets the ranks too high besides. The Colocation version doesn\u2019t need pre-existing clones and should be Corr 4/Life 2/Mind 1 The controlling multiple clones version doesn\u2019t need Mind 5, it needs Mind 3 for a mental link, so Mind 3/Corr 3 (HDYDT terminology)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Also, for some strange reason, HDYDT keeps saying that cloning does not provide muscle memory even when Life 5 and Mind 5 are involved. I can\u2019t follow the reasoning.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">32 \u2013 Corr 4/Forces 4 to summon sunlight by opening a gateway to somewhere where there is sunlight. There is no need to use Forces if you can open the gateway. This is Corr 4.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">34 \u2013 Corr 1 to be able to see while invisible. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">This would work. It is also unnecessary. Invisibility is already a Forces 2 effect and Forces 2 can also amplify or duplicate light and sound, so it is easy enough to bend light or sound around yourself while letting a tiny amount through and amplifying it as it hits your eyes and ears. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">34 \u2013 Corr 2/Matter 2 to shoot at one place and have the bullet come out somewhere else. Correspondence is explicit that whole patterns DO NOT need additional spheres to be teleported. This is Correspondence 2 alone if the mage is changing where the gun fires from and Correspondence 3 if he is changing the bullet's location or direction in mid flight. The best explanation I have of how Correspondence 2 object manipulation works is that it is extending the mage\u2019s natural reach. He\u2019s literally picking up the object, he\u2019s just not limited to his arm length. Without other spheres he can\u2019t reach out and pick up a bullet in flight. This either needs bullet catching spheres or it is a full teleportation effect. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">39 \u2013 Making it rain on another continent is said to be Forces 5/Corr 5</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">. <span style=\"color:#c00000\">Controlling weather is Forces 4, not 5, so this is Forces 4/Correspondence 4.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">40 \u2013 Corr 3/Forces 3/Entropy 2 to make minor tweaks to the weather. There is so much wrong here.</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">First: Entropy doesn\u2019t need help in controlling probability</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Second: Forces doesn\u2019t need help controlling Forces</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Third: Controlling weather is Forces 4, and I thought this had more to do with complexity than scale.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Fourth: If Correspondence can bypass the area restrictions on Forces (and I like the idea), it can do so on Forces 2, so this would be (as HDYDT calculates Corr) Forces 2/Corr 2.</span></span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">41 \u2013 Really analyzing Realm creation is beyond what I want to do right now. Corr 5 to do a major feat not covered in the normal Corr rules is at least a reasonable line of thought. It\u2019s fine by M20 logic. I would, however, allow alternative spheres.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">45 \u2013 A rare moment where HDYDT says something consistent with M20. Pulling Quintessence from a distant periapt is Corr 2/Prime 2.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">54 \u2013 Corr 2 and Mind 2 to extend sensory magic to another person over a long distance. Technically true, but overengineered. It is Mind 2 to extend sensory magic to another person in the same room, but you don\u2019t even need that to extend it to someone by touch. Since Corr explicitly allows a mage to touch someone from a distance, it alone is enough. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Of course, extending it by touch doesn\u2019t really make sense, so I\u2019d rather it be Corr 2/Mind 2</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">54 \u2013 Mind 3/Corr 3 to extend that magic to an unwilling person. It is reasonable to say a Mind 3 attack is necessary to extend those perceptions in this case, touch or no. So, in HDYDT terminology this would take Mind 3/Corr 3 if the person is out of sensory range.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">55 \u2013 Corr 2 added to a [Sphere] 1 perception effect allows perception at a distance.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">62 \u2013 Battlefield sense. Correspondence 1 to see the big picture of the entire battlefield. I think this would be Corr 2, since Corr 1 doesn\u2019t extend the range of your perceptions.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">62 \u2013 Mind 3/Corr 1 allows the mage to see the area and command through a squad of allies. This should be Corr 2 for the sight at distance, and a mage needs to have Corr 3 to be able to use Mind 3 at a distance </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">62 \u2013 Correspondence is one of the spheres that can \u201cread an opponent\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">67 \u2013 Correspondence 1 or 2 to use Slipstream which adds +1 to the difficulty to hit the Mage per success. Correspondence 1 lets the mage dodge by micrometers. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">Correspondence 2 allows them to appear slightly elsewhere, which is a new ability for that rank. I can\u2019t think of a reason to use a higher rank to do the same effect, but if a player wants to then I suppose it works.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">68 \u2013 The Time Dilation section suggests that a Time Dilation effect can be \u201cattached\u201d to the target via Correspondence 2 or Life 3. Correspondence is not a locking sphere. If it were, it would let the mage lock the spell to a location and spells default to locations anyways. Given that M20 consistently uses 2 as the rank for locking, I think either the locking rules weren\u2019t written when this section was or the rules were forgotten.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">70 \u2013 A basic restatement of Correspondence teleportation capabilities at each rank. There\u2019s nothing wrong with it, and nothing new, although the author wants you to know how very, very vulgar layering space on top of itself. Seriously, you need to know it is vulgar.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">75 \u2013 Entropy 3/Correspondence 3 to clear a crowd via pattern manipulation. The Correspondence 3 allow Entropy 3 to be cast beyond sensory range. (HDYDT terminology). </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">76 \u2013 Correspondence + Mind to call a cab or </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Correspondence + Entropy to catch one at just the right time. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">Assuming the cabbie is out of range the former is correct. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">The latter one less so. Entropy doesn\u2019t need the help as it is adjusting the odds of a cab showing up, not calling a specific one.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">77 \u2013 Sometimes it seems like HDYDT can\u2019t decide whether Corr 1 or 2 is correct so it suggests both. Here it is suggesting using either one to scope out potential teleportation destinations. This was probably meant as a placeholder and the wrong one was meant to be edited out. It wasn\u2019t. Correspondence 1 can\u2019t do this. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">Correspondence 2 is the correct option. This </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">is, otherwise, a clever and useful effect. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">77 \u2013 Correspondence 3 to blink- that is to make several quick teleports. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">77 \u2013 Correspondence 3/Forces 2 to enhance the cover of smoke and darkness for a teleport, creating potentially coincidental short-range teleportation. HAP/HOP arguments aside, the spheres are the correct levels for what they are doing.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">78 \u2013 Tether is an extremely badly explained effect. It initially sounds like tethering is a necessary step for teleporting things to the mage. It is actually a way of binding an object or creature to a mage so that it always counts as within sight distance. That is a good effect. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">That said, this section falls into the classic scope mistake and assigns spheres based on the complexity of the target: Matter 2 for inanimate objects, Life 4 for complex organisms, etc. There is no indication that tethering involves any kind of pattern manipulation, so complexity shouldn\u2019t matter. This should either be a locked Correspondence effect (so Corr 2/Pattern 2) or it should be something that the sphere of connections can do on its own (so Corr 2). </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As a side note, this is quite a situational power. Having a piece of the thing you want to teleport also drops the range to 1 success. For instance, if you really want to be able to easily summon your cat, keeping a small amount of cat hair on you (which is almost impossible to avoid anyways) is a lot simpler than setting up a Life 4/Corr 4 spell.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">79 \u2013 Colocation requires 1 success per extra location plus successes based on the most distant/foreign location. This is about as low a requirement as this spell could reasonably cost, and is in accordance with M20s Correspondence charts</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">It also says that Life 3 is required to independently act in each location, which counters M20s Life 2 requirement, although in this case I think HDYDT is closer to the mark.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">79 \u2013 HDYDT practically quotes M20 verbatim for a bit regarding rank and successes. Spirit 4 additionally allows the gate to go to a realm (which works since Spirit 4 is the rank to bring other people into the Umbra), and Mind 5/Spirit 4 allows it to go to a personalized Astral Realm or Demense</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">. I don\u2019t see the purpose of Spirit 4 in that case.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">80 \u2013 Warp Gate seems to be another description of teleportation. The only reason it even has a special name is to include it in the Gates and Portals section. I\u2019d flag multiple parts of this section for editing, but as an effect it is correct.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">80 \u2013 Correspondence 5 to shrink internal dimensions. Bog standard use of Spatial Mutation. This is the last time HDYDT will get anything right about Correspondence 5.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">80 \u2013 The Bringing \u201cThere\u201d to \u201cHere\u201d struggles to handle Correspondence 5\u2019s spatial distortion effects and gives a base set of rules that do not take into account the size or subtlety of the effect. According to the list, almost all of these effects are Vulgar, inflict a minimum of 5 points of paradox (as opposed to the automatic 1 of a normal vulgar roll), are automatically Outlandish or Godlike (so 10 successes base), and also says permanency of these effects requires 10 successes (The default for gates rather than the 6+ of the chart). On the very next page HDYDT will start contradicting this.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">81 \u2013 Bridging Similar Locations is about using Correspondence 5 to create Spatial Mutations that connect two locations. Functionally that is an identical effect to making a gate, which is normally Correspondence 4, and the description of how a mage does this with Correspondence 5 would be a perfectly adequate description of how they might do it with Correspondence 4. Also, this costs 5 successes plus familiarity requirements, which is both higher than it should be based on the magical effects chart (duration + familiarity requirements) and lower than the previous list indicated (10 successes minimum)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">81 \u2013 Indefinite mutations gives both a vague description of the effect (both stretching a hallway for miles and compressing the distance between two locations are given) and a vague sense of how to calculate the required successes (mostly ST judgement, but compressing a 90 mile trip by an undefined amount is 6 successes while a trip halfway around the world would take 10 successes). No reason is given for why this effect gets more difficult with distance when the nearly identical Bridging Similar Locations does not. Many of the examples given don\u2019t seem to pass through the intervening distance so there\u2019s no reason that distance would even matter. Also, subtle and potentially coincidental examples of this spell are given, which is correct but contradicts the list on page 80. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">I\u2019ll add that an obvious use of this ability, hiding buildings and neighborhoods in existing terrain Harry Potter style, is not mentioned. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">81 \u2013 Manipulating local physics in gross and vulgar ways (Inception, MC Escher paintings etc) is not specific enough. Three possibilities are given. For the first and second (Corr 5/Matter 4 for physics defying landscapes and Corr 5/Forces 4/Matter 4/Prime 2 for landscapes with impossible elements) I can come up with examples that should be Correspondence alone or the other spheres alone. For the last (Corr 5/Life 5 for Gigeresque landscapes) most of what I can come up with is Life 5 alone. Of course there will be examples where are the spheres given are needed, but this section is thoroughly unhelpful for determining that.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2026deep breath\u2026</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2026happy thoughts\u2026</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2026sigh\u2026</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I need a new color. Red is simply not enough for this next one. I need a color for when the book is not only wrong it is egregiously and intentionally wrong with malice aforethought. I need a color for when HDYDT looks deep into the void and the void says \u201cquit staring at me, you are freaking me out\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">82 \u2013 The given systems for transposing locations are arbitrarily harsh and suspend many of the normal rules of Mage in order to make things harder:</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">10 successes per layer + 10 successes per quarter mile area beyond the first at base\u2026 for reasons</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Normal rules for duration are suspended. This effect costs an additional 1 success per 10 minute duration\u2026 for reasons</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Normal rules for modifiers are suspended. This effect cannot have its difficulty reduced by tools, quintessence, or anything else\u2026 for reasons</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Normal paradox rules are suspended. This spell\u2019s paradox isn\u2019t determined by the roll but by the duration. At least 5 points per 10 minutes of the effect\u2026 for reasons</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">And oddly enough, familiarity with the locations in question doesn\u2019t matter. There are no additional success requirements for unfamiliar locations. </span></span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Co-Location is supposed to be one of the signature abilities of Correspondence 5, but I haven\u2019t seen this much animosity towards an effect or this many invented penalties since M20s writeup of the Vampire Lawn Chair.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">82 \u2013 While Moving Mountains is not as actively hostile to the effect it describes, it has all the rest of HDYDT\u2019s flagrant disregard for helpfulness and sense. This is, for all intents and purposes, a grand scale teleportation spell (Corr 4) except instead of moving everything in a location, this spell just moves the location. It\u2019s essentially a roundabout way of using a higher sphere to do the same thing less effectively, because it has a higher difficulty, automatically incurs 5 paradox (why?) and costs extra if it needs to be permanent. If it\u2019s not permanent, instead of everything popping back into place at the end, it crumbles into dust. To prevent that costs at least 10 successes and 10 quintessence, which is absurd. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">It also has a cavalcade of improperly added spheres: Corr 5/Forces 5/Matter 5/Prime 4. Again, Correspondence doesn\u2019t need help unless it is transporting <i>part</i> of a pattern. A mountain or building might require Matter 3 or 4 to separate it from its foundations, but otherwise Correspondence is fine on its own. Prime is an even more baffling addition.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">This is a great marauder spell. I struggle to see why anyone else would bother.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At this point, I\u2019d say things have gotten as bad as they can get, but we haven\u2019t gotten into Warding. That\u2019s coming after this next one.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">90 \u2013 Correspondence 2 to pull a small living creature from somewhere else, Corr 4 for a bigger one. This time with no extraneous sphere charge. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">It is stated that Life 2 or Mind 2 can get them on your side, which is actually a rare case where HDYDT goes too low on the pattern spheres.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:black\">Now we are into the section I was dreading most for Correspondence\u2026 Warding. This section is badly organized and has almost endless ways of getting things wrong.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#7030a0\">95 \u2013 Correspondence apparently can start warding against objectives at Correspondence 2 and is an application of Thickening Space. Keep in mind that M20 described thickening space in terms of blocking scrying and nothing else. This is a dramatically new interpretation of the ability and one so tenuous that even this paragraph has to put \u201cthickens\u201d in quotation marks. There is, however, one example in M20 which refers to a Corr 2 ward, so I do think this was always the intention.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">95 \u2013 Despite this not being a ranged effect, HDYDT makes it very clear that warding still uses the standard rules relating Correspondence to other Spheres. I don\u2019t see the logic. Neither does HDYDT because it will forget it said this.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">95 \u2013 Wards can be locked onto things, but either they don\u2019t use the normal locking rules or the normal locking rules were forgotten. Instead of the usual [Pattern Sphere] 2, they now use Matter 2+, Forces 3+, or Life 4. There\u2019s an additional Prime 2 + 1 point of Quintessence requirement if the ward is meant to move around. Considering that moving the spell is one of the primary reasons to lock it, that\u2019s a hefty tax. It\u2019s also not an ability of Prime, nor is it a requirement of any other locking effect.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Time to imagine that soul destroying color that doesn\u2019t exist again.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">96 \u2013 Warding against Objectives, the Corr 2 version of Ward, now gets its writeup and it is a mess of harsh and inconsistent rulings. There is no rhyme or reason to how supporting spheres are chosen. Despite this somehow being an application of \u201cthickening space,\u201d many, but not all, of the permutations set the supporting spheres as if they, not Correspondence, are doing the heavy lifting. Some set them so high that they could accomplish the same effect without Correspondence. Some aren\u2019t even wards. I don\u2019t think any two spheres are calculated the same way.</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">To block Matter the mage has to have Matter 2 for bricks, 3 for somewhat complicated materials, and 4 for really complex things like computers. This doesn\u2019t correspond to the normal progression of Matter. </span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">To block Forces, the mage has to have Forces at the required level to <i>transmute</i> that force, that is Forces 3 for most forces, and 5 for the really potent stuff.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Life, though, can block entire classes of creatures at 3, regardless of type.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Forces 3 can make something airtight. Not Matter 2, which would actually make sense, Forces 3. </span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">A nuclear blast takes Matter 5 as well as Forces 5.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Life 4/Mind 4 is required to block types of people\u2026 for reasons. Mind 4 can do this on its own.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Mind 4 is required to block specific people\u2026 for reasons. Mind 4 can do this on its own.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Spirit 4 can ban against spirits. I think it can do this on its own.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Entropy blocks misfortune, which is an effect Entropy can do on its own.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Time 5 can set up a ward where time flows differently on either side. Like Entropy, I think Time can do this on its own and at lower levels.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Prime 4 <i>might</i> be able to ward against resonance. It\u2019s an optional rule.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">Mind is the only sphere listed that affects how the ward expresses itself with the option to send bad vibes at Mind 2 and Life 3/Mind 3 to give a (presumably non bashing) psychic shock. Since in this case the spheres in question are doing something specific, it makes sense. I should point out, though, that Secure the Scene from M20 lets Mind do these things on its own.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Of course after reading what this kind of Ward does with a Mind augment I now have the question of what it does by default. <b><i>That\u2019s not stated in this section</i></b>. The wording of Minor Ward makes me think this is supposed to be the same thing, (-1 success on any rolls that involve the objective per success in the casting roll) but Minor Ward has different Sphere requirements and this doesn\u2019t match with the success calculations of Warding against Objectives. The other possibility, suggested in the terminology of traveling wards, is that the substance is banned, which is super powerful and well beyond the ability of Correspondence 2</span></span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Also, the costs of this spell are insanely high.</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">This kind of ward costs a success per level of duration (warding comes with its own chart) plus a success per \u201cobjective\u201d. A permanent ward costs 10 successes plus a success per \u201cobjective.\u201d Extending the ward out from the surface of the area warded costs an additional 3 successes per yard. Note that M20 has an example of this that costs much fewer successes for permanency. </span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">A temporary ward also costs a point of quintessence per objective and may also cost an additional point as a base cost (it is stated differently at different points).</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">A permanent ward costs a base point of quintessence, plus a point per objective, <b><i>plus a point per sphere involved including Correspondence</i></b> I have no idea why this should be so expensive.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Locking the ward requires an extra point of quintessence.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">A triggered ward uses Time 4 to activate when conditions are met, and costs a base 1 quintessence + 1 per objective, and takes only 1 success.</span></span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">97 \u2013 Minor wards sound like they should be the same things, but they apparently use Prime 2, and just Life 2 to hinder living creatures or Spirit 2 to hinder spirits. For this, they subtract 1 success per success from the rolls of the barred thing. Prime isn\u2019t doing anything and this costs a quintessence point plus a point per objective. Whether this is meant to be an alternate cost to Warding against Objective or that section was just cut and paste with no editing, I just don\u2019t know.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">98 \u2013 Minor Area Ward. Essentially the same effect as Minor Ward, but with a Mind 2 effect saying Get Out or Stay In. No quintessence cost is given, though I suspect that\u2019s just because this is a variant of Minor Ward.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">99 \u2013 Major Ward continues the trend. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">It is based on Correspondence 4\u2019s Ward/Ban ability.</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\"> That\u2019s the extent of its reasonableness. Every Major ward costs the standard ward costs, plus a point of quintessence per sphere involved. Permanent wards cost two quintessence per sphere involved. I don\u2019t even see the need for a single point of quintessence for warding so this cost is wildly out of place.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">100 \u2013 The Ban variant of Major Ward costs Correspondence 4, scope spheres, and, for some reason Prime 2 or 4 to \u201cinvest energy into the ward.\u201d There is no reason this spell should require that. Ban/Ward is one of the signature abilities of Correspondence 4, it should not require another sphere as a base requirement. Scope defining spheres to tailor specific applications are fine, a baseline requirement is not.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Of course, the suggested scope spheres are also too high, once again being set like they are manipulating the substances in question rather than setting the terms of a Correspondence effect. Life 3 or 4 to ban living things is not only too high, but also the wrong combination for manipulating, Spirit 4 and Mind 4 are so high they can accomplish much of the effect on their own.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">This also costs a minimum of 5 successes even before covering scope or duration, which means HDYDT considers this to be at minimum a Mighty Feat. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">However, banning an individual also requires having something close to that target, like a true name or an important item. This is completely arbitrary. At most it should take more successes to accomplish the effect without that. Also, if a mage has something important to the target, they have a Correspondence connection to them and do not need another sphere like Life to define the target.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Seriously, this reads like a list of requirements for specific scenarios that were accidentally merged together into the requirements for all wards.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">100 \u2013 The Co-occupational ward uses Correspondence 5 to make the banned things pass through the protected things. No extra requirements are added beyond those of Ban, so despite this being hyper-inflated in terms of cost, it is probably still less costly than Co-location was.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">100 \u2013 The luck ward uses Entropy 2+ and lets a mage make an Arete roll when an event could result in \u201cgood or bad luck\u201d within an area. What this roll accomplishes is not stated in this section, and it is suggested that we should use the rules for Fate and Fortune 30 pages later. This can only happen one time for each quintessence spent on the ward. No reason is given for why this specific version of ward uses such different rules.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">101 \u2013 The psychic ward is an expansion of the Objective Ward option to use Mind to mentally attack people within the ward. </span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">Mind 2 for suggestions of unease. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">No need for Correspondence since there\u2019s no actual barrier to entry</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#548235\">Mind 3 for mental pain, which uses the casters Arete to make a \u201cvulgar magic attack.\u201d </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Since, by the wording, this does\u2019t stop the offender from entering the area Mind 3 can do this alone, no need for Correspondence. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c45911\">Also, the section then takes the time to spell out what the difficulty would be if it were vulgar, then says that because it \u201cremains invisible\u201d it actually uses the targets willpower as a difficulty. I have no idea why it wasted the wordcount.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">Mind 3 or sensory stunning, Mind 4 for mind control, etc. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">No need for Correspondence, though.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Mind 4 or Spirit 4 to just bar a person or set of people. Mind 4 can do this without Correspondence and Spirit 4 makes little sense.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">Mind 4 or Spirit 4 to bar people with a certain mood. Same as above.</span></span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">102 \u2013 Paradigm wards ban people who follow forbidden paradigms and makes their magic Vulgar With Witnesses. This requires Correspondence 5/Entropy/Life 4/Mind 4/Prime 4, it also costs 3 quintessence and 3 successes per paradigm barred. For once, I will not complain about a ward having a quintessence cost, as quintessence reinforces reality. That said, I don\u2019t know why it would be 3 points. There is also no reason to include Life and Entropy in this. There\u2019s also an optional variant where intruders have their beliefs challenged by a Conceptual Entropy assault, which is normally not something that can be done without complex interaction and rapport.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">103 \u2013 The Time Ward uses Correspondence 5/Time 5 to do something Time 3 or 4 can do on its own.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There\u2019s more wrong with wards, but I\u2019m getting so tangled up in it I have to stop.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">105 \u2013 Correspondence 5/Prime 5/Spirit 5 to craft an extradimensional ephemeral realm to act as a spirit prison. I need to look deeper into realm creation for this, but Correspondence 4 was enough to trap things in a pocket realm and spirit binding is Spirit 4, so it\u2019s hard to see why this has such a high requirement.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">109 \u2013 Time 1/Corr 1 to see the right place at the right time, or Corr 3 to be at that place. This is actually good.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">112 \u2013 Incorporating Corr 4 into an Anchor point allows a mage to return to it from a great distance. This is sort of a normally closed gateway, so I\u2019m okay with this.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">113 \u2013 When using Time Freeze a mage has to add Correspondence 4 to bind a location in stasis. Magic defaults to being on a location, so you don\u2019t need Correspondence to set that at all, let alone Correspondence 4.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">113 \u2013 On the other hand by incorporating Corr 4 a mage can create a metaphysical bubble outside space and time. I\u2019m not sure what having the bubble be outside both space and time accomplishes, but this is the correct combo for that.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">116 \u2013 Corr 2 to cast at a distance. Check.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">116 \u2013 Corr 3/Mind 3 to connect multiple people across distance. Corr needs to be 3 because of Mind 3 (by HDYDT terminology), so check.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#538135\">122 \u2013 Life 3/Corr 3 to shut down or overload nerves from a distance.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T08:54:11-07:00","id":1539213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539207#post1539207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#c00000\">95 \u2013 Wards can be locked onto things, but either they don\u2019t use the normal locking rules or the normal locking rules were forgotten. Instead of the usual [Pattern Sphere] 2, they now use Matter 2+, Forces 3+, or Life 4. There\u2019s an additional Prime 2 + 1 point of Quintessence requirement if the ward is meant to move around. Considering that moving the spell is one of the primary reasons to lock it, that\u2019s a hefty tax. It\u2019s also not an ability of Prime, nor is it a requirement of any other locking effect.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I think HDYDT actually snuck in its own rules for Locking Effects:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HDYDT, p.31</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <u>&quot;Locked&quot; Quirks of Physics</u><br /> <br /> A temporary field of bent physics, however, may be \u201clocked\u201d into a Pattern by using the appropriate Rank of that Pattern\u2019s Sphere. <b>Locking a Forces Effect onto a person, for instance, would also demand Life 4, while investing it into a jacket would also require Matter 2 or higher.</b> (Yes, living creatures are more complex than inanimate objects.) That way, the creature or object in question can carry the warped physics around to other locations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine. Broadly, it seems to require you to have whatever Pattern Sphere level would be necessary to make major alterations to the Pattern in question. I'm using &quot;major alterations&quot; a bit loosely because exactly what kinds of changes you can make at different levels vary somewhat between Pattern Spheres.<br /> <br /> And yeah, it blatantly contradicts the best example that M20 gives on the Common Magickal Effects chart, where turning a living being invisible is Forces 2/Life 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 07-25-2024, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T16:16:42-07:00","id":1539264,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> <br /> Point 25 it does specify that mind 5 is to transfer your entire mind over to the other clone/clones. <br /> <br /> point 34. If you want light to go around you, it goes around you. There is nothing written in any edition of mage that allows the selective push of light to your eyes and not anywhere else. So this feels more like a self made ruling clashing with what is written. Forces 2 is a blunt instrument. And generally speaking your effects can only do a few actions, get it to bend around you, or to amplify, or to diminish. These are all separate effects. In the same way you can't simultaneously damage one person and heal another with the same effect or create two gates with corr 4 to different locations with the same effect. This is why using alternate senses via first rank spheres is useful if you wish to no longer rely on light.<br /> <br /> Even allowing for this rather generous interpretation of what Forces 2 is capable of doing with a single spell, if you allow light to to hit your eyes, this means all but your eyes will be invisible. Which to the outside observe will be seen as a big black bar floating in the air where the light going to your eyes does not reflect. Anyone you see will see this black bar.<br /> <br /> The other point 34, regarding corr and matter. This is apportation, and it has always been the case across mage editions including 2e and revised that if you want to apportate a matter pattern, it is corr 2 matter 2. Correspondence on its own only affects the self typically until the 4th rank. Whether you agree with it or not, you have to admit it is being consistent with previous editions of mage. This is the nature of corr 2 apportation. If anything, the sections which imply that Correspondence alone can do these things is what is actually inconsistent with what is established. And I do believe that this is more an act of omission of the need for Matter or Life rather than confirmation that Matter or Life is unnecessary. Same with how HDYDT also says periapts need Prime 3 but neglects to mention Matter 5, which is spelt out as necessary both in BoS, and revised's FBDF. Omission is not confirmation.<br /> <br /> point 39. Forces 4 is unlikely to cause rain unless you already have the conditions for rain immanent and you need only rush it along. Forces 5 enables one to convert wind momentum in the cold energy, which causes rain to occur regardless of what is going on. So I think it is not unfair to use Forces 5 for illustrative purposes in this case.<br /> <br /> Point 40. This is again another transmutation effect, this is why Forces 3 is at minimum required. The idea is that you are transmuting the forces pattern within the weather, such as wind speed in to heat, cold in to stillness needed for cloud formation, etc. In theory you could try to do this with Forces 2, but it would be far more limited as you would have fewer things you could pull from. What Entropy 2 does is it allows you to specify a desired endpoint for what is a random outcome. This is always how adding Entropy to effects works as Entropy can specify where you want things more or less to end up, but not the specifics of how to get there, that's where other spheres come in. For example you could use Entropy 3 to specify a car crash happens, you could use Forces 3 to force a car to suddenly stop in the road. But using them together means you can force a car to stop in the middle of the road, and guarantee that because of this a car crash happens. It's the same idea with the weather stuff, you can fluff about the elements of climate with Forces, but with such a small grip on control there you are essentially hoping that this amounts to something tangible, what Entropy 2 does is it allows a bit of control over the random elements of climate to make it so the changes you introduce are more likely to chain reaction in to the kind of weather you are hoping to see.<br /> <br /> Point 62 Corr 1 allows you to see around objects and perspectives. Think of it like being able to see all planes at once. Within your 360 view you can see not just the person in front of you, but what they are hiding behind their back as well. You can see the painting on the wall and what is behind the frame, you can sense not just the table but what is under the table. This aspect is what I believe the effect is referring to.<br /> <br /> Point 68, Really it should be Life 4 to lock the effect to another person, all things being consistent. Though the idea of locking an effect via correspondence is interesting if we consider the Chain effect. Might be that you could get around the need for Life 4 to lock an effect by locking it into another pattern, and then using Chain to tie the connection to the target to the level of body sample. I imagine the main discouraging factor is that it requires a tonne more successes to pull off, which does make it less useful in a high stakes situation. <br /> <br /> Just as a general note:<br /> The way locking works is that you are transmuting the subject to incorporate the magic being cast. Matter 2 is to lock an effect to a simple homogenous matter pattern, Life 4 is for other humans. Life 3 would be for yourself, and Life 2 for simple life patterns such as plants and some insects.<br /> <br /> So any time you see Life 4 as necessary to lock something in to a human's life pattern, that is actually being consistent.<br /> <br /> Point 76 same point as before, Entropy 2 can be used to enhance the odds, though I might argue this is more of an Entropy 3 effect since this is a specific outcome rather than something based on random chance.<br /> <br /> <br /> Point 96 to make one thing clear, I don't like the correspondence warding rules presented here either. But I there is one point to state here. Matter progression has always been like this, Matter 2 allows transmutation of homogenous items, Matter 3 for things with a bit more complexity to them, and Matter 4 for mechanisms. It's like how Matter 2 can turn a stone in to a nugget of glass, Matter 3 can turn that stone in to a wooden box, and Matter 4 can turn that stone into a clock. <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't know whether or not it is worth going through the rest of your points, this is already a lot to look through, so I'll leave it there right now.Speak","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T16:28:07-07:00","id":1539267,"title":"","content":"This is probably not helpful, but I've always interpreted the Correspondence +/- life and matter to not be a contradiction so much as an alternate method. If you're using Correspondence with life or matter, you're just grabbing the object or life form, which is a fairly simple process. If you're only using Correspondence, then you're not grabbing the object/life form so much as transforming/moving the space around them. (Like the ship engines in Futurama.) The latter is possible, but it's more complicated and thus requires a higher sphere level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T18:57:19-07:00","id":1539283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539264#post1539264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know whether or not it is worth going through the rest of your points, this is already a lot to look through, so I'll leave it there right now.Speak</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, HDYDT is exhausting isn't it?<br /> <br /> A few general points before going into detail.<br /> <br /> First, this isn't a thread about Mage in general, it is a thread about M20. What previous editions did can be edifying but they do not override what M20 says directly. Things can change between editions. The M20 Correspondence section is very clear about whole patterns not needing Pattern Spheres and that is the rule I am using. Yes there are points in M20 and HDYDT that say differently, but M20 does that alot (see our previous discussion of Consecration). <br /> <br /> Second, I applaud your ability to come up with explanations for rules and combos, it's really quite impressive. Nevertheless, just because you can come up with an explanation doesn't mean it is the right explanation or that the rule you are explaining is right. For the entire thread I've been using Pattern Sphere 2 as the required level for locking and I've given my explanation of how I came to that conclusion. I also think it is the easiest and best way for both adjudication and utility.<br /> <br /> Giving a possible explanation doesn't change that. Yes, locking <i>could</i> be explained by altering the pattern the spell is locked to. If that had to be the rule that would be a good explanation for why. However, I can think of a few ways to justify Pattern Sphere 2 as the cost for locking and I'm betting you can to.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T20:50:53-07:00","id":1539293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539264#post1539264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a><br /> Point 25 it does specify that mind 5 is to transfer your entire mind over to the other clone/clones.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of a couple of entries that I'm not sure you caught what I was saying. As I specified, the clones were already made with Mind 5. They already have minds. That mind transfer already happened.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> point 34. ...And generally speaking your effects can only do a few actions, get it to bend around you, or to amplify, or to diminish. These are all separate effects. </div> </div> </div>I didn't say it had to be conjunctional, that wasn't the issue I was tackling. The Forces 2 amplification was listed as an alternative to a Correspondence 1 perception effect. It's as conjunctional as that one is. <br /> <br /> For what it is worth I would let a mage cast a Forces 2/Corr 1 invisibility spell, the effects are aligned well enough. Of course it's not likely to come up as I would only make invisibility blind a character if the player actually wanted that. This is one of HDYDTs many invented restrictions. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> point 39. Forces 4 is unlikely to cause rain unless you already have the conditions for rain immanent and you need only rush it along. </div> </div> </div>Forces 4 is explicitly the sphere for Weather Witching, which is the section we are in.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Point 62 Corr 1 allows you to see around objects and perspectives. ... </div> </div> </div>Indeed, but only within your immediate vicinity. To extend senses beyond that you need Correspondence 2.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Point 76 same point as before, Entropy 2 can be used to enhance the odds... </div> </div> </div>Yes, I agree, Entropy enhances the odds. The unnecessary sphere is Correspondence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Point 96 ... Matter progression has always been like this, Matter 2 allows transmutation of homogenous items, Matter 3 for things with a bit more complexity to them, and Matter 4 for mechanisms. </div> </div> </div>No, there is no semi-complex clause for Matter 3. It's just Matter 2 and Matter 4.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T01:23:22-07:00","id":1539297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539283#post1539283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, HDYDT is exhausting isn't it?<br /> <br /> A few general points before going into detail.<br /> <br /> First, this isn't a thread about Mage in general, it is a thread about M20. What previous editions did can be edifying but they do not override what M20 says directly. Things can change between editions. The M20 Correspondence section is very clear about whole patterns not needing Pattern Spheres and that is the rule I am using. Yes there are points in M20 and HDYDT that say differently, but M20 does that alot (see our previous discussion of Consecration).<br /> <br /> Second, I applaud your ability to come up with explanations for rules and combos, it's really quite impressive. Nevertheless, just because you can come up with an explanation doesn't mean it is the right explanation or that the rule you are explaining is right. For the entire thread I've been using Pattern Sphere 2 as the required level for locking and I've given my explanation of how I came to that conclusion. I also think it is the easiest and best way for both adjudication and utility.<br /> <br /> Giving a possible explanation doesn't change that. Yes, locking <i>could</i> be explained by altering the pattern the spell is locked to. If that had to be the rule that would be a good explanation for why. However, I can think of a few ways to justify Pattern Sphere 2 as the cost for locking and I'm betting you can to.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me this reads like you have personally decided how it works and no one, not even the books, are going to tell you otherwise.<br /> <br /> this then becomes less a list of inconsistencies and more a list of personal disagreements. The way you dismissed pretty much anything I offered you as defacto not right unless you already agreed with it says as much.<br /> <br /> so I question the point of this exercise, why publicise this if you are going to dismiss opposing opinions as wrong out of hand?<br /> If you have decided your understanding is the right understanding, then what point is there even suggesting where we disagree?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T07:27:32-07:00","id":1539312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539297#post1539297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To me this reads like you have personally decided how it works and no one, not even the books, are going to tell you otherwise.<br /> <br /> <br /> this then becomes less a list of inconsistencies and more a list of personal disagreements. The way you dismissed pretty much anything I offered you as defacto not right unless you already agreed with it says as much.<br /> <br /> so I question the point of this exercise, why publicise this if you are going to dismiss opposing opinions as wrong out of hand?<br /> If you have decided your understanding is the right understanding, then what point is there even suggesting where we disagree?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's disingenuous. I've discussed both Correspondence teleportation and locking spheres before in this thread. In fact the very first discussion here, on page 1, was on Correspondence teleportation and supporting spheres and how they've changed between editions. The first detailed discussion of correct locking spheres was on page 3, over a year ago.<br /> <br /> Not only that, but I've discussed Correspondence teleportation spheres with you specifically. We practically took over the <b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions\">[M20] Correspondence Questions</a> </b>thread for a page or two on that exact issue. <br /> <br /> The issue is not that I am dismissing your arguments out of hand, the issue is I wanted you to bring something new to the table. I've heard these from you before and they weren't convincing the first time.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T07:55:16-07:00","id":1539313,"title":"","content":"It's too soon to edit the last post, but there should have been another line:<br /> <br /> Or to put it more nicely, I'm more than willing to keep discussing this with you, just remember three things: 1) Previous editions don't have veto power over M20, 2) just because you can come up with an explanation doesn't mean its only one or the best one, and 3) just because you put forth an argument doesn't mean everyone will agree with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T08:10:49-07:00","id":1539315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539312#post1539312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's disingenuous. I've discussed both Correspondence teleportation and locking spheres before in this thread. In fact the very first discussion here, on page 1, was on Correspondence teleportation and supporting spheres and how they've changed between editions. The first detailed discussion of correct locking spheres was on page 3, over a year ago.<br /> <br /> Not only that, but I've discussed Correspondence teleportation spheres with you specifically. We practically took over the <b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions\">[M20] Correspondence Questions</a> </b>thread for a page or two on that exact issue.<br /> <br /> The issue is not that I am dismissing your arguments out of hand, the issue is I wanted you to bring something new to the table. I've heard these from you before and they weren't convincing the first time.</div> </div> </div> </div>You did say that an explanation of what the rule may mean for how these spheres are being utilised, one which I assume you can agree with the logic of as you consider such explanations impressive, are not right nor are the rules right. I then have to ask what criteria are you measuring all this against?<br /> <br /> for my part I am using consistency across multiple sources and editions, as well as identifying areas which were changed between editions that are internally consistent. But you dismiss this approach choosing to look exclusively at M20 and from what I can tell deciding whether or not it makes sense to you or not.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t see how else you are making these decisions. What is the \u2018correct\u2019 answer based on except this vibe test? <br /> <br /> When it comes to locking in effects, the rule<br /> is clear that it is about transmutation ranks of that sphere being required. To transmute matter is Matter 2, to transmute another person is Life 4. This is specifically stated in HDYDT Pg 31<br /> <br /> M20 itself doesn\u2019t give the ranks but just says it needs to integrate the spell in to the pattern. And that is entirely consistent with the need for transmutation levels of the effect.<br /> <br /> there are no other references to locking an effect in the rest of the book. So I can only conclude that you came to the decision to downgrade it to Life 2 based on your own preferences.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T10:23:14-07:00","id":1539323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539315#post1539315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You did say that an explanation of what the rule may mean for how these spheres are being utilised, one which I assume you can agree with the logic of as you consider such explanations impressive, are not right nor are the rules right. I then have to ask what criteria are you measuring all this against?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sphere ranks should be consistent, it should be clear what the sphere is doing and why it is handled that way, and the rule itself needs to be understandable and usable as a game mechanic. We can't always get all of those things, but that's the ideal.<br /> <br /> I also favor using the lowest combination of spheres possible, so if there are two different ways of understanding an effect I'm going to go with the one with the simpler one.<br /> <br /> There's more to it than that, but that's the basic approach.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But you dismiss this approach choosing to look exclusively at M20 and from what I can tell deciding whether or not it makes sense to you or not. </div> </div> </div>I don't dismiss previous editions, I just give them much, much less weight than I give M20. That shouldn't be controversial in a thread specifically about M20. When M20 gives a specific ruling about Correspondence teleporting, 2nd edition doesn't get to veto that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When it comes to locking in effects, the rule<br /> is clear that it is about transmutation ranks of that sphere being required. To transmute matter is Matter 2, to transmute another person is Life 4. This is specifically stated in HDYDT Pg 31<br /> <br /> M20 itself doesn\u2019t give the ranks but just says it needs to integrate the spell in to the pattern. And that is entirely consistent with the need for transmutation levels of the effect.<br /> <br /> there are no other references to locking an effect in the rest of the book. So I can only conclude that you came to the decision to downgrade it to Life 2 based on your own preferences.<br /> </div> </div> </div>As I've described previously, Locking as [Pattern Sphere] 2 came from M20. M20, in one of its great failings, never gave specific rules for locking. That said, every time an effect can be reasonably interpreted as using a locking sphere, it uses rank 2 (except for one time that it uses rank 1). Notable examples include the Common Magical Effects chart entries for invisibility and flight. This is the strongest thing we have to go on in M20.<br /> <br /> Now I realize that HDYDT does things differently but it should come as no surprise that I do <i>not</i> consider HDYDT to be a good source. It's pretty close to the point where if HDYDT says something, its a strong indicator that thing is wrong. That's not a joke. I wish it was. In locking alone HDYDT sometimes uses alteration levels (e.g. Life 2 and 4), sometimes uses transmutation levels (e.g Life 3 and 5),sometimes uses a single level regardless of complexity (locked wards uses Life 4 for all living creatures), and sometimes makes something completely new up (in the section on flight it is Life 2 for self and Life 3 for everything else).<br /> <br /> So going back to how M20 handles it we have the distinct possibility that locking is a simple effect that is always supposed to use [Pattern Sphere] 2 and not scale with the target. As a rule it is simple to calculate and simple to adjudicate, which is good in a gaming system. The only real downside is that it goes outside of the stated abilities of the Pattern Spheres, but that's not all that unusual.<br /> <br /> Now we <i>can</i> view locking as changing the pattern, but we don't have to, and even if we do it is such a small change as to be really pushing the definition of alteration or transmutation. Doing so makes for a more complicated calculation, implies that it should be harder to lock a spell to a car than a rock (which I'm not convinced about). <br /> <br /> For all those reasons, as well as it having the lower reasonable sphere combination, I favor [Pattern] 2.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T14:27:29-07:00","id":1539340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539323#post1539323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> For all those reasons, as well as it having the lower reasonable sphere combination, I favor [Pattern] 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, but maybe it would make more sense for it to be 1 as it is basically detection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T18:49:38-07:00","id":1539352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539323#post1539323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sphere ranks should be consistent, it should be clear what the sphere is doing and why it is handled that way, and the rule itself needs to be understandable and usable as a game mechanic. We can't always get all of those things, but that's the ideal.</div> </div> </div> </div>i agree, and that is what my explanations aim to provide<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539323#post1539323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also favor using the lowest combination of spheres possible, so if there are two different ways of understanding an effect I'm going to go with the one with the simpler one.<br /> <br /> There's more to it than that, but that's the basic approach.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>to me, that is a flawed approach which is antithetical to knowing what each sphere is contributing. For example, if you see a rote that has Time 2 inexplicably capable of time travel, are you going to rule this going forwards?<br /> <br /> the better way to go about it is to understand how the two approaches differ and what the new rank would provide to enable the shift. It\u2019s a question of understanding how they can coexist rather than choosing one over the other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539323#post1539323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't dismiss previous editions, I just give them much, much less weight than I give M20. That shouldn't be controversial in a thread specifically about M20. When M20 gives a specific ruling about Correspondence teleporting, 2nd edition doesn't get to veto that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s about context. M20 is poorly communicated, the previous editions are much better communicated and also have far more examples to work with. The way I see it is if a rule is conserved between editions, then there must be a reason for its conservation, and I favour that as more lilely the intended version of said rule.<br /> <br /> similarly, the explanations provided in previous editions still fit for M20, which is less a new edition and more a collection of the previous material. One example of this is divided successes, which directly references Mage revised showing they intended to lift the rule straight from there, but they actually miscalculate how it is tabulated, leading to it be far more success heavy than it is supposed to be. For example, in revised, if you wanted to hit someone with a Life 3 attack, you get 3 successes, 1 will go towards hitting a non self target, and the other two go in to damage, giving you 4 points of damage.<br /> M20, instead says you need 2 points min to hit non self, and then you purchase damage, which means 3 successes only gives you 2 points of damage.<br /> <br /> revised already factored in the 2 sux minimum with the 1 split to target non self. And as such is a more succinct system<br /> <br /> so, you could either decide \u201cnah, M20 only\u201d and play using the miscalculated version which require more successes for no benefit, or you could learn of how the rule originally was intended to work back in revised, realise it is a miscalculation, and use the version of the rule as it was supposed to work.<br /> <br /> and that is essentially my approach, better understanding by reviewing the evolution of the idea and consider whether Brucatto simply misunderstood what he was writing about<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539323#post1539323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> As I've described previously, Locking as [Pattern Sphere] 2 came from M20. M20, in one of its great failings, never gave specific rules for locking. That said, every time an effect can be reasonably interpreted as using a locking sphere, it uses rank 2 (except for one time that it uses rank 1). Notable examples include the Common Magical Effects chart entries for invisibility and flight. This is the strongest thing we have to go on in M20.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>We have to consider that M20 is poorly communicated, and loaded with little typos. It is very possible, and actually more consistent, if it was simply the case that he meant to write<br /> <br /> invisibility on living being Forces 2 Life 2+<br /> <br /> the idea being you could lock invisibility on to lesser creatures such as insects. While Life 3 is for self and Life 4 for other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539323#post1539323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> Now I realize that HDYDT does things differently but it should come as no surprise that I do <i>not</i> consider HDYDT to be a good source. It's pretty close to the point where if HDYDT says something, its a strong indicator that thing is wrong. That's not a joke. I wish it was. In locking alone HDYDT sometimes uses alteration levels (e.g. Life 2 and 4), sometimes uses transmutation levels (e.g Life 3 and 5),sometimes uses a single level regardless of complexity (locked wards uses Life 4 for all living creatures), and sometimes makes something completely new up (in the section on flight it is Life 2 for self and Life 3 for everything else).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>this is such a \u2018baby out with the bathwater\u2019 stance to take. My approach is to try and understand the thinking that went behind the decisions made to see how it could be better communicated. Comparisons with previous editions is also useful to confirm if this ruling has always been the case or if it a new interpretation.<br /> <br /> but deciding it\u2019s all wrong out of hand is only going to put you in the wrong frame of mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539323#post1539323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> So going back to how M20 handles it we have the distinct possibility that locking is a simple effect that is always supposed to use [Pattern Sphere] 2 and not scale with the target. As a rule it is simple to calculate and simple to adjudicate, which is good in a gaming system. The only real downside is that it goes outside of the stated abilities of the Pattern Spheres, but that's not all that unusual.<br /> <br /> Now we <i>can</i> view locking as changing the pattern, but we don't have to, and even if we do it is such a small change as to be really pushing the definition of alteration or transmutation. Doing so makes for a more complicated calculation, implies that it should be harder to lock a spell to a car than a rock (which I'm not convinced about).<br /> <br /> For all those reasons, as well as it having the lower reasonable sphere combination, I favor [Pattern] 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn\u2019t feel like a good conclusion to come to, especially as it ignores the common rule of Life effects which is that it is easier to cast upon the self than upon others.<br /> <br /> that and it becomes arbitrary as to why pattern 2. When tied with transmutation, this makes a lot of sense, the effect is essentially be trans mutated in to the pattern itself.<br /> <br /> wheras with Life 2, it\u2019s like wait, so I can change their body to let light pass through them, but I can\u2019t change their skin colour? I can cause have their skin glow with a radiant light, but I can\u2019t have their hair grow longer? I can have their body burn with an eternal flame, but I can\u2019t heal them? Your ruling just doesn\u2019t fit consistency, while transmutation does.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T11:24:54-07:00","id":1539486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1539352#post1539352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> to me, that is a flawed approach which is antithetical to knowing what each sphere is contributing. For example, if you see a rote that has Time 2 inexplicably capable of time travel, are you going to rule this going forwards?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's clearly not what I meant. Indeed, if you go back through this thread I have called out examples before for using spheres that are too low.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It\u2019s about context. M20 is poorly communicated, the previous editions are much better communicated and also have far more examples to work with. The way I see it is if a rule is conserved between editions, then there must be a reason for its conservation, and I favour that as more lilely the intended version of said rule.<br /> ...<br /> and that is essentially my approach, better understanding by reviewing the evolution of the idea and consider whether Brucatto simply misunderstood what he was writing about </div> </div> </div>And that's fine in some circumstances, and I have brought up previous editions myself on some occasions (Correspondence based flight, to name one), but you have to remember that this will cut both ways. Sometimes overreliance on previous editions will get in the way of understanding M20. Indeed I suspect that some of M20s contradictions are because of elements lifted out of previous editions without checking to make sure they meshed well.<br /> <br /> In any case, that's not really relevant here. M20 gives a really clear statement on whole pattern teleportation. It's clear, easy to understand as a rule, easy to use as a rule, and we can tell exactly what each sphere is doing when it is involved. This is not a place it matters what previous editions said.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We have to consider that M20 is poorly communicated, and loaded with little typos. It is very possible, and actually more consistent, if it was simply the case that he meant to writeinvisibility on living being Forces 2 Life 2+ </div> </div> </div>I agree about M20 being loaded with typos. That's the point of this thread. However, I can't agree about higher locking spheres. The argument that locking is altering or transmuting a pattern really stretches the definition of altering and transmuting to the breaking point. We can't clearly tell what the change is. Now if those were the only things the pattern spheres were capable of, I would agree with you, but we have examples of pattern sphere uses that not only don't, but can't be altering patterns. Setting the conditions on wards, for instance. Sometimes effects don't need to alter, sometimes they only need to detect or touch.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, the game isn't going to break whether we use [Pattern] 2 or [Pattern] 2/3/4, but [Pattern] 2 is more consistent with the examples we see, slightly more consistent with what little we get in the locking section (spheres rather than ranks), and simpler as a game mechanic, while [Pattern] 2/3/4 is harder to justify what the spheres are doing and is more unwieldy.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to stop you from running the game how you want, of course, but I'm also not going to change previous references to locking in this thread. I have to go with the best I can pull out of M20.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> wheras with Life 2, it\u2019s like wait, so I can change their body to let light pass through them, but I can\u2019t change their skin colour? I can cause have their skin glow with a radiant light, but I can\u2019t have their hair grow longer? I can have their body burn with an eternal flame, but I can\u2019t heal them? Your ruling just doesn\u2019t fit consistency, while transmutation does. </div> </div> </div>I see the issue, but this seem to me to be more a problem with the difference between Life and Forces, not a problem with locking. A lot of that imbalance still exists even if the spell isn't locked, its just easier for the person to wander away from the area of effect.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-18T09:16:11-08:00","id":1548562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20#post1511445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Next up we have levitation/flight. Despite the sheer nonsense that is HDYDT's levitation section the Common Effects Chart is quite simple. Correspondence 3 (or Forces 2) to levitate things, Life or Matter as locking spheres. The only real problem here is that nowhere in the Correspondence writeup does it say that the Sphere is capable of this. The idea of Correspondence based flight has been in Mage for a decades, though, so I'm guessing this was an oversight.<br /> <br /> However, then the Sphere writeup says: &quot;Also, by combining Correspondence 3 with Forces, Life, or Matter, the mage can move things around from a distance, levitating, manipulating or teleporting them without physical contact.&quot; That's cool, but levitation at a distance, manipulation at a distance, and teleportation at a distance are several very different effects. The recommendation works for remote levitation and remote manipulation since the first is the same spell as above (with a range augment that's already covered) and the second is a Forces, Life, and/or Matter spell with a range augment. On the other hand remote teleportation and just physically picking up and moving objects from a distance are merely Correspondence 2 on its own, no other spheres required.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've recently been going back over the sphere writeups and trying to reinterpret them while throwing out as little as possible and I realized that the section I had problems in the second paragraph may be the statement that Correspondence based flight is possible. I previously assumed that it was saying manipulation with Forces, Life, or Matter with a Correspondence augment (which would be Corr 2), but my first move should have been to check if this was manipulation with Correspondence with a Forces, Life, or Matter augment. And indeed, all four examples (move things, levitate them, manipulate them, or teleport them) can be viewed that way if we read this entry to mean that Correspondence 3 can manipulate a target's position without physical touch. That is a reasonable power for Correspondence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-18T10:46:53-08:00","id":1548563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1548562#post1548562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've recently been going back over the sphere writeups and trying to reinterpret them while throwing out as little as possible and I realized that the section I had problems in the second paragraph may be the statement that Correspondence based flight is possible. I previously assumed that it was saying manipulation with Forces, Life, or Matter with a Correspondence augment (which would be Corr 2), but my first move should have been to check if this was manipulation with Correspondence with a Forces, Life, or Matter augment. And indeed, all four examples (move things, levitate them, manipulate them, or teleport them) can be viewed that way if we read this entry to mean that Correspondence 3 can manipulate a target's position without physical touch. That is a reasonable power for Correspondence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but it seems more like space distortion and thats more of a 4 thing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-18T11:28:35-08:00","id":1548564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1548563#post1548563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes but it seems more like space distortion and thats more of a 4 thing</div> </div> </div> </div>Not distortion so much. The mage isn't altering space at all really. Instead, I think the idea is instead that Correspondence 3 can control something's position in space. That's something it can already do by teleportation anyways, this just extends the principle to other manifestations of that control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-18T12:45:07-08:00","id":1548566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20?p=1548564#post1548564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not distortion so much. The mage isn't altering space at all really. Instead, I think the idea is instead that Correspondence 3 can control something's position in space. That's something it can already do by teleportation anyways, this just extends the principle to other manifestations of that control.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait i thought teleporting was creating a minor portal that binds 2 points in space, not just relocating willy nilly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-18T14:03:46-08:00","id":1548571,"title":"","content":"That's certainly one of the things Corr 3 can do. I believe it says something like the mage tears a hole in space and steps through. Teleportation, though, could include disappearing in one place and appearing in another. I doubt mages are limited to just one way either. The particular presentation sounds more like it comes from paradigm and practice than anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-19T05:10:12-08:00","id":1548582,"title":"","content":"Interesting, would you allow this kind of telekinesis to have any &quot;ramming power&quot;? Can you hit nyone with the previously stationary truck you are &quot;relocating?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-19T08:34:46-08:00","id":1548585,"title":"","content":"That's a good question. On a technical level I could see arguments either way. From a rules standpoint, though... well the Common Magical Effects chart acts like Forces based flight and Correspondence based flight/levitation are equivalent, and it is much easier to treat them like the same thing rather than make special exceptions. Ultimately, though, it would be an ST call.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would, just as I would allow the truck to be teleported just above a target. I'd probably stick with the size progression Correspondence uses, though, so moving the truck would be Corr 4. Throwing one person into another would be available at Corr 3, though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-19T21:20:46-08:00","id":1548605,"title":"","content":"In Calculus, we're taught that velocity is the rate of change of position, and that acceleration is the rate of change of velocity. That is, if changing position is under the purview of Correspondence, then influencing motion should be under its purview as well. <br /> <br /> I personally would allow Correspondence to use its TK-like aspects to hit someone and inflict damage; but then, I'm not a fan of there being a strict segregation of what different Spheres can do: just because Forces can be used to make something move around, that doesn't mean that Correspondence shouldn't be able to. Available Effects should overlap when the underlying concepts overlap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}